window.TRENDS = {"academic":{"updated":"2026-11-19","sourcesRead":["https://www.nature.com/subjects/synthetic-biology","https://www.nature.com/subjects/synthetic-biology/nature","https://www.nature.com/subjects/synthetic-biology/nbt","https://www.nature.com/subjects/synthetic-biology/nmeth","https://www.nature.com/subjects/synthetic-biology/natrevbioeng","https://www.nature.com/search?q=synthetic+biology&order=date","https://www.nature.com/search?q=protein+design&order=date","https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-026-10574-9","https://www.nature.com/articles/s41587-026-03373-0","https://www.nature.com/articles/s41587-026-03081-9","bioRxiv Synthetic Biology category feed via MCP, 2026-06-01 to 2026-11-19 (two windows, ~60 preprints inspected)","PubMed via MCP: 'optogenetic AND Bacillus subtilis' (all years; 12 records total)","Consensus via MCP: ML-guided DBTL / metabolic engineering titers","WebSearch: co-folding model landscape (Boltz-2, Chai-1/2, OpenFold3, Protenix, AlphaFold3 licensing)","WebSearch: Arc Institute STATE / Evo 2 / Virtual Cell Challenge 2026","WebSearch: self-driving labs, agentic biofoundries, Robin / Biomni / Co-Scientist","WebSearch: RFdiffusion2 / BindCraft / binder design success rates","WebSearch: cell-free and CRISPR point-of-care biosensors 2026","WebSearch: genome-scale metabolic models + ML strain design 2026","WebSearch: engineered nitrogen-fixing microbiomes and agricultural field trials 2026","WebSearch: SBOL / FAIR data / reproducibility in synthetic biology 2026","WebSearch: optogenetic bioreactor feedback control / cybergenetics 2026","WebSearch: nucleic acid synthesis screening governance (NSTM-6, IBBIS, IGSC)","WebSearch: Pinal natural-language protein design (Nature 2026)","WebSearch: generative genome design with DNA language models (Evo-designed phages)"],"sourcesBlocked":["https://www.nature.com/search?q=protein%20design&order=date&date_range=2026-2026 — returned an Akamai/JS 'Client Challenge' page (3 KB) rather than results; all date_range-filtered Nature search URLs failed this way after the first few curl requests","https://www.nature.com/search?q=synthetic%20biology&order=date&date_range=2026-2026 — same JS client challenge","https://www.nature.com/search?q=protein%20language%20model&order=date&date_range=2026-2026 — same JS client challenge","https://www.nature.com/subjects/synthetic-biology/research-and-reviews — HTTP 302 redirect loop, no body returned","Nature's plain search endpoints DO work via curl but IGNORE order=date and return relevance-ranked results, so the 2026 picture was reconstructed from the per-journal subject listings (which are chronological) rather than from search","Full text of paywalled Nature/Nature Biotechnology articles — abstracts were retrievable, bodies were not (no institutional access). Numbers quoted below come from abstracts, Research Briefings, News & Views or open-access papers only","One WebSearch query phrased around 'AI biosecurity / generative protein design misuse' was refused by the search back-end; the biosecurity trend below was therefore built from the published defensive/policy literature (Nature Communications screening papers, NSTM-6, IBBIS) instead","Nature Machine Intelligence, Nature Chemical Biology and Communications Biology dedicated synthetic-biology subject listings were not fetched individually, to stay under Nature's rate limit; their items were picked up via the subject feed and search pages"],"trends":[{"id":"cofolding-commodity","title":"Structure and complex prediction became free infrastructure, and open weights beat the flagship","title_zh":"結構與複合物預測成為免費的基礎設施，開放權重更勝旗艦模型","oneLine":"AlphaFold3's architecture was reproduced and surpassed in openness by Boltz-1/Boltz-2, Chai-1, Protenix and OpenFold3, so predicting a protein-ligand complex is now a commodity step, not a project.","oneLine_zh":"AlphaFold3 的架構已被 Boltz-1/Boltz-2、Chai-1、Protenix 與 OpenFold3 複現，並在開放程度上超越，預測蛋白質與配體的複合物如今只是一個標準化的步驟，而不是一個專案。","body":"AlphaFold2 made monomer structure free; the 2024-2026 wave made co-folding (protein plus ligand, nucleic acid, ion and modified residue) free as well. AlphaFold3's weights remain gated to non-commercial use through a restricted-access agreement and its outputs may not be used to train competing models, which directly provoked an open counter-movement: MIT's Boltz-1 and then Boltz-2 shipped under MIT licence with weights, Chai Discovery released Chai-1, ByteDance released Protenix, and the OpenFold consortium released OpenFold3. Boltz-2 is the practically important one for engineering because it folds binding-affinity prediction into the same model rather than requiring a separate docking or free-energy pipeline. The downstream effect visible in the 2026 Nature literature is that structure prediction has stopped being the contribution and become the substrate: Nature Communications papers such as RASSCCoL (rapid physics-based design of small-molecule-binding proteins, 19 Oct 2026) and DeltaCata (geometric deep learning for mutation-induced changes in enzyme kinetic parameters, 5 Nov 2026) assume accurate structures and compete on what is predicted next - chemical complementarity, kcat/KM shifts, hydrogel stress relaxation. The honest caveat, raised repeatedly in 2026 benchmarking write-ups, is that co-folding models interpolate the PDB rather than learn physics, so they are strong on natural-like complexes and weak on genuinely novel chemistry and on affinity ranking within a congeneric series. For a teaching institution the significance is cost: the entire structural step of a project now runs on one GPU in seconds to minutes.","body_zh":"AlphaFold2 讓單體結構預測變成免費；2024 至 2026 年這一波浪潮則讓共摺疊（蛋白質加上配體、核酸、離子與修飾殘基）也免費了。AlphaFold3 的權重仍透過限制性使用協議僅開放給非商業用途，其輸出也不得用於訓練競爭模型，這直接引發了一場開放陣營的反制運動：MIT 先後以 MIT 授權釋出附帶權重的 Boltz-1 與 Boltz-2，Chai Discovery 釋出 Chai-1，ByteDance 釋出 Protenix，OpenFold 聯盟則釋出 OpenFold3。對工程應用而言，Boltz-2 才是真正重要的那一個，因為它把結合親和力預測整併進同一個模型，不必再另外搭一條對接或自由能計算的流程。在 2026 年的 Nature 系列文獻中可以看到的下游效應是：結構預測已不再是論文的貢獻，而成了底層材料。Nature Communications 上的 RASSCCoL（以物理為基礎快速設計小分子結合蛋白，2026 年 10 月 19 日）與 DeltaCata（以幾何深度學習預測突變造成的酵素動力學參數變化，2026 年 11 月 5 日）等論文都直接假定結構是準確的，競爭的是下一層要預測什麼——化學互補性、kcat/KM 的位移、水凝膠的應力鬆弛。必須誠實指出的保留是（2026 年多份基準評測報告反覆提到）：共摺疊模型是在 PDB 之間做內插，而不是學會物理，因此面對接近天然的複合物時表現很好，面對真正新穎的化學、以及同系列化合物之間的親和力排序時則很弱。對教學型機構來說，意義在於成本：一個專案的整個結構環節現在只需一張 GPU、在數秒到數分鐘內就能跑完。","whyItMatters":"A research institution no longer needs a structural biology core, a crystallography budget or an HPC allocation to work at the frontier of protein engineering - it needs one GPU and a student who can read a PAE plot. That collapses the capital barrier between a well-funded university lab and a small institute, which is exactly the asymmetry GEMS can exploit. It also means the scarce skill has shifted from obtaining structures to judging which predicted structures to believe.","whyItMatters_zh":"研究機構要站上蛋白質工程的前沿，已不需要結構生物學核心設施、晶體學經費或高效能運算配額——只需要一張 GPU，和一位看得懂 PAE 圖的學生。這讓資源充裕的大學實驗室與小型研究機構之間的資本門檻瓦解，而這正是 GEMS 可以利用的不對稱。這也意味著稀缺的能力已經從「取得結構」轉移到「判斷哪些預測結構值得相信」。","gemsAction":"Stand up a single shared GPU box (or a modest cloud budget) running Boltz-2 and ColabFold behind a simple internal queue, and make 'fold it, then check the confidence metrics' a required step in every student project rather than an optional extra. Build one hard institutional skill that most undergraduate programmes lack: reading pLDDT/PAE/ipTM honestly, including a written rule for when a prediction is too low-confidence to act on. Within 12 months GEMS should be able to show a project where a Boltz-2 affinity prediction was experimentally checked, right or wrong - the negative result is as valuable a teaching artefact as the positive one.","gemsAction_zh":"架一台共用的 GPU 主機（或一筆不大的雲端預算），在一個簡單的內部排程後面跑 Boltz-2 與 ColabFold，並把「先摺疊，再檢查信賴度指標」訂為每個學生專案的必要步驟，而不是可選的加分項。培養一項多數大學部課程都缺乏的硬能力：誠實地解讀 pLDDT/PAE/ipTM，並明文訂出什麼情況下的預測信賴度太低、不足以作為行動依據。12 個月內，GEMS 應該要能展示一個把 Boltz-2 親和力預測拿去實驗驗證的專案，對或錯都好——陰性結果作為教學素材，價值不輸正面結果。","maturity":"mainstream","refs":[{"title":"Rapid assessment of chemical complementarity of ligands for protein design (RASSCCoL)","url":"https://www.nature.com/search?q=protein+design&order=date","venue":"Nature Communications","year":2026},{"title":"Effective enzyme engineering through modeling kinetic parameter changes upon mutations with geometric deep learning (DeltaCata)","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-026-79287-x","venue":"Nature Communications","year":2026},{"title":"Tracking Boltz-2 Benchmarks","url":"https://www.rowansci.com/blog/boltz2-benchmarks","venue":"Rowan Scientific (independent benchmark write-up)","year":2026},{"title":"Next-Generation Foundation Models: The Open Source Counter-Movement Led by Boltz and Chai, and the Post-AlphaFold 3 Drug Discovery Landscape","url":"https://note.com/pharma_insight/n/nfe3c598ff7c3?hl=en","venue":"Pharma Insight Lab (licensing survey)","year":2026},{"title":"Five protein-design questions that still challenge AI","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-024-03595-9","venue":"Nature","year":2024}]},{"id":"generative-design-crosses-into-function","title":"Generative protein design crossed from 'does it fold' to 'does it work', including design from plain English","title_zh":"生成式蛋白質設計從「摺得起來嗎」跨到「有沒有功能」，甚至能直接從白話英文設計","oneLine":"RFdiffusion2, LigandMPNN and BindCraft made de novo binders and enzymes routine enough to benchmark, and Pinal now designs functional proteins from a natural-language prompt.","oneLine_zh":"RFdiffusion2、LigandMPNN 與 BindCraft 讓從頭設計的結合蛋白與酵素普及到足以做基準評測，而 Pinal 已經能從自然語言提示設計出有功能的蛋白質。","body":"The 2026 state of the art is no longer backbone generation but functional success rate, and the field has started reporting it honestly. BindCraft (Nature 2025) reported per-target success rates spanning 10 to 100 percent with a mean of 46.3 percent, while independent commentary puts the realistic cross-target rate nearer 25 percent and notes that the most comprehensive single-target dataset - the Nipah G binder competition - came in under 10 percent. On the enzyme side, a March 2026 preprint benchmarked RFdiffusion2 (which depends on LigandMPNN for sequence design followed by RF3 refolding) at 30/41 on an enzyme design benchmark, with the challenger model reaching 41/41. The Baker lab's De novo design of miniproteins targeting GPCRs (Nature, 21 May 2026) is the clearest proof that this now reaches hard, membrane-embedded, therapeutically relevant targets: designed miniprotein agonists and antagonists against receptors implicated in itch, pain, cancer, metabolic disease and migraine, validated through a receptor-diversion microscopy screen. The genuinely new modality is language-conditioned design: Pinal, a 16-billion-parameter model from Fajie Yuan's group at Westlake University (Nature, 21 Oct 2026), was trained on roughly 1.7 billion synthetically annotated protein-text pairs and designs candidates from a written functional description; its validated outputs span GFP, a PET-degrading enzyme, an alcohol dehydrogenase and a glycine-cleavage H-protein, where the designed version raised final product concentration to 1.7x the natural E. coli protein. Preprint versions report Pinal recovering roughly 77 percent of requested functional keywords against about 12 percent for ESM3 on keyword-only design, though the figure shifts between versions and should be treated as indicative.","body_zh":"2026 年的技術前沿已不在主鏈生成，而在功能成功率，而且這個領域開始誠實地回報這個數字。BindCraft（Nature 2025）回報各標的的成功率介於 10% 到 100%，平均 46.3%，但獨立評論認為跨標的的實際成功率更接近 25%，並指出目前最完整的單一標的資料集——Nipah G 結合蛋白競賽——成功率低於 10%。在酵素方面，2026 年 3 月的一篇預印本在酵素設計基準上評測 RFdiffusion2（它需要 LigandMPNN 做序列設計，再用 RF3 重新摺疊驗證），得分 30/41，而挑戰者模型達到 41/41。Baker 實驗室的 De novo design of miniproteins targeting GPCRs（Nature，2026 年 5 月 21 日）最清楚地證明這套方法已經能處理困難的、嵌在膜上的、具治療意義的標的：他們設計出針對與搔癢、疼痛、癌症、代謝疾病與偏頭痛相關受體的迷你蛋白促效劑與拮抗劑，並以受體轉移的顯微鏡篩選加以驗證。真正新的模式是以語言為條件的設計：Pinal 是西湖大學 Fajie Yuan 團隊的 160 億參數模型（Nature，2026 年 10 月 21 日），以約 17 億組合成標註的蛋白質—文字配對訓練，能從一段文字功能描述產生候選設計；已驗證的產出包括 GFP、一個可分解 PET 的酵素、一個醇脫氫酶，以及一個甘胺酸裂解系統的 H-protein，其中設計版本把最終產物濃度提高到天然 E. coli 蛋白的 1.7 倍。預印本版本回報，在僅給關鍵詞的設計任務上，Pinal 能還原約 77% 所要求的功能關鍵詞，ESM3 約為 12%，不過這個數字在不同版本之間有變動，應視為參考性數值。","whyItMatters":"Design is becoming a text-and-screening problem rather than a structural-intuition problem, which is unusually accessible to early-career scientists - the bottleneck moves to assay design and honest hit calling, which is teachable. It also means an institution that cannot make 10,000 designs can still compete, because the discriminating skill is choosing the 20 to test and building a trustworthy assay for them.","whyItMatters_zh":"設計正在變成一個文字加篩選的問題，而不是結構直覺的問題，這對生涯初期的科學家格外友善——瓶頸轉移到檢測設計與誠實判讀命中，而這些都可以教。這也意味著做不出一萬個設計的機構仍然能競爭，因為真正拉開差距的能力是挑出要測的那 20 個，並為它們建立可信的檢測。","gemsAction":"Run one contained design-and-test campaign in the next 12 months with a deliberately cheap, unambiguous readout - a de novo binder or a light-responsive switch against a target GEMS already has an assay for - using BindCraft or ProteinMPNN/LigandMPNN for design and ordering 10 to 20 constructs rather than hundreds. Record and publish the success rate including the failures, because calibrated in-house hit rates are the single most useful number an institution can own and almost nobody reports them at this scale. Treat Pinal-style natural-language design as a literacy exercise for students, not yet as a production tool.","gemsAction_zh":"在未來 12 個月內，針對 GEMS 已經有檢測方法的標的，執行一次範圍明確的設計與測試行動，刻意選用便宜且判讀無歧義的讀出訊號——一個從頭設計的結合蛋白，或一個光反應開關——用 BindCraft 或 ProteinMPNN/LigandMPNN 做設計，只訂製 10 到 20 個構築體，而不是幾百個。把成功率連同失敗一起記錄並發表，因為經過校準的自家命中率是一個機構能擁有的最有用的數字，而在這個規模上幾乎沒有人回報。把 Pinal 這類自然語言設計當成學生的素養訓練，而非現階段的生產工具。","maturity":"accelerating","refs":[{"title":"De novo design of miniproteins targeting GPCRs","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-026-10656-8","venue":"Nature","year":2026},{"title":"Programmable design of functional proteins from natural language (Pinal)","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-026-11205-z","venue":"Nature","year":2026},{"title":"One-shot design of functional protein binders with BindCraft","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-025-09429-6","venue":"Nature","year":2025},{"title":"Scaling Atomistic Protein Binder Design with Generative Pretraining and Test-Time Compute (RFdiffusion2 enzyme benchmark comparison)","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2603.27950","venue":"arXiv preprint","year":2026},{"title":"Researchers Develop AI Model That Designs Proteins From Plain-Language Descriptions","url":"https://en.westlake.edu.cn/news_events/westlakenews/research/202610/t20261023_70614.html","venue":"Westlake University (institutional release)","year":2026}]},{"id":"virtual-cell-foundation-models","title":"Biological foundation models and the race to a virtual cell","title_zh":"生物基礎模型與通往虛擬細胞的競賽","oneLine":"Evo 2, Arc's STATE and a Nature Perspective on a virtual yeast have turned 'simulate the cell' from rhetoric into a funded, benchmarked programme with an open prize.","oneLine_zh":"Evo 2、Arc 的 STATE，以及 Nature 上一篇關於虛擬酵母的 Perspective，把「模擬整個細胞」從口號變成有經費、有基準、還有公開獎金的研究計畫。","body":"Three strands converged in 2026. First, DNA foundation models: Evo 2, published in Nature in March 2026, was trained on 9.3 trillion bases from more than 128,000 genomes across all domains of life, scaled to 40 billion parameters, handles context windows up to one million bases, and shipped with open weights. Second, perturbation models: Arc Institute's STATE, its first virtual cell model, was trained on observational data from roughly 170 million cells plus perturbational data from over 100 million cells across 70 human cell lines, split into a State Embedding model for the transcriptome and a State Transition model for predicting perturbation-induced shifts; it is released under a non-commercial licence with State 2 in development, and Arc added an in-context-learning successor in January 2026. Arc has made this a community sport through the 2026 Virtual Cell Challenge, which scores models on predicting gene-knockdown responses in six cell lines they never saw in training, with a 100,000 USD prize. Third, and most relevant to synthetic biology, the microbial virtual cell: Towards the construction of a virtual yeast (Nature Perspective, 1 July 2026, Qian, Zhou and Guo) proposes decomposing S. cerevisiae into eight function-centred modules - genetic, metabolic and structural - each as a domain-specific AI tool coordinated by an LLM orchestration layer over three data pillars (mechanistic knowledge, subcellular architecture, dynamic states), inside a closed loop that autonomously designs and runs experiments. Nature Methods separately highlighted a 4D whole-cell model of a minimal cell (14 April 2026), and bioRxiv work is already building virtual viruses inside a JCVI-syn3A-based spatial minimal cell. The honest status: none of these predicts a novel engineered phenotype reliably, and the Virtual Cell Challenge exists precisely because generalisation to unseen contexts is unsolved.","body_zh":"2026 年有三條線匯流。第一條是 DNA 基礎模型：2026 年 3 月發表於 Nature 的 Evo 2，以涵蓋三域生物、超過 128,000 個基因組的 9.3 兆個鹼基訓練，規模達 400 億參數，可處理長達一百萬個鹼基的上下文窗口，並附帶開放權重釋出。第二條是擾動模型：Arc Institute 的 STATE 是其第一個虛擬細胞模型，訓練資料包含約 1.7 億個細胞的觀察性資料，以及橫跨 70 條人類細胞株、超過 1 億個細胞的擾動資料，並拆成負責轉錄體的 State Embedding 模型與預測擾動造成位移的 State Transition 模型；它以非商業授權釋出，State 2 正在開發中，Arc 並於 2026 年 1 月加入了一個採用情境學習的後繼模型。Arc 透過 2026 年 Virtual Cell Challenge 把這件事變成社群競賽，以模型在訓練時從未見過的六條細胞株上預測基因敲低反應的表現評分，獎金 10 萬美元。第三條，也是與合成生物學最相關的，是微生物虛擬細胞：Towards the construction of a virtual yeast（Nature Perspective，2026 年 7 月 1 日，Qian、Zhou 與 Guo）主張把 S. cerevisiae 拆解成八個以功能為核心的模組——遺傳、代謝與結構——每個模組都是一個特定領域的 AI 工具，由一個 LLM 協調層統整，底下架在三根資料支柱上（機制知識、次細胞結構、動態狀態），整體置於一個能自主設計並執行實驗的閉環之中。Nature Methods 另外介紹了一個最小細胞的 4D 全細胞模型（2026 年 4 月 14 日），bioRxiv 上也已經有人在以 JCVI-syn3A 為基礎的空間最小細胞中建構虛擬病毒。誠實的現況是：這些模型都還不能可靠預測一個新設計出來的表現型，而 Virtual Cell Challenge 之所以存在，正是因為「推廣到未見過的情境」尚未解決。","whyItMatters":"If virtual cells work even partially, the expensive part of synthetic biology moves from the bench to the GPU, and institutions that have invested in modelling literacy will set the agenda while wet-lab-only institutions become service providers. Yeast and minimal cells are where this will be decided first, and they are cheap, safe and teachable - which is a rare alignment of frontier relevance and institutional feasibility.","whyItMatters_zh":"虛擬細胞只要部分可行，合成生物學最花錢的環節就會從實驗檯移到 GPU 上，投資於建模素養的機構會主導議題，只有濕式實驗室的機構則會淪為服務提供者。這件事會先在酵母與最小細胞上見真章，而這兩者便宜、安全、好教——前沿相關性與機構可行性難得地對上了。","gemsAction":"Enter a GEMS student team in the next Virtual Cell Challenge cycle: it is a free, externally scored, genuinely unsolved benchmark with a public leaderboard, which is the cheapest credible way for a young institution to demonstrate dry-lab capability. In parall, pick one microbial model system GEMS already runs wet (ideally Bacillus or yeast) and start assembling the three data pillars for it - curated mechanistic knowledge, growth and expression time-series, imaging - so that GEMS owns a dataset rather than only consuming models. Reach out to Arc Institute's tools community and to the virtual-yeast authors; both are actively recruiting benchmark contributors.","gemsAction_zh":"派一支 GEMS 學生隊伍參加下一輪 Virtual Cell Challenge：它免費、由外部評分、是真正未解的基準，而且有公開排行榜，對一所年輕機構而言，這是展現乾式實驗室能力最便宜又可信的方式。同時，挑一個 GEMS 已經在做濕式實驗的微生物模式系統（最好是 Bacillus 或酵母），開始為它組建那三根資料支柱——經過整理的機制知識、生長與表現量的時間序列、影像——讓 GEMS 擁有資料集，而不只是消費別人的模型。主動聯繫 Arc Institute 的工具社群，以及虛擬酵母論文的作者群；兩邊都在積極招募基準測試的貢獻者。","maturity":"emerging","refs":[{"title":"Towards the construction of a virtual yeast","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-026-10574-9","venue":"Nature (Perspective)","year":2026},{"title":"The 2026 Virtual Cell Challenge: predicting perturbation responses in cell contexts a model has never seen","url":"https://arcinstitute.org/news/virtual-cell-challenge-2026","venue":"Arc Institute","year":2026},{"title":"Arc Institute Releases its First Virtual Cell Model (STATE), trained on 270 million cells","url":"https://www.biopharmatrend.com/news/arc-institute-releases-its-first-virtual-cell-model-trained-on-270-million-cells-1302/","venue":"BiopharmaTrend","year":2025},{"title":"4D whole-cell model of a minimal cell","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41592-026-03075-0","venue":"Nature Methods (Research Highlight)","year":2026},{"title":"Arc Tools Hub (Evo 2, STATE model releases and weights)","url":"https://arcinstitute.org/tools","venue":"Arc Institute","year":2026}]},{"id":"generative-genome-design","title":"Genome-scale generative design: models now write whole genomes that boot","title_zh":"基因組尺度的生成式設計：模型現在寫出的整個基因組真的能啟動","oneLine":"Genome language models have gone from annotating DNA to authoring viable bacteriophage genomes, and Nature Reviews is already publishing how-to pieces on it.","oneLine_zh":"基因組語言模型已從標註 DNA 進展到撰寫能存活的噬菌體基因組，Nature Reviews 甚至已經在刊登操作指南型的文章。","body":"The landmark result is the Stanford and Arc Institute phage work: Evo 1 and Evo 2 were used to generate complete bacteriophage genomes modelled on the 5,386-nucleotide phiX174, roughly 700,000 candidate genomes were sampled, 285 were chemically synthesised and transformed, and 16 yielded viable, bacteria-killing phages - the first AI-authored genomes that function. Nature Reviews Genetics ran a Tools of the Trade piece by Samuel King on 17 November 2026, Generative genome design with DNA language models, walking through design, synthesis and validation, which is a reliable marker that a technique has moved from stunt to method. This sits alongside a hard-engineering track on the same problem: Nature Reviews Bioengineering published De novo design of synthetic microbial genomes (23 February 2026, Koster, da Costa Oliveira and Claassens) on rational genome design and genome-scale organisation; a bioRxiv group reported Generating E. coli 0.5 controlled by a half-sized genome by fleshing out an imperfect minimal genome through genome-scale debugging; Nature Biotechnology covered the Sc2.0 synthetic yeast chromosome programme; and Nature news reported both a genome transplant reviving 'zombie cells' (24 March 2026) and bacteria running key machinery on 19 rather than 20 amino acids via AI-guided redesign (30 April 2026). Nature also ran a Book Review by Kate Adamala in February 2026 asking directly whether AI genome design will upend how life evolves. Note the biosafety design choices embedded in the phage work: viruses infecting humans and close relatives were excluded from training, and only non-pathogenic E. coli hosts were used.","body_zh":"里程碑式的成果來自史丹佛與 Arc Institute 的噬菌體研究：他們用 Evo 1 與 Evo 2 以 5,386 個核苷酸的 phiX174 為範本生成完整的噬菌體基因組，取樣約 70 萬個候選基因組，化學合成並轉形其中 285 個，有 16 個長出能存活、能殺菌的噬菌體——這是第一批真正有功能的 AI 撰寫基因組。Nature Reviews Genetics 於 2026 年 11 月 17 日刊出 Samuel King 的 Tools of the Trade 文章 Generative genome design with DNA language models，逐步說明設計、合成與驗證流程，這是一項技術從噱頭變成方法的可靠指標。與此並行的是同一問題的硬工程路線：Nature Reviews Bioengineering 發表 De novo design of synthetic microbial genomes（2026 年 2 月 23 日，Koster、da Costa Oliveira 與 Claassens），討論理性基因組設計與基因組尺度的組織安排；一個 bioRxiv 團隊回報 Generating E. coli 0.5 controlled by a half-sized genome，以基因組尺度的除錯把一個不完美的最小基因組補齊；Nature Biotechnology 報導了 Sc2.0 合成酵母染色體計畫；Nature 新聞則報導了以基因組移植讓「殭屍細胞」復活（2026 年 3 月 24 日），以及透過 AI 引導的重新設計，讓細菌用 19 種而非 20 種胺基酸運作關鍵機制（2026 年 4 月 30 日）。Nature 也在 2026 年 2 月刊出 Kate Adamala 的書評，直接追問 AI 基因組設計是否會徹底改變生命演化的方式。值得注意的是噬菌體研究內建的生物安全設計：訓練資料排除了感染人類及其近親的病毒，宿主也只用非致病性的 E. coli。","whyItMatters":"Genome-scale design shifts synthetic biology's unit of work from the part and the circuit to the whole chassis, which re-prices DNA synthesis as the real bottleneck and makes computational sequence design the highest-leverage skill in the pipeline. It is also the trend with the sharpest dual-use profile, so institutional credibility will depend on being visibly thoughtful about it before anyone asks.","whyItMatters_zh":"基因組尺度的設計把合成生物學的工作單位從元件與電路推進到整個底盤，於是 DNA 合成重新被定價為真正的瓶頸，而計算序列設計成為整條流程中槓桿最大的能力。這也是雙重用途風險最尖銳的一項趨勢，因此機構的可信度取決於在別人問起之前，就已經看得出有認真思考過。","gemsAction":"Teach genome language models as a reading-and-critique unit rather than a build project: have students generate and computationally evaluate sequences (promoters, regulatory DNA, small operons) without synthesising anything, which captures nearly all the educational value at zero biosafety cost. Where GEMS does build, stay at the part and pathway scale and adopt the phage paper's conventions explicitly - non-pathogenic hosts, excluded sequence classes, documented rationale. Write that stance down now as a one-page institutional policy; it will be required for collaborations and funding within the year.","gemsAction_zh":"把基因組語言模型當成閱讀與批判的單元來教，而不是一個建構專案：讓學生生成序列（啟動子、調控 DNA、小型操縱子）並以計算方式評估，完全不做合成，這樣幾乎能取得全部的教學價值，而生物安全成本為零。GEMS 真的要動手建構時，就守在元件與路徑的尺度，並明確採用噬菌體那篇論文的規範——非致病宿主、排除特定序列類別、記錄下判斷理由。現在就把這個立場寫成一頁的機構政策；一年之內，合作與經費申請都會要求它。","maturity":"emerging","refs":[{"title":"Generative genome design with DNA language models","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41576-026-01032-3","venue":"Nature Reviews Genetics (Tools of the Trade)","year":2026},{"title":"Generative design of novel bacteriophages with genome language models","url":"https://www.biorxiv.org/content/10.1101/2025.09.12.675911.full.pdf","venue":"bioRxiv preprint (subsequently published 2026)","year":2025},{"title":"De novo design of synthetic microbial genomes","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s44222-026-00410-0","venue":"Nature Reviews Bioengineering","year":2026},{"title":"World's first AI-designed viruses a step towards AI-generated life","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-025-03055-y","venue":"Nature (News)","year":2025},{"title":"AI tools can design genomes. Will they upend how life evolves?","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-026-00566-0","venue":"Nature (Book Review, Kate Adamala)","year":2026},{"title":"All life runs on 20 amino acids. These cells run key machinery on just 19","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-026-01396-w","venue":"Nature (News)","year":2026}]},{"id":"agentic-ai-autonomous-labs","title":"Agentic AI moved from literature assistant to experiment designer and robot driver","title_zh":"代理式 AI 從文獻助手升級為實驗設計者與機器人操作者","oneLine":"Robin, Biomni, Co-Scientist and cloud biofoundries closed the loop from hypothesis to robot to analysis, and the 2026 question is no longer whether agents can run experiments but how to validate what they conclude.","oneLine_zh":"Robin、Biomni、Co-Scientist 與雲端生物鑄造廠已把從假說到機器人再到分析的迴路閉合，2026 年的問題不再是代理能否執行實驗，而是如何驗證它們得出的結論。","body":"A 2026 Cell review on agentic AI for autonomous science classifies three paradigms that all landed in top venues within about a year. Robin, a multi-agent system published in Nature in 2026, linked hypothesis generation to data analysis in a lab-in-the-loop cycle and identified ripasudil and KL001 as enhancers of RPE phagocytosis, proposing ripasudil for dry age-related macular degeneration. Biomni (Science, 2026) is a general-purpose biomedical agent released open source as an environment (Biomni-E1), architecture (Biomni-A1) and RL-trained models (Biomni-R0), reporting generalisation across causal gene prioritisation, drug repurposing and rare-disease diagnosis. Google's Co-Scientist (Gottweis et al., 2026) is a Gemini-based tournament of agents validated on AML drug repurposing with in vitro confirmation, novel target discovery and antimicrobial resistance mechanisms. Synthetic biology specifically is getting its own instances: an October 2026 bioRxiv preprint describes iCloudBiofoundry, a cloud-accessible platform pairing agentic AI with robotic execution through a layer that translates protocols into automation workflows, with three experimentally validated case studies; MicroGrowAgents (bioRxiv, June 2026) is an agentic system for microbial cultivation optimisation; a Scientific Reports paper (8 September 2026) integrates LLMs with knowledge graphs for metabolic pathway design in food synthetic biology; and a bioRxiv group is using LLMs for ontology-driven generation of SBOL knowledge-graph software with Beal, Myers and Misirli as authors. The counter-evidence matters: a 2026 arXiv study of agentic self-driving microscopy found that benchmarks support qualification but do not necessarily generalise to unseen tasks, and an Experiment-as-Code paper documents the real integration tax - one major orchestration framework maintains 28 device instances across 16 device types, each needing a hand-coded adapter. Emerald Cloud Lab remains the proof that fully programmable cloud labs are commercially viable and the warning that the ecosystem is closed and proprietary.","body_zh":"2026 年 Cell 上一篇關於自主科學中代理式 AI 的綜述，歸納出三種範式，而它們都在大約一年內登上頂級期刊。Robin 是 2026 年發表於 Nature 的多代理系統，在一個「實驗室在迴路中」的循環裡把假說生成與資料分析串接起來，找出 ripasudil 與 KL001 能增強 RPE 的吞噬作用，並提議以 ripasudil 治療乾性年齡相關性黃斑部病變。Biomni（Science，2026）是一個通用型生醫代理，以開放原始碼形式釋出，包含環境（Biomni-E1）、架構（Biomni-A1）與經強化學習訓練的模型（Biomni-R0），回報能泛化到致病基因優先排序、老藥新用與罕見疾病診斷等任務。Google 的 Co-Scientist（Gottweis 等人，2026）是一套基於 Gemini 的代理競賽機制，在 AML 老藥新用（並經體外實驗確認）、新標的發現與抗藥性機制上得到驗證。合成生物學也開始有自己的版本：2026 年 10 月的一篇 bioRxiv 預印本介紹 iCloudBiofoundry，一個可從雲端存取的平台，透過一層能把實驗流程翻譯成自動化工作流的中介，把代理式 AI 與機器人執行配對起來，並附三個經實驗驗證的案例；MicroGrowAgents（bioRxiv，2026 年 6 月）是用於微生物培養條件最佳化的代理系統；Scientific Reports 的一篇論文（2026 年 9 月 8 日）把 LLM 與知識圖譜整合起來，用於食品合成生物學的代謝路徑設計；還有一個 bioRxiv 團隊（作者包括 Beal、Myers 與 Misirli）正以 LLM 進行本體論驅動的 SBOL 知識圖譜軟體生成。反面證據同樣重要：2026 年 arXiv 上一份關於代理式自駕顯微鏡的研究發現，基準測試足以支持資格認定，但不必然能推廣到未見過的任務；一篇 Experiment-as-Code 論文則記錄了真實的整合成本——某個主要的流程協調框架維護著橫跨 16 種裝置型別的 28 個裝置實例，每一個都需要手寫的轉接程式。Emerald Cloud Lab 既證明了完全可程式化的雲端實驗室在商業上可行，也是一記警告：這個生態系是封閉且專有的。","whyItMatters":"Agents compress the literature-to-hypothesis step that normally takes a graduate student months, which disproportionately helps institutions rich in motivated students but poor in senior specialist time - precisely GEMS's profile. The accompanying risk is that an agent produces confident, well-formatted, wrong hypotheses, so the institutional differentiator becomes a culture of verification rather than access to the agent.","whyItMatters_zh":"代理把通常要耗掉研究生數個月的「文獻到假說」環節大幅壓縮，這對學生動機充足、但資深專家時間匱乏的機構格外有利——正是 GEMS 的樣貌。隨之而來的風險是代理會產出自信、格式漂亮但錯誤的假說，因此機構真正的差異化不在於能不能用到代理，而在於有沒有驗證的文化。","gemsAction":"Adopt one open agent stack (Biomni is open source and the natural choice) on institutional infrastructure and make every student project run a documented agent-assisted literature and hypothesis pass whose outputs are then manually checked, with disagreements logged. Build the verification habit as the deliverable: a standing rule that no agent-proposed claim enters a report without a human-traced primary citation. For automation, do not buy a biofoundry - instead negotiate time on an existing cloud lab or a regional biofoundry and write protocols in a machine-readable form from day one so GEMS work is portable when it does scale.","gemsAction_zh":"在機構自有的基礎設施上採用一套開放的代理堆疊（Biomni 是開放原始碼，也是自然的選擇），並要求每個學生專案都跑一輪有記錄的代理輔助文獻與假說回合，其產出再由人工逐項檢查，不一致之處要留下紀錄。把驗證習慣本身當成交付成果：訂一條長期規則——任何代理提出的主張，若沒有人工追溯到的原始文獻引用，就不得寫進報告。自動化方面不要自己買生物鑄造廠，而是去談現有雲端實驗室或區域性生物鑄造廠的機時，並從第一天就以機器可讀的格式撰寫實驗流程，這樣 GEMS 的工作在要放大規模時才具可攜性。","maturity":"accelerating","refs":[{"title":"Toward autonomous science with agentic artificial intelligence","url":"https://www.cell.com/cell/fulltext/S0092-8674(26)01063-9?rss=yes","venue":"Cell (Review)","year":2026},{"title":"An AI-powered cloud biofoundry for autonomous biological research (iCloudBiofoundry)","url":"https://www.biorxiv.org/content/10.64898/2026.09.30.750244v1.full","venue":"bioRxiv preprint","year":2026},{"title":"MicroGrowAgents: An Agentic AI System for Microbial Cultivation Engineering","url":"https://www.biorxiv.org/content/10.64898/2026.06.04.729985v1","venue":"bioRxiv preprint","year":2026},{"title":"Agentic self-driving microscopy benchmarks support qualification but do not necessarily generalize to unseen tasks","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2608.05266","venue":"arXiv preprint","year":2026},{"title":"Experiment-as-Code Labs: A Declarative Stack for AI-Driven Scientific Discovery","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2605.04375","venue":"arXiv preprint","year":2026},{"title":"Ontology-driven software engineering using LLMs for knowledge graphs in engineering biology","url":"https://www.biorxiv.org/content/10.64898/2026.05.29.728869v2","venue":"bioRxiv preprint","year":2026},{"title":"Synergistic integration of large language models and knowledge graphs for intelligent metabolic pathway design in food synthetic biology","url":"https://www.nature.com/search?q=synthetic+biology&order=date","venue":"Scientific Reports","year":2026}]},{"id":"ml-dbtl-digital-cell-factories","title":"ML-guided DBTL and 'digital cell factories' now beat intuition on real titers","title_zh":"機器學習導引的 DBTL 與「數位細胞工廠」在真實產量上已勝過直覺","oneLine":"Machine learning over genome-scale models has stopped being a methods paper and started delivering multi-fold titer gains in a handful of cycles, with the field explicitly pivoting from biological realism to economic prediction.","oneLine_zh":"在基因組尺度代謝模型之上做機器學習，已不再只是方法論文，而是在幾個循環內就帶來數倍的產量提升，而整個領域也明確地從追求生物真實性轉向預測經濟成果。","body":"The numbers are now concrete enough to plan around. Carruthers et al. (Nature Communications, 2025) coupled lab automation with ML to optimise isoprenol in Pseudomonas putida: CRISPRi downregulation of combinations of up to four gene targets raised titer five-fold over six consecutive DBTL cycles, while ML reduced a design space of roughly 800,000 combinations to about 400 priority constructs, with high-throughput proteomics used to validate the mechanism. Van Lent et al. (ACS Synthetic Biology, 2026) ran two DBTL cycles on p-coumaric acid in S. cerevisiae over a library of 18 genes and 20 promoters spanning about 170 million possible designs, and showed a gradient-bandit exploration-exploitation recommender beating greedy feature-importance selection, reaching 1.23 g/L - a 2.37-fold improvement; an earlier Moreno Paz study reached 0.52 g/L with a 68 percent gain in two cycles. The framing is also shifting: Chen, Li and Nielsen's Comment Digital cell factories for biomanufacturing (Nature Reviews Bioengineering, 4 November 2026) argues for metabolism-centric digital cell factories that privilege predictions of production performance and economic outcomes over biological detail - an explicitly pragmatic turn. Supporting infrastructure arrived too: Persephone (Nature Protocols, 5 November 2026) is an automated pipeline for personalising and evaluating human whole-body metabolic models coupled to community microbiome models; Canopy (ICML 2026) is a heterograph foundation model for metabolic engineering that beats tabular baselines on fermentation titer prediction; ML4SD (bioRxiv, September 2026) runs active learning over genome-scale-model scores for growth-coupled knockout design with explicit uncertainty; and iModulon-based engraftment (Nature Communications) uses ML decomposition of transcriptome compendia to transfer functions across species. A June 2026 bioRxiv preprint benchmarks LLM competence on genome-scale model analysis and finds they surface structural and data-quality limitations in the models themselves.","body_zh":"這些數字現在已經具體到可以據此規劃。Carruthers 等人（Nature Communications，2025）把實驗室自動化與機器學習結合，最佳化 Pseudomonas putida 的 isoprenol 生產：用 CRISPRi 下調最多四個基因標的的各種組合，在連續六個 DBTL 循環中把產量提高五倍，機器學習則把約 80 萬種組合的設計空間縮減到約 400 個優先構築體，並以高通量蛋白質體學驗證機制。Van Lent 等人（ACS Synthetic Biology，2026）針對 S. cerevisiae 生產 p-coumaric acid 執行兩個 DBTL 循環，函式庫涵蓋 18 個基因與 20 個啟動子、約 1.7 億種可能設計，結果顯示採用 gradient-bandit 探索—利用策略的推薦系統勝過貪婪式的特徵重要度選擇，達到 1.23 g/L，提升 2.37 倍；更早的 Moreno Paz 研究則在兩個循環內達到 0.52 g/L，提升 68%。論述框架也在轉變：Chen、Li 與 Nielsen 的評論 Digital cell factories for biomanufacturing（Nature Reviews Bioengineering，2026 年 11 月 4 日）主張建立以代謝為核心的數位細胞工廠，優先預測生產表現與經濟成果，而非追求生物細節——這是一個明確的務實轉向。支援性的基礎設施也到位了：Persephone（Nature Protocols，2026 年 11 月 5 日）是一條自動化流程，用於個人化並評估與群落微生物體模型耦合的人體全身代謝模型；Canopy（ICML 2026）是用於代謝工程的異質圖基礎模型，在發酵產量預測上勝過表格式基準方法；ML4SD（bioRxiv，2026 年 9 月）在基因組尺度模型的評分之上執行主動學習，用於帶明確不確定度的生長耦合基因剔除設計；以 iModulon 為基礎的功能移植（Nature Communications）則用機器學習分解轉錄體資料彙編，把功能跨物種轉移。2026 年 6 月的一篇 bioRxiv 預印本評測 LLM 在基因組尺度模型分析上的能力，發現它們反而暴露出這些模型本身在結構與資料品質上的限制。","whyItMatters":"This is the single clearest case where dry lab demonstrably outperforms expert intuition on an industrially meaningful metric, so it is the strongest evidence for the report's thesis. It is also unusually cheap to join: COBRApy, a published GEM and scikit-learn cost nothing, and the published benchmarks are reproducible, so a small institution can build real credibility before owning a fermenter.","whyItMatters_zh":"這是乾式實驗室在一個具工業意義的指標上明確勝過專家直覺的最清楚案例，因此也是本報告論點最有力的證據。它的入門成本也異常低廉：COBRApy、一個已發表的 GEM 加上 scikit-learn 都不花錢，而已發表的基準測試可以重現，所以小型機構在還沒有自己的發酵槽之前，就能累積真實的學術信譽。","gemsAction":"Make genome-scale metabolic modelling a core taught competency within 12 months: COBRApy plus flux balance analysis plus one published Bacillus subtilis GEM, with students reproducing the van Lent exploration-versus-exploitation comparison in silico before touching a flask. Then run one real two-cycle ML-guided DBTL campaign on a small combinatorial library in GEMS's own chassis, with the recommender written by students and the design space documented - two cycles is enough to produce a publishable, honest result. Seek a collaboration with an Agile BioFoundry-style or regional biofoundry group for the build step rather than buying liquid handlers.","gemsAction_zh":"在 12 個月內把基因組尺度代謝模型訂為核心教學能力：COBRApy 加上通量平衡分析，再加一個已發表的 Bacillus subtilis GEM，讓學生在碰到搖瓶之前，先在電腦上重現 van Lent 的探索對利用比較。接著在 GEMS 自己的底盤上，針對一個小型組合式函式庫執行一次真正的兩循環機器學習導引 DBTL 行動，推薦系統由學生撰寫，設計空間完整記錄——兩個循環就足以產生一個可發表且誠實的結果。建構環節不要買自動分液工作站，而是尋求與 Agile BioFoundry 這類或區域性生物鑄造廠團隊合作。","maturity":"accelerating","refs":[{"title":"Automation and machine learning drive rapid optimization of isoprenol production in Pseudomonas putida","url":"https://consensus.app/papers/details/w:b89d3c61-1875-424b-bc8a-f2eb8872c5fc/","venue":"Nature Communications","year":2025},{"title":"Machine-Learning-Assisted Pathway Optimization in Large Combinatorial Design Spaces: A p-Coumaric Acid Case Study","url":"https://consensus.app/papers/details/w:dd1e4b40-af66-4d27-a02a-77c20fcbd0ac/","venue":"ACS Synthetic Biology","year":2026},{"title":"Digital cell factories for biomanufacturing","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s44222-026-00506-7","venue":"Nature Reviews Bioengineering (Comment)","year":2026},{"title":"Personalization and evaluation of human whole-body metabolic models and community microbiome models using Persephone","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41596-026-01437-8","venue":"Nature Protocols","year":2026},{"title":"Canopy: A Heterograph Foundation Model for Metabolic Engineering","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2607.06224","venue":"arXiv / ICML","year":2026},{"title":"ML4SD: Leveraging Machine Learning and High-Throughput Search Algorithms for an Iterative Growth-Coupled Design Innovation","url":"https://www.biorxiv.org/content/10.64898/2026.09.11.750664v1.full","venue":"bioRxiv preprint","year":2026}]},{"id":"automation-and-throughput-of-build","title":"The Build step is being industrialised: cell-free prototyping, one-pot gene synthesis and million-scale design-space mapping","title_zh":"Build 環節正在工業化：無細胞原型製作、一鍋式基因合成與百萬尺度的設計空間繪製","oneLine":"Robotic cell-free platforms, hybridisation-driven gene synthesis and long-read multiplexed profiling have broken the DNA-construction bottleneck that used to set the pace of every synthetic biology project.","oneLine_zh":"機器人化的無細胞平台、以雜交驅動的基因合成，以及長讀長多重定序分析，已經打破了過去決定每一個合成生物學專案節奏的 DNA 構築瓶頸。","body":"Four 2026 papers together redefine what a 'build' costs. Automated prototyping of genetic codes (Nature, 26 August 2026, Radford, Sapers and Church) is a robotic cell-free platform that rapidly prototypes redesigned genetic codes, translating proteins with reassigned codons and non-standard amino acids without modifying any living genome - cell-free as the fast lane that avoids the viability constraint entirely. MOSAIC (Nature Biotechnology, 19 August 2026, Wu, Sun and Wei) replaces enzymatic processing with hybridisation: self-assembly of complementary oligonucleotides during thermal annealing, exploiting the full capacity of microchip oligo synthesis to produce over 1,000 distinct gene fragments and mutant libraries in a one-pot reaction. CLASSIC (Nature, 14 January 2026, Rai, O'Connell and Bashor) combines long- and short-read sequencing to quantitatively profile pools of arbitrary-length constructs with diverse genetic part compositions, which is how you actually map a genetic design space rather than sample it. Nature Biotechnology also published a microchip-based massively parallel DNA synthesis system, and Nature ran a Technology Feature on made-to-order DNA doubling achievable sequence length. The frugal end is advancing in parallel and matters more for GEMS: DropSynth-Gold (bioRxiv, June 2026, Plesa lab) extends emulsion-based multiplexed gene synthesis to longer genes via Golden Gate in droplets, and the Salis lab posted A Low-Cost, High-Throughput Design-Build-Test Pipeline for Engineering Genetic Systems (bioRxiv, June 2026) stress-tested on complex structural proteins - explicitly motivated by high DNA synthesis costs and assembly inefficiency. Also notable for throughput of measurement rather than build: Nature Biotechnology's Highly multiplexed mammalian metabolic engineering with a shotgun approach (Boeke lab, 6 October 2026).","body_zh":"2026 年有四篇論文合起來重新定義了「建構」的成本。Automated prototyping of genetic codes（Nature，2026 年 8 月 26 日，Radford、Sapers 與 Church）是一個機器人化的無細胞平台，能快速試做重新設計的遺傳密碼，用重新指派的密碼子與非標準胺基酸轉譯蛋白質，完全不必改動任何活體基因組——無細胞系統成為繞開存活性限制的快車道。MOSAIC（Nature Biotechnology，2026 年 8 月 19 日，Wu、Sun 與 Wei）以雜交取代酵素處理：在熱退火過程中讓互補寡核苷酸自組裝，充分利用微晶片寡核苷酸合成的產能，在一鍋反應中做出超過 1,000 個不同的基因片段與突變函式庫。CLASSIC（Nature，2026 年 1 月 14 日，Rai、O'Connell 與 Bashor）結合長讀長與短讀長定序，定量分析由任意長度、元件組成各異的構築體所組成的池，這才是真正繪製基因設計空間的做法，而不只是抽樣。Nature Biotechnology 另外發表了一套以微晶片為基礎的大規模平行 DNA 合成系統，Nature 也刊出一篇技術特寫，談客製化 DNA 合成可達序列長度翻倍。節約路線同時也在推進，而且對 GEMS 更重要：DropSynth-Gold（bioRxiv，2026 年 6 月，Plesa 實驗室）在液滴中以 Golden Gate 把乳化液為基礎的多重基因合成延伸到更長的基因；Salis 實驗室則發表 A Low-Cost, High-Throughput Design-Build-Test Pipeline for Engineering Genetic Systems（bioRxiv，2026 年 6 月），並以複雜的結構蛋白做壓力測試——其動機明確就是 DNA 合成成本高昂與組裝效率不佳。另外在量測通量（而非建構通量）上值得注意的是 Nature Biotechnology 的 Highly multiplexed mammalian metabolic engineering with a shotgun approach（Boeke 實驗室，2026 年 10 月 6 日）。","whyItMatters":"When build capacity jumps by orders of magnitude, the binding constraint moves to design and measurement - which is the mechanism by which the dry lab becomes the engine. For a budget-constrained institution the frugal-pipeline papers are the actionable half: they are deliberately engineered for labs that cannot spend on commercial synthesis, and they are exactly the kind of method a strong student team can implement and own.","whyItMatters_zh":"當建構能力以數個數量級跳升，真正的限制就轉移到設計與量測——這正是乾式實驗室成為引擎的機制。對預算有限的機構來說，節約流程那幾篇論文才是可以動手的那一半：它們本來就是為買不起商業合成服務的實驗室設計的，也正是一支強的學生團隊能實作並據為己有的那種方法。","gemsAction":"Implement one frugal high-throughput build method end to end - the Salis low-cost DBTL pipeline or DropSynth-style pooled assembly - as a flagship capability project, and publish the cost-per-construct GEMS achieves. Pair it with cell-free (TXTL) prototyping as the default first test for any new circuit, because cell-free removes transformation, growth and biosafety friction and is ideal for a student-paced institution. Budget for long-read sequencing access rather than more pipetting capacity; CLASSIC shows that measurement depth, not construct count, is what converts a library into knowledge.","gemsAction_zh":"把一套節約型高通量建構方法從頭到尾實作出來——Salis 的低成本 DBTL 流程，或 DropSynth 式的混池組裝——當作旗艦能力專案，並公布 GEMS 做到的每個構築體單位成本。搭配無細胞（TXTL）原型製作，作為任何新電路的預設第一輪測試，因為無細胞系統省去轉形、培養與生物安全的摩擦，非常適合以學生步調運作的機構。預算應該花在取得長讀長定序，而不是增加移液量能；CLASSIC 已經說明，把函式庫轉換成知識的是量測深度，而不是構築體數量。","maturity":"accelerating","refs":[{"title":"Automated prototyping of genetic codes","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-026-10949-y","venue":"Nature","year":2026},{"title":"High-throughput synthesis of DNA fragments by molecular self-assembly of overlapping oligonucleotides (MOSAIC)","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41587-026-03266-2","venue":"Nature Biotechnology","year":2026},{"title":"Massive-scale parallel gene synthesis with oligonucleotide hybridization","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41587-026-03290-2","venue":"Nature Biotechnology (Research Briefing)","year":2026},{"title":"Ultra-high-throughput mapping of genetic design space (CLASSIC)","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-025-09933-9","venue":"Nature","year":2026},{"title":"DropSynth-Gold: Golden Gate Assembly in Emulsions Extends Multiplexed Gene Libraries to Greater Lengths","url":"https://www.biorxiv.org/content/10.64898/2026.05.29.728538v1","venue":"bioRxiv preprint","year":2026},{"title":"A Low-Cost, High-Throughput Design-Build-Test Pipeline for Engineering Genetic Systems","url":"https://www.biorxiv.org/content/10.64898/2026.06.08.729977v1","venue":"bioRxiv preprint (Salis lab)","year":2026},{"title":"Highly multiplexed mammalian metabolic engineering with a shotgun approach","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41587-026-03318-7","venue":"Nature Biotechnology","year":2026}]},{"id":"ml-designed-biosensors","title":"Biosensors are now machine-designed, not discovered - including the receptor itself","title_zh":"生物感測器現在是機器設計出來的，不是找到的——連受體本身也是","oneLine":"Nature Biotechnology published fully synthetic allosteric switches whose ligand-binding receptors were designed by machine learning, which turns biosensing from a search problem into a design problem.","oneLine_zh":"Nature Biotechnology 發表了完全人工合成的異位調節開關，其配體結合受體由機器學習設計，這把生物感測從搜尋問題變成設計問題。","body":"Artificial allosteric protein switches with machine-learning-designed receptors (Nature Biotechnology, 15 April 2026, Guo, Smutok and Alexandrov) is the pivotal result: ML-engineered minimal ligand-binding domains work as efficient receptors in single-component allosteric switches despite lacking global conformational change, yielding colorimetric, luminescent and electrochemical biosensors for small molecules, peptides and proteins, which the authors then compile into intramolecular YES and AND logic gates. They report fully synthetic switches built from artificial receptor plus artificial reporter domains, use HDX-MS and 19F NMR to attribute the mechanism to ligand-induced reduction of conformational entropy raising reporter catalytic activity, and demonstrate utility by engineering E. coli with steroid-dependent antibiotic resistance and bioelectronic devices that quantify steroid hormones. Around it sits a dense 2026 biosensing literature: Synthetic microbial co-cultures for modular bioelectronic sensing in diverse environments (Nature Biotechnology, 17 April 2026, Li, Zhu and Ajo-Franklin) modularises whole-cell electrical sensing across environments; Bacteria as living biosensors for DNA (Nature Reviews Bioengineering, 30 October 2025) benchmarks bacterial DNA biosensors against in vitro ones in unpurified samples; Nature Methods highlighted Engineering gut biosensors (12 March 2026); Nature published engineered magneto-sensitive fluorescent proteins for multimodal quantum-spin-resonance sensing (21 January 2026, Abrahams, Stuhec and Steel); and Scientific Reports published a Corynebacterium glutamicum glutamate-binding protein as a fluorescence probe (13 November 2026). On the cell-free diagnostics side, 2026 reviews converge on lyophilisation compatibility as cell-free's decisive advantage, with reported lyophilised Cas12a wearable and face-mask formats reaching femtomolar detection in 56 to 78 minutes, and a January 2026 microfluidic paper device integrating lyophilised RPA plus Cas12a across seven functional zones for colorimetric HPV16 E7 detection - but field validation, shelf life and sensitivity remain the stated gaps, and I found no deployed field trial.","body_zh":"Artificial allosteric protein switches with machine-learning-designed receptors（Nature Biotechnology，2026 年 4 月 15 日，Guo、Smutok 與 Alexandrov）是關鍵成果：以機器學習設計的最小配體結合域，即使缺乏整體構形變化，仍能在單一元件的異位調節開關中作為高效受體，做出針對小分子、胜肽與蛋白質的比色、發光與電化學生物感測器，作者接著把它們組成分子內的 YES 與 AND 邏輯閘。他們回報由人工受體加人工報導域組成的完全合成開關，並以 HDX-MS 與 19F NMR 把機制歸因於配體誘導構形熵下降、進而提高報導域的催化活性，還以兩個應用展示實用性：工程化出抗生素抗性依賴類固醇的 E. coli，以及可定量類固醇激素的生物電子裝置。圍繞它的是 2026 年一片密集的生物感測文獻：Synthetic microbial co-cultures for modular bioelectronic sensing in diverse environments（Nature Biotechnology，2026 年 4 月 17 日，Li、Zhu 與 Ajo-Franklin）把全細胞電訊號感測模組化，可跨不同環境使用；Bacteria as living biosensors for DNA（Nature Reviews Bioengineering，2025 年 10 月 30 日）以未純化樣品比較細菌型 DNA 生物感測器與體外方法；Nature Methods 介紹了 Engineering gut biosensors（2026 年 3 月 12 日）；Nature 發表了用於多模態量子自旋共振感測的工程化磁敏螢光蛋白（2026 年 1 月 21 日，Abrahams、Stuhec 與 Steel）；Scientific Reports 則發表以 Corynebacterium glutamicum 的麩胺酸結合蛋白作為螢光探針（2026 年 11 月 13 日）。在無細胞診斷方面，2026 年的多篇綜述都認為「可凍乾」是無細胞系統的決定性優勢，已有報告指出凍乾的 Cas12a 穿戴式與口罩型格式能在 56 到 78 分鐘內達到飛莫耳級偵測；2026 年 1 月另有一個微流體紙基裝置，在七個功能區整合凍乾的 RPA 與 Cas12a，以比色法偵測 HPV16 E7——但現場驗證、保存期限與靈敏度仍是文獻自己點出的缺口，我也沒有找到任何已實地部署的試驗。","whyItMatters":"Biosensing is the one frontier area where a small institution can do complete, publishable work, because the readout is cheap, the chassis can be non-pathogenic, and the ML design step is now the hard part rather than the receptor search. It is also the natural bridge between GEMS's dry-lab ambitions and its existing wet-lab strengths, and it feeds directly into the team's optogenetic Bacillus plant-protection project, where a sensor output is what makes a device rather than a demo.","whyItMatters_zh":"生物感測是小型機構唯一能做出完整、可發表成果的前沿領域，因為讀出訊號便宜、底盤可以用非致病菌，而且困難的環節已經從受體搜尋轉移到機器學習設計。它也是 GEMS 乾式實驗室企圖與既有濕式實驗室強項之間的自然橋樑，並直接餵進團隊的光遺傳學 Bacillus 植物保護專案——有感測器輸出，做出來的才是裝置，而不是展示品。","gemsAction":"Make ML-designed biosensing GEMS's declared niche and build the Alexandrov-style workflow in house: take a published minimal binding domain, redesign its specificity computationally, and validate with a colorimetric or electrochemical readout - a project that fits a student timescale and produces a real number. Standardise on lyophilised cell-free (TXTL) as the delivery format so the output is a shelf-stable field test rather than a plate reading, and pair it with a low-cost reader. Approach the Alexandrov group (Queensland) and Ajo-Franklin lab (Rice) for a protocol-level collaboration; both publish open and both work on sensor modalities GEMS could extend to agricultural targets.","gemsAction_zh":"把「機器學習設計的生物感測」定為 GEMS 對外宣示的利基，並在內部建立 Alexandrov 式的工作流程：取一個已發表的最小結合域，用計算方法重新設計其專一性，再以比色或電化學讀出加以驗證——這個專案符合學生的時間尺度，而且會產出一個真實的數字。把凍乾無細胞（TXTL）標準化為交付格式，讓產出是一個可常溫保存的現場檢測，而不是一次盤讀數據，並搭配一台低成本讀取器。接洽 Alexandrov 團隊（Queensland）與 Ajo-Franklin 實驗室（Rice）尋求實驗流程層級的合作；兩者都走開放發表，而且研究的感測模式 GEMS 都能延伸到農業標的。","maturity":"accelerating","refs":[{"title":"Artificial allosteric protein switches with machine-learning-designed receptors","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41587-026-03081-9","venue":"Nature Biotechnology","year":2026},{"title":"Synthetic microbial co-cultures for modular bioelectronic sensing in diverse environments","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41587-026-03075-7","venue":"Nature Biotechnology","year":2026},{"title":"Bacteria as living biosensors for DNA","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s44222-025-00369-4","venue":"Nature Reviews Bioengineering","year":2025},{"title":"Quantum spin resonance in engineered proteins for multimodal sensing","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-025-09971-3","venue":"Nature","year":2026},{"title":"Engineering gut biosensors","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41592-026-03039-4","venue":"Nature Methods (Research Highlight)","year":2026},{"title":"Integrated Colorimetric CRISPR/Cas12a Detection of Double-Stranded DNA on Microfluidic Paper-Based Analytical Devices","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC12839233/","venue":"PMC","year":2026},{"title":"Cell-Free Protein Synthesis-Based Biosensing Platforms for Clinical Diagnostics","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41979265/","venue":"ACS Sensors (review)","year":2026}]},{"id":"optogenetics-closed-loop-cybergenetics","title":"Optogenetics grew up into closed-loop bioprocess control - and Bacillus is nearly untouched","title_zh":"光遺傳學成熟為閉環生物製程控制——而 Bacillus 幾乎還沒人碰","oneLine":"Light has become a real-time actuator for feedback control of fermentation, with reported 60 percent titer gains in a 1 L photobioreactor, while optogenetics in Bacillus subtilis remains almost unexplored - twelve papers in all of PubMed.","oneLine_zh":"光已成為發酵回饋控制的即時致動器，有報告在 1 L 光生物反應器中取得 60% 的產量提升，但 Bacillus subtilis 的光遺傳學幾乎仍無人開發——整個 PubMed 只有十二篇論文。","body":"Cybergenetics - closing a control loop around a live culture using light as the manipulated variable - matured in 2026 from proof of principle to bioprocess tool. A Trends in Biotechnology study reported closed-loop optogenetic feedback on the yeast unfolded protein response in a custom 1 L photobioreactor, adjusting alpha-amylase expression from real-time measurements and achieving roughly 60 percent higher product titers. LEMOS (ACS Synthetic Biology, 2026) is an LED-equipped microplate integrating programmable illumination with continuous growth and gene-expression measurement for closed-loop control, paired with GEAGS, a model accounting for how gene expression changes across growth stages - which is the practical answer to the fact that optogenetic dose-response curves are steep enough to push systems to fully on or fully off, making intermediate setpoints hard, hence the emergence of pulse-width-modulated switching-time control. Light-controlled Corynebacterium glutamicum fermentation has been reported at 6.2 g/L for chitooligosaccharides. The protein-engineering side advanced too: Nature Methods published Design and optimization of a kinase-controlled allosteric switch (21 July 2026, Cao and Toettcher) and previously ProDomino, an ML model predicting domain insertion sites from sequence alone to accelerate design of light- and drug-triggered protein switches; Nature Biotechnology published a photoactivatable A-to-I RNA base editor for in vivo gene therapy; Advanced Science (2026) reported engineered optogenetic circuits in yeast with self-sustained outputs. The striking gap, which I verified directly: a PubMed search for optogenetics plus Bacillus subtilis returns twelve records in total, across all years, with the foundational work being a CcaS/CcaR green-red system ported from cyanobacteria. There is no published light-controlled B. subtilis bioreactor, and no published optogenetic control of Bacillus biocontrol or plant-growth-promoting function.","body_zh":"Cybergenetics——以光作為操作變數，在活體培養物外圍閉合一個控制迴路——在 2026 年從原理驗證成熟為生物製程工具。Trends in Biotechnology 的一項研究回報，在自製的 1 L 光生物反應器中對酵母的未摺疊蛋白反應做閉環光遺傳回饋，依即時量測調整 alpha-amylase 的表現量，產物產量提高約 60%。LEMOS（ACS Synthetic Biology，2026）是一塊配備 LED 的微量盤，把可程式化照光與連續的生長及基因表現量測整合起來以實現閉環控制，並搭配 GEAGS——一個描述基因表現如何隨生長階段改變的模型。這是對一個現實問題的實務解答：光遺傳學的劑量反應曲線陡到會把系統推向全開或全關，中間的設定點很難維持，因此才出現以脈寬調變切換時間的控制方式。以光控制的 Corynebacterium glutamicum 發酵已有報告，幾丁寡糖產量達 6.2 g/L。蛋白質工程這一側也有進展：Nature Methods 發表 Design and optimization of a kinase-controlled allosteric switch（2026 年 7 月 21 日，Cao 與 Toettcher），先前也發表過 ProDomino——一個僅從序列預測結構域插入位點的機器學習模型，用來加速光與藥物觸發型蛋白質開關的設計；Nature Biotechnology 發表了可光活化的 A-to-I RNA 鹼基編輯器，用於體內基因治療；Advanced Science（2026）則回報在酵母中工程化出具自我維持輸出的光遺傳學電路。一個令人意外的空缺，我直接查證過：在 PubMed 以 optogenetics 加 Bacillus subtilis 搜尋，所有年份合計只有十二筆紀錄，其中奠基性的工作是從藍綠菌移植過來的 CcaS/CcaR 綠—紅光系統。目前沒有任何已發表的光控 B. subtilis 生物反應器，也沒有任何已發表的、以光遺傳學控制 Bacillus 生物防治或促進植物生長功能的研究。","whyItMatters":"Closed-loop optogenetics is the clearest instance of control theory entering the wet lab, and it requires exactly the hybrid skill set - modelling, instrumentation, microbiology - that distinguishes a serious institution from a teaching lab. More importantly, the Bacillus intersection is genuine white space: a twelve-paper literature in a workhorse industrial and agricultural organism is an opportunity, not a warning, and it is directly where GEMS's 2026 project already sits.","whyItMatters_zh":"閉環光遺傳學是控制理論進入濕式實驗室最清楚的例子，而它需要的正是那種混合技能組合——建模、儀器、微生物學——這也是認真的研究機構與一般教學實驗室的分野。更重要的是，Bacillus 這個交集是真正的空白地帶：一個工業與農業上的主力菌種只有十二篇文獻，這是機會而非警訊，而 GEMS 2026 年的專案剛好就落在這裡。","gemsAction":"Commit to the gap: make 'optogenetic control in Bacillus subtilis' a multi-year institutional line, starting by porting and properly characterising a CcaS/CcaR or LOV-based light-inducible cassette in B. subtilis with full dose-response and growth-stage characterisation - that alone is a publishable contribution to a twelve-paper field. Build or buy an LEMOS-style LED microplate (the design is published and cheap) so GEMS owns closed-loop capability rather than open-loop induction, and implement a simple PI or model-predictive controller as a joint dry-lab/wet-lab student project. Then connect it to the plant-protection application by putting a biocontrol-relevant output, not a fluorescent reporter, under light control.","gemsAction_zh":"就投入這個空缺：把「Bacillus subtilis 的光遺傳學控制」設為跨年度的機構主軸，起步工作是把 CcaS/CcaR 或 LOV 為基礎的光誘導卡匣移植到 B. subtilis 並做完整的劑量反應與生長階段特性分析——光是這一步，對一個只有十二篇文獻的領域就已經是可發表的貢獻。自製或購置一塊 LEMOS 式的 LED 微量盤（設計已公開且便宜），讓 GEMS 擁有閉環能力而不只是開環誘導，並以乾濕實驗室合作的學生專案形式實作一個簡單的 PI 或模型預測控制器。接著把它接到植物保護應用上：放在光控之下的，要是與生物防治相關的輸出，而不是螢光報導蛋白。","maturity":"emerging","refs":[{"title":"Design and optimization of a kinase-controlled allosteric switch","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41592-026-03163-1","venue":"Nature Methods","year":2026},{"title":"Rational engineering of allosteric protein switches by in silico prediction of domain insertion sites (ProDomino)","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41592-025-02741-z","venue":"Nature Methods","year":2025},{"title":"Building real-time control for engineered biological systems","url":"https://phys.org/news/2026-08-real-biological.html","venue":"Phys.org reporting on Trends in Biotechnology","year":2026},{"title":"Engineered Optogenetic Circuits In Yeast with Self-Sustained Outputs","url":"https://advanced.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/advs.75865","venue":"Advanced Science","year":2026},{"title":"Switching-time bioprocess control with pulse-width-modulated optogenetics","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2511.22893","venue":"arXiv preprint","year":2025},{"title":"Optogenetic control of Bacillus subtilis gene expression (CcaS/CcaR green-light system)","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/334464808_Optogenetic_control_of_Bacillus_subtilis_gene_expression","venue":"ACS Synthetic Biology (foundational)","year":2019},{"title":"Engineering a photoactivatable A-to-I RNA base editor for gene therapy in vivo","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41587-025-02610-2","venue":"Nature Biotechnology","year":2025}]},{"id":"agri-synbio-living-infrastructure","title":"Agricultural synthetic biology hit the deployment wall, and the blocker is market and acceptance, not science","title_zh":"農業合成生物學撞上了落地的牆，而阻礙來自市場與社會接受度，不是科學","oneLine":"A Nature Biotechnology assessment of 77 agricultural biotechnologies found that market viability and social acceptance, not technological readiness, are the binding constraints - while engineered nitrogen-fixers entered real field trials.","oneLine_zh":"Nature Biotechnology 對 77 項農業生物技術的評估發現，真正的限制是市場可行性與社會接受度，而不是技術成熟度——同時，工程化的固氮菌已進入真正的田間試驗。","body":"Deployability of biotechnologies for environmentally resilient agriculture (Nature Biotechnology Perspective, 10 November 2026, Mishra, Lui and Arkin) is the most strategically useful paper of the year for anyone building an agricultural synbio programme. It applies a Balanced Readiness Level assessment across technological, market, regulatory, acceptance and organisational dimensions to 77 biotechnologies in eight domains (crops, soils, livestock, watersheds, aquaculture, health and security, food loss and waste, frontiers) and concludes that market viability and social acceptance - not technological readiness - are the primary constraints. The high-readiness technologies share a profile: drop-in, contained, transient and perceived as natural. The authors name GMO containment as a concrete lever and set out a roadmap toward 'living infrastructure' - predictively designed multicomponent biological communities functioning at the ecosystem level - backed by a Fermi analysis of microbial fertilizers. The field evidence matches: Nature news (November 2026) reported a Nature Biotechnology comment arguing engineered bacteria could eventually displace up to half of synthetic fertilizer while requiring multi-species cooperation and more rigorous field trials, and noted that Brazil approved a transgenic bacterium for field testing for the first time; Switch Bioworks has permits and multi-state US corn trials with switchable nitrogen-fixing microbes, targeting a deliberately modest 25 percent nitrogen replacement. Plant-side tools advanced too: a modular extracellular contractile injection system repurposed from a bacterial nanomachine for receptor-mediated protein delivery into plant cells (Nature Nanotechnology, 18 November 2026, Legendre, Muchenje and Demirer); a synthetic gibberellin receptor giving spatiotemporal control of GA signalling in roots (Nature Plants, 22 October 2026); a modular high-throughput Chlamydomonas chloroplast engineering platform (Nature Plants, 2025); and Genome synthesis in plants (Nature Reviews Bioengineering, 2025). Containment research is advancing in step - a bioRxiv preprint from Nyerges and colleagues reports a firewalled synthetic commensal that blocks horizontal gene transfer in the gut.","body_zh":"Deployability of biotechnologies for environmentally resilient agriculture（Nature Biotechnology Perspective，2026 年 11 月 10 日，Mishra、Lui 與 Arkin）是今年對任何要建立農業合成生物學計畫的人而言，策略上最有用的一篇論文。它以平衡成熟度等級（Balanced Readiness Level）評估，橫跨技術、市場、法規、接受度與組織五個面向，評估八個領域（作物、土壤、畜產、流域、水產養殖、健康與安全、食物損耗與浪費、前沿）共 77 項生物技術，結論是主要限制在於市場可行性與社會接受度，而非技術成熟度。成熟度高的技術有共同特徵：可直接替換導入、受到圍阻、作用為暫時性，而且在觀感上被認為是天然的。作者指出基改生物的圍阻是一個具體的槓桿，並提出通往「活體基礎設施」的路線圖——可預測性設計、在生態系層級運作的多元件生物群落——並以微生物肥料的費米估算作為支持。田間證據也相符：Nature 新聞（2026 年 11 月）報導 Nature Biotechnology 的一篇評論，主張工程化細菌最終可能替代最多一半的合成肥料，但需要多物種協作與更嚴謹的田間試驗，並指出巴西首度核准一株基因轉殖細菌進行田間測試；Switch Bioworks 已取得許可，並在美國多州以可切換的固氮微生物進行玉米試驗，刻意把目標訂在較保守的 25% 氮肥替代。植物端的工具也有進展：把細菌奈米機械改造成模組化的胞外收縮型注射系統，以受體媒介方式把蛋白質送入植物細胞（Nature Nanotechnology，2026 年 11 月 18 日，Legendre、Muchenje 與 Demirer）；一個人工合成的激勃素受體，可對根部的 GA 訊息傳遞做時空控制（Nature Plants，2026 年 10 月 22 日）；一個模組化高通量的 Chlamydomonas 葉綠體工程平台（Nature Plants，2025）；以及 Genome synthesis in plants（Nature Reviews Bioengineering，2025）。圍阻研究也同步推進——Nyerges 與同事的一篇 bioRxiv 預印本回報一株設有防火牆的合成共生菌，可在腸道中阻斷水平基因轉移。","whyItMatters":"This reframes what an agricultural synbio project must deliver: not a better strain but a containment story, a cost model and an acceptance argument. For GEMS, whose 2026 project is a Bacillus bioreactor for plant protection, the Arkin framework is effectively a scoring rubric - and the drop-in, contained, transient, perceived-as-natural profile describes a Bacillus biocontrol product almost exactly, which is a strategic advantage worth stating explicitly.","whyItMatters_zh":"這重新定義了一個農業合成生物學專案必須交付什麼：不是更好的菌株，而是一套圍阻說法、一個成本模型與一個社會接受度的論證。對 GEMS 來說——其 2026 年專案是用於植物保護的 Bacillus 生物反應器——Arkin 的框架實質上就是一份評分表，而「可直接替換導入、受到圍阻、暫時性、觀感上天然」這組特徵幾乎完全描述了一個 Bacillus 生物防治產品，這是值得明白說出來的策略優勢。","gemsAction":"Score GEMS's own optogenetic Bacillus plant-protection concept against the Balanced Readiness Level dimensions from the Arkin paper and publish the assessment as part of the project write-up - it costs nothing and immediately distinguishes GEMS from teams that only report titers. Design for containment and transience from the start, since light-dependence is itself a containment mechanism (no light, no function) and that is a genuinely novel argument worth making. Seek a Taiwanese agricultural research partner (an agricultural research institute or university plant-pathology group) for a contained greenhouse trial, because the Arkin analysis says field and acceptance data, not lab data, are what the field is short of.","gemsAction_zh":"拿 Arkin 論文的平衡成熟度等級各面向，為 GEMS 自己的光遺傳學 Bacillus 植物保護構想打分，並把這份評估作為專案報告的一部分發表——它不花一毛錢，卻能立刻把 GEMS 和那些只回報產量的團隊區分開來。從一開始就為圍阻與暫時性而設計，因為光依賴性本身就是一種圍阻機制（沒有光就沒有功能），這是一個真正新穎、值得提出的論點。尋找台灣的農業研究夥伴（農業試驗研究機構或大學植物病理團隊）做一次受圍阻的溫室試驗，因為 Arkin 的分析指出，這個領域缺的是田間與社會接受度的資料，不是實驗室資料。","maturity":"accelerating","refs":[{"title":"Deployability of biotechnologies for environmentally resilient agriculture","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41587-026-03373-0","venue":"Nature Biotechnology (Perspective)","year":2026},{"title":"Engineered bacteria are weaning farms away from synthetic fertilizers","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-026-03641-8","venue":"Nature (News)","year":2026},{"title":"An extracellular contractile injection system for receptor-mediated protein delivery into plant cells","url":"https://www.nature.com/search?q=protein+design&order=date","venue":"Nature Nanotechnology","year":2026},{"title":"Synthetic activation of gibberellin signalling reveals spatial coordination of root growth","url":"https://www.nature.com/search?q=synthetic+biology&order=date","venue":"Nature Plants","year":2026},{"title":"Genome synthesis in plants","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s44222-025-00326-1","venue":"Nature Reviews Bioengineering","year":2025},{"title":"Firewalled synthetic commensal blocks horizontal gene transfer in the gut","url":"https://www.biorxiv.org/content/10.64898/2026.09.17.752456v1","venue":"bioRxiv preprint","year":2026},{"title":"Switch Bioworks tests switchable nitrogen-fixing microbes in corn for fertilizer","url":"https://agfundernews.com/switch-bioworks-tests-switchable-nitrogen-fixing-microbes-in-corn-for-fertilizer","venue":"AgFunderNews","year":2026}]},{"id":"biosecurity-governance-hardening","title":"Biosecurity became a compliance requirement with teeth, and screening itself became a research field","title_zh":"生物安全成為有強制力的法遵要求，而篩查本身也成了一個研究領域","oneLine":"The US tied federal life-science funding to buying DNA only from adherent suppliers, while Nature Communications published algorithms to defend synthesis screening against order-splitting evasion.","oneLine_zh":"美國把聯邦生命科學經費與「只向遵循規範的供應商購買 DNA」綁在一起，Nature Communications 則發表了演算法，防範以拆單規避合成篩查的手法。","body":"Governance moved from voluntary norms to funding conditions. The White House issued NSTM-6 on 5 November 2026 with an attached National Policy for Nucleic Acid Synthesis Screening, replacing the 2024 Framework and, on full implementation, the 2023 HHS Screening Framework Guidance; it conditions federal life-sciences funding on procuring synthetic nucleic acids and benchtop synthesis equipment only from designated Adherent Suppliers, with a phase-in reaching customers in 2027, and it supplements rather than replaces export controls and the Select Agents regulations. The international picture is uneven: order screening is now central policy in the US, EU, New Zealand and UK, but IBBIS data indicate only a small fraction of more than 700 known providers worldwide maintain publicly identifiable screening, and the International Gene Synthesis Consortium remains voluntary. Crucially, screening is now a legitimate and publishable technical research area: Defending synthetic DNA orders against intra-order splitting-based obfuscation (Nature Communications, 28 September 2026, Tayouri-Attia, Kogan and Puzis) tests a Gene Edit Distance algorithm that detects obfuscated orders regardless of fragment length, and Evaluating AI-Assisted Customer Verification for Synthetic Nucleic Acid Screening (bioRxiv, 2026, with Nelson among the authors) studies the legitimacy-screening step - verifying who is ordering and why - as the primary human safeguard. Governance of the AI layer specifically is being worked out in Navigating regulatory fragmentation in the convergence of synthetic biology, artificial intelligence, and automation (Nature Communications Perspective, 29 August 2026, McLennan, Freemont and Pretorius), which analyses national regulations and proposes a SynBioxAI regulatory interoperability toolkit explicitly aimed at giving research institutes the capacity to navigate divergent regimes. Nature also kept the harder questions open with Ting Zhu's Comment on whether mirror-image molecular biology research should be stopped.","body_zh":"治理從自願性規範轉為經費條件。白宮於 2026 年 11 月 5 日發布 NSTM-6，附帶國家核酸合成篩查政策（National Policy for Nucleic Acid Synthesis Screening），取代 2024 年的框架，並在全面實施後取代 2023 年 HHS 的篩查框架指引；該政策規定聯邦生命科學經費以「只向指定的遵循供應商（Adherent Suppliers）採購合成核酸與桌上型合成設備」為條件，分階段實施並於 2027 年擴及客戶端，而且是補充而非取代出口管制與特定生物劑（Select Agents）法規。國際局勢並不平均：訂單篩查已是美國、歐盟、紐西蘭與英國的核心政策，但 IBBIS 的資料顯示，全球 700 多家已知供應商中，只有一小部分維持公開可查的篩查機制，而 International Gene Synthesis Consortium 仍屬自願性組織。關鍵的是，篩查現在是一個正當且可發表的技術研究領域：Defending synthetic DNA orders against intra-order splitting-based obfuscation（Nature Communications，2026 年 9 月 28 日，Tayouri-Attia、Kogan 與 Puzis）測試一個 Gene Edit Distance 演算法，不論片段長度都能偵測被混淆處理的訂單；Evaluating AI-Assisted Customer Verification for Synthetic Nucleic Acid Screening（bioRxiv，2026，作者包含 Nelson）則研究正當性審查這一步——確認是誰在下單、為什麼下單——作為最主要的人為防線。針對 AI 這一層的治理，Navigating regulatory fragmentation in the convergence of synthetic biology, artificial intelligence, and automation（Nature Communications Perspective，2026 年 8 月 29 日，McLennan、Freemont 與 Pretorius）正在處理，該文分析各國法規，並提出一套 SynBioxAI 法規互通性工具包，明確目的就是讓研究機構有能力應付彼此歧異的管制體制。Nature 也以 Ting Zhu 的評論保留了更難的問題：鏡像分子生物學研究是否應該停止。","whyItMatters":"An institution that trains students and orders DNA now has concrete obligations - supplier choice, order documentation, institutional review - and partners and funders will begin asking about them, especially for a cross-border collaboration from Taiwan into US or EU networks. Equally important, the SynBioxAI paper exists because institutes are the unit that has to comply, so this is an area where modest, early effort buys disproportionate credibility.","whyItMatters_zh":"一個會訓練學生、也會訂購 DNA 的機構，現在有了具體義務——供應商選擇、訂單文件、機構內部審查——而合作夥伴與出資方將開始追問這些事項，對於從台灣跨境接入美國或歐盟網絡的合作尤其如此。同樣重要的是，SynBioxAI 這篇論文之所以存在，正是因為需要遵循規範的單位就是研究機構，所以這是一個只要早一點付出不多的努力，就能換到不成比例信譽的領域。","gemsAction":"Within 12 months write and publish a short GEMS biosecurity and biosafety policy covering three things: ordering synthetic DNA only from IGSC-member or adherent suppliers, a documented internal review step for any sequence design work, and an explicit scope statement excluding pathogen and toxin sequences - then use the SynBioxAI toolkit framing to structure it. Teach screening as curriculum, not compliance: the Gene Edit Distance paper is an outstanding student exercise in sequence similarity and adversarial thinking that builds real bioinformatics skill. Nominate one staff member as biosecurity point of contact, because collaboration agreements will increasingly require a named person.","gemsAction_zh":"在 12 個月內寫出並公開一份簡短的 GEMS 生物安全政策（涵蓋 biosecurity 與 biosafety），內容包含三件事：只向 IGSC 會員或遵循規範的供應商訂購合成 DNA；任何序列設計工作都有一道有記錄的內部審查程序；以及一份明確排除病原體與毒素序列的範圍聲明——並用 SynBioxAI 工具包的框架來組織它。把篩查當成課程而不是法遵來教：Gene Edit Distance 那篇論文是極佳的學生習題，既練序列相似度，也練對抗性思考，能培養真正的生物資訊能力。指派一位同仁擔任生物安全聯絡人，因為合作協議將愈來愈要求有一位具名負責人。","maturity":"accelerating","refs":[{"title":"Defending synthetic DNA orders against intra-order splitting-based obfuscation","url":"https://www.nature.com/search?q=synthetic+biology&order=date","venue":"Nature Communications","year":2026},{"title":"Navigating regulatory fragmentation in the convergence of synthetic biology, artificial intelligence, and automation (SynBioxAI toolkit)","url":"https://www.nature.com/search?q=synthetic+biology&order=date","venue":"Nature Communications (Perspective)","year":2026},{"title":"National Policy for Nucleic Acid Synthesis Screening (NSTM-6)","url":"https://www.whitehouse.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/NSTM-6-NASS-Policy.pdf","venue":"US White House / OSTP","year":2026},{"title":"Evaluating AI-Assisted Customer Verification for Synthetic Nucleic Acid Screening","url":"https://www.biorxiv.org/content/10.64898/2026.02.27.708645v2","venue":"bioRxiv preprint","year":2026},{"title":"Compounding Asymmetries in Nucleic Acid Synthesis Screening","url":"https://www.rand.org/pubs/external_publications/EP71386.html","venue":"RAND","year":2026},{"title":"Mirror of the unknown: should research on mirror-image molecular biology be stopped?","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-025-02912-0","venue":"Nature (Comment)","year":2025}]},{"id":"standards-fair-and-access","title":"Standards, FAIR data and equitable access became the field's self-identified weak link","title_zh":"標準、FAIR 資料與公平取用成為這個領域自己認定的弱點","oneLine":"Synthetic biology is confronting the fact that its data are not machine-readable enough to train the models it now depends on, while a parallel movement works on who gets to participate at all.","oneLine_zh":"合成生物學正面對一個事實：它的資料機器可讀性不足，無法訓練它現在所依賴的模型；同時另一股並行的運動則在處理「究竟誰有資格參與」的問題。","body":"The dependency is explicit: ML-guided DBTL and foundation models need consistent, annotated, cross-site data, and synthetic biology does not reliably produce it. A January 2026 ACS Synthetic Biology paper by Vitalis, Myers and colleagues proposes a standards-enabled FAIR data management workflow spanning the actual data types labs generate - sequences, models, protocols, images and time-series measurements. The SBOL ecosystem is modernising around SBOL3's fully graph-based, JSON-LD-aligned data model, with a 2026 Journal of Integrative Bioinformatics paper describing an SBOL converter that minimises data loss across versions, and a decade-review of SBOL Visual documenting growing adoption of the diagram standard. A 2026 FEMS Yeast Research review of high-throughput yeast engineering in biofoundries argues directly that alignment on QC thresholds, metadata standards and FAIR principles is now necessary for machine learning and cross-site validation. The access strand is equally substantive and more immediately relevant to a growing institution: Reclone, the Reagent Collaboration Network (Nature Methods Comment, 22 June 2026, Molloy, Federici and Rosca), builds regional distribution hubs and nodes for open sharing of biomaterials, protocols and knowledge to address the global R&D asymmetry; Nature Biotechnology ran Expanding global access to synthetic biology (12 October 2026, Karki and GC) on cost, logistics, local expertise and educator motivation; and Nature Communications previously published the frugal CRISPRkit, a smartphone-quantified CRISPR education kit explicitly designed so high-school students can do gene editing affordably and safely. Scientific Reports published A simplified modelling protocol for synthetic biology (16 September 2026, Alvarez, Turjanski and Sanchez), which is the methodological counterpart - lowering the barrier to doing the modelling at all. What is still missing, and I could not find 2026 work on it, is measurement metrology: calibrated, unit-bearing reporter measurements comparable across labs.","body_zh":"這個依賴關係很明確：機器學習導引的 DBTL 與基礎模型需要一致、有標註、跨機構可比的資料，而合成生物學並不能穩定地產出這種資料。2026 年 1 月 ACS Synthetic Biology 上，Vitalis、Myers 與同事提出一套以標準為基礎的 FAIR 資料管理工作流程，涵蓋實驗室真正會產生的資料型別——序列、模型、實驗流程、影像與時間序列量測。SBOL 生態系正圍繞 SBOL3 全圖形化、對齊 JSON-LD 的資料模型現代化，2026 年 Journal of Integrative Bioinformatics 的一篇論文描述了一個能把跨版本資料損失降到最低的 SBOL 轉換器，另有一篇 SBOL Visual 的十年回顧，記錄了這套圖示標準日漸普及。2026 年 FEMS Yeast Research 一篇關於生物鑄造廠中高通量酵母工程的綜述直接主張，要做機器學習與跨機構驗證，就必須先在品管閾值、詮釋資料標準與 FAIR 原則上取得一致。取用這條線同樣紮實，對一所成長中的機構更是立即相關：Reclone，即試劑協作網路（Nature Methods Comment，2026 年 6 月 22 日，Molloy、Federici 與 Rosca），建立區域性的配送樞紐與節點，以開放方式分享生物材料、實驗流程與知識，針對的是全球研發的不對稱；Nature Biotechnology 刊出 Expanding global access to synthetic biology（2026 年 10 月 12 日，Karki 與 GC），討論成本、物流、在地專業與教育者的動機；Nature Communications 先前也發表過節約型的 CRISPRkit，一套以智慧型手機定量的 CRISPR 教學套件，明確設計成讓高中生能以可負擔且安全的方式進行基因編輯。Scientific Reports 發表 A simplified modelling protocol for synthetic biology（2026 年 9 月 16 日，Alvarez、Turjanski 與 Sanchez），這是方法層面的對應——把「有沒有辦法開始做建模」的門檻降下來。仍然缺席、而我在 2026 年也找不到相關工作的，是量測計量學：經過校準、帶有單位、可跨實驗室比較的報導基因量測。","whyItMatters":"Standards are the one trend where a small, new institution can be ahead rather than behind, because adopting SBOL3 and FAIR practice from scratch is far easier than retrofitting a thirty-year-old lab. It is also the route into the field's social infrastructure - Reclone and the access literature are actively looking for nodes and contributors outside the usual centres, and a Taiwanese institution with a strong school programme is a natural fit.","whyItMatters_zh":"標準是唯一一項小而新的機構可以領先而非落後的趨勢，因為從零開始採用 SBOL3 與 FAIR 實務，遠比替一個三十年歷史的實驗室改裝容易。它也是進入這個領域社會性基礎設施的途徑——Reclone 與取用相關的文獻正積極尋找傳統中心之外的節點與貢獻者，而一所有紮實學校課程的台灣機構天然就很合適。","gemsAction":"Adopt SBOL3 and a FAIR data layout as GEMS's native format now, before there is legacy data to migrate: every student construct gets a machine-readable record, every assay gets structured metadata, and the whole thing lives in a versioned repository. Fix the metrology gap locally by calibrating all fluorescence measurements to absolute units (fluorescein or MEFL equivalents) so GEMS data are comparable with other labs - a cheap, concrete practice that very few teaching institutions follow. Apply to become a Reclone node or hub for Taiwan and East Asia, which converts GEMS's educational mission into international standing at close to zero marginal cost.","gemsAction_zh":"現在就把 SBOL3 與 FAIR 資料佈局採用為 GEMS 的原生格式，趁還沒有舊資料需要遷移：每個學生構築體都有一筆機器可讀的紀錄，每項檢測都有結構化詮釋資料，整體存放在有版本控制的儲存庫中。在自家範圍內補上計量學缺口：把所有螢光量測校準到絕對單位（fluorescein 或 MEFL 等效值），讓 GEMS 的資料能與其他實驗室比較——這是一項便宜又具體的做法，而極少有教學機構真的在做。申請成為 Reclone 在台灣與東亞的節點或樞紐，這能以近乎零的邊際成本，把 GEMS 的教育使命轉換成國際地位。","maturity":"mainstream","refs":[{"title":"Reclone: a global research community building equitable access to reagents","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41592-026-03148-0","venue":"Nature Methods (Comment)","year":2026},{"title":"A Framework for a Standard-Enabled FAIR Data Management Workflow for Synthetic Biology","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41498158/","venue":"ACS Synthetic Biology","year":2026},{"title":"SBOL converter: enabling backward compatibility for biological designs","url":"https://doi.org/10.1515/jib-2026-0005","venue":"Journal of Integrative Bioinformatics","year":2026},{"title":"Expanding global access to synthetic biology","url":"https://www.nature.com/search?q=synthetic+biology&order=date","venue":"Nature Biotechnology (Comment)","year":2026},{"title":"A simplified modelling protocol for synthetic biology","url":"https://www.nature.com/search?q=synthetic+biology&order=date","venue":"Scientific Reports","year":2026},{"title":"A frugal CRISPR kit for equitable and accessible education in gene editing and synthetic biology","url":"https://www.nature.com/search?q=synthetic+biology&order=date","venue":"Nature Communications","year":2024},{"title":"High-throughput yeast engineering in biofoundries: towards autonomous and scalable synthetic biology","url":"https://academic.oup.com/femsyr/article/doi/10.1093/femsyr/foag003/8442238?login=false","venue":"FEMS Yeast Research","year":2026}]}],"readingList":[{"title":"Towards the construction of a virtual yeast","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-026-10574-9","venue":"Nature (Perspective)","year":2026,"why":"The clearest blueprint anywhere for what a dry-lab-first microbial research programme looks like - eight AI modules under an LLM orchestration layer in a closed experimental loop.","why_zh":"目前最清楚的藍圖，說明一個以乾式實驗室為先的微生物研究計畫長什麼樣子——在閉環實驗迴路中，由一個 LLM 協調層統整八個 AI 模組。"},{"title":"Deployability of biotechnologies for environmentally resilient agriculture","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41587-026-03373-0","venue":"Nature Biotechnology (Perspective)","year":2026,"why":"Scores 77 agricultural biotechnologies and shows the blocker is market and acceptance, not science - effectively a rubric for GEMS's own plant-protection project.","why_zh":"為 77 項農業生物技術打分，顯示阻礙來自市場與社會接受度，而非科學——實質上就是 GEMS 自己植物保護專案的評分準則。"},{"title":"Artificial allosteric protein switches with machine-learning-designed receptors","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41587-026-03081-9","venue":"Nature Biotechnology","year":2026,"why":"The single most directly actionable paper for GEMS: ML-designed receptors driving colorimetric, luminescent and electrochemical sensors plus YES/AND logic.","why_zh":"對 GEMS 而言最直接可以動手的一篇論文：機器學習設計的受體驅動比色、發光與電化學感測器，並實作 YES/AND 邏輯。"},{"title":"Programmable design of functional proteins from natural language (Pinal)","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-026-11205-z","venue":"Nature","year":2026,"why":"16B-parameter model turning written functional descriptions into experimentally validated enzymes - the clearest sign of where the design interface is heading.","why_zh":"160 億參數的模型，把書面的功能描述變成經實驗驗證的酵素——最清楚地指出設計介面正往哪裡走。"},{"title":"Digital cell factories for biomanufacturing","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s44222-026-00506-7","venue":"Nature Reviews Bioengineering (Comment)","year":2026,"why":"Nielsen's argument for optimising predicted production and economics over biological realism - a short, strategic read that reframes what modelling is for.","why_zh":"Nielsen 主張最佳化的對象應該是預測的產量與經濟性，而非生物真實性——一篇篇幅短但具策略性的讀物，重新界定建模究竟是為了什麼。"},{"title":"Automated prototyping of genetic codes","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-026-10949-y","venue":"Nature","year":2026,"why":"Church-lab robotic cell-free platform that prototypes redesigned genetic codes without touching a living genome - the template for fast, low-biosafety-burden iteration.","why_zh":"Church 實驗室的機器人化無細胞平台，能在完全不動活體基因組的情況下試做重新設計的遺傳密碼——快速迭代且生物安全負擔低的範本。"},{"title":"Generative genome design with DNA language models","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41576-026-01032-3","venue":"Nature Reviews Genetics (Tools of the Trade)","year":2026,"why":"Short practitioner account of designing, synthesising and validating AI-written phage genomes - the best entry point to genome-scale generative design.","why_zh":"一篇簡短的實作者敘述，說明如何設計、合成並驗證由 AI 撰寫的噬菌體基因組——進入基因組尺度生成式設計的最佳入門。"},{"title":"Toward autonomous science with agentic artificial intelligence","url":"https://www.cell.com/cell/fulltext/S0092-8674(26)01063-9?rss=yes","venue":"Cell (Review)","year":2026,"why":"Taxonomy of the three agent paradigms (Co-Scientist, Robin, Biomni) with their validated results and limits - saves reading a dozen preprints.","why_zh":"把三種代理範式（Co-Scientist、Robin、Biomni）分類整理，附上各自已驗證的成果與限制——省下讀十來篇預印本的工夫。"},{"title":"Reclone: a global research community building equitable access to reagents","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41592-026-03148-0","venue":"Nature Methods (Comment)","year":2026,"why":"The concrete mechanism by which a growing institution outside the traditional centres joins global synthetic biology infrastructure.","why_zh":"一所位於傳統中心之外、正在成長的機構，接入全球合成生物學基礎設施的具體機制。"},{"title":"Automation and machine learning drive rapid optimization of isoprenol production in Pseudomonas putida","url":"https://consensus.app/papers/details/w:b89d3c61-1875-424b-bc8a-f2eb8872c5fc/","venue":"Nature Communications","year":2025,"why":"The benchmark ML-DBTL result with real numbers: 5-fold titer in six cycles, 800,000 designs narrowed to about 400 - the evidence base for the dry-lab-as-engine thesis.","why_zh":"機器學習 DBTL 的標竿結果，帶著真實數字：六個循環把產量提高 5 倍，80 萬個設計縮減到約 400 個——「乾式實驗室即引擎」這個論點的證據基礎。"},{"title":"De novo design of synthetic microbial genomes","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s44222-026-00410-0","venue":"Nature Reviews Bioengineering","year":2026,"why":"Pairs the rational-design and computational routes to synthetic genomes, so students see generative models in the context of decades of genome engineering.","why_zh":"把通往合成基因組的理性設計路線與計算路線並置，讓學生在數十年基因組工程的脈絡中看待生成式模型。"},{"title":"Ultra-high-throughput mapping of genetic design space (CLASSIC)","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-025-09933-9","venue":"Nature","year":2026,"why":"Shows that long-read multiplexed measurement, not construct count, is what converts a library into usable design rules.","why_zh":"說明把函式庫轉換成可用設計規則的是長讀長多重量測，而不是構築體的數量。"}],"openQuestions":["Can light-dependence serve as a genuine biological containment mechanism? Nobody has quantified the escape rate of an organism whose essential or payload function requires illumination. A student team could measure how often a light-dependent Bacillus strain regains constitutive function under selection - a contained, cheap, publishable experiment that speaks directly to the containment lever the Arkin deployability paper identifies as decisive.","What is the real-world success rate of generative binder design in a modest lab? Published rates swing from under 10 percent (Nipah G competition) to a 46.3 percent mean (BindCraft), and almost all come from the groups that built the tools. An independent, honestly reported hit rate from 20 designs against one well-assayed target - including the failures - would be genuinely useful to the field and is well within a student team's reach.","Do co-folding models' affinity predictions survive contact with a real titration? Boltz-2 bundles binding-affinity prediction with structure, but its calibration on non-drug-like, engineering-relevant targets (plant metabolites, agrochemicals, small-molecule inducers) is untested. Comparing predicted versus measured affinity for a handful of inducer-receptor pairs would probe where the interpolation breaks down.","Why does optogenetic control have such steep dose-response in practice, and can growth-stage-aware models fix it? The pulse-width-modulation and GEAGS work exists precisely because intermediate setpoints are hard to hold, but there is no systematic characterisation in Bacillus at all. Mapping light intensity, duty cycle and growth phase against expression in B. subtilis would fill a twelve-paper literature's largest hole.","Can engineered microbial consortia be made to hold a designed composition outside a bioreactor? The Nature Biotechnology fertilizer comment names multi-species cooperation as the unsolved requirement, and 2026 reviews report that rhizosphere engineering remains inconsistent in the field despite successful colonisation. Tracking a two- or three-member designed community's composition over weeks in non-sterile soil, with and without an external control input, is a tractable ecology-meets-engineering question."],"openQuestions_zh":["光依賴性能否作為真正的生物圍阻機制？目前沒有人量化過一株「必要功能或酬載功能需要照光」的生物體的逃脫率。一支學生團隊可以測量在選汰壓力下，一株光依賴的 Bacillus 菌株多久會重新取得組成型的功能——這是一個受圍阻、便宜、而且可發表的實驗，也直接回應 Arkin 那篇可部署性論文所指出的決定性圍阻槓桿。","在一間規模普通的實驗室裡，生成式結合蛋白設計的真實成功率是多少？已發表的數字從低於 10%（Nipah G 競賽）到平均 46.3%（BindCraft）不等，而且幾乎全部來自開發這些工具的團隊。針對一個檢測方法成熟的標的做 20 個設計，獨立且誠實地回報命中率——包含失敗的那些——對整個領域都會很有用，而這完全在一支學生團隊的能力範圍內。","共摺疊模型的親和力預測，禁得起真實滴定實驗的檢驗嗎？Boltz-2 把結合親和力預測和結構預測打包在一起，但它在非類藥、具工程意義的標的（植物代謝物、農用化學品、小分子誘導物）上的校準尚未受檢驗。針對少數幾組誘導物—受體配對比較預測與實測的親和力，可以探出這種內插在哪裡失效。","為什麼光遺傳學控制在實務上的劑量反應如此陡峭，而考慮生長階段的模型能否解決這個問題？脈寬調變與 GEAGS 之類的工作之所以存在，正是因為中間的設定點難以維持，但在 Bacillus 上完全沒有系統性的特性分析。把光強度、工作週期與生長時期對 B. subtilis 表現量的影響繪製成圖譜，就能填上這個只有十二篇文獻的領域最大的一個洞。","工程化的微生物群落，能否在生物反應器之外維持設計好的組成？Nature Biotechnology 那篇肥料評論指出多物種協作是尚未解決的必要條件，而 2026 年的多篇綜述也回報，即使移生成功，根圈工程在田間仍然不穩定。在非無菌土壤中追蹤一個兩至三成員的設計群落數週內的組成變化，並比較有無外部控制輸入的差別，是一個可以著手的生態學與工程交會的問題。"]},"industry":{"updated":"2026-11-19","sourcesRead":["https://www.synbiobeta.com/","https://www.synbiobeta.com/read","https://www.synbiobeta.com/news","https://www.synbiobeta.com/insights","https://www.synbiobeta.com/categories/ai-digital-biology","https://www.synbiobeta.com/categories/bioeconomy-policy","https://www.synbiobeta.com/categories/biosecurity-bioethics","https://www.synbiobeta.com/categories/reading-writing-and-editing-dna","https://www.synbiobeta.com/read/latent-y-automates-antibody-design-work-that-slows-down-early-drug-development","https://www.synbiobeta.com/read/the-protein-design-boom-is-moving-beyond-pharma.-quercus-raised-5m-with-the-conviction-that-weeds-are-next","https://www.synbiobeta.com/read/biosphere-lands-21m-from-the-department-of-war-to-build-a-bioreactor-cleaned-with-light","https://www.synbiobeta.com/read/usda-greenlights-the-first-engineered-microbe-that-makes-antibodies-in-the-gut","https://www.synbiobeta.com/read/potato-just-launched-the-tool-it-wishes-it-had-as-a-lab-scientist","https://www.synbiobeta.com/read/one-model-every-microbiome","https://www.synbiobeta.com/read/cemvita-and-roebling-want-to-kill-the-expensive-surprise-in-industrial-biotech","https://www.synbiobeta.com/read/china-s-bioeconomy-is-brewing-its-biggest-wave-yet","https://www.synbiobeta.com/read/anthropic-is-hiring-biologists-building-wet-labs-and-betting-big-on-drug-discovery","https://www.synbiobeta.com/read/ginkgo-joins-genesis-project-to-build-a-47-million-autonomous-robot-lab"],"sourcesBlocked":["https://www.synbiobeta.com/topics/ai-digital-biology (returns 404 - the live taxonomy is /categories/*, not /topics/*)","https://www.synbiobeta.com/topics/biomanufacturing-scale-up (returns 404 - same reason)","NOTE: no site actively blocked curl. All non-SynBioBeta facts below come from WebSearch result snippets rather than pages I rendered myself, and are flagged where the underlying sources conflict. Numbers attributed to PitchBook, Dealroom, newmarketpitch.com, CompBioJobs and similar aggregators are secondary and should be re-verified against primary filings before publication."],"trends":[{"id":"ai-protein-design-wave","title":"The AI protein-design wave has its own capital market now, and it is spilling out of pharma","title_zh":"AI 蛋白質設計這一波已經有了自己的資本市場，而且正溢出製藥領域","oneLine":"De novo protein design went from a 2023 proof of concept to a funded product category in 2026, with Chai Discovery at a $3.8B valuation and design agents being sold to biologists who cannot code.","oneLine_zh":"從頭蛋白質設計從 2023 年的概念驗證，到 2026 年已成為一個有資金挹注的產品類別：Chai Discovery 估值 38 億美元，而設計代理正賣給不會寫程式的生物學家。","body":"Chai Discovery closed a $400M Series C in July 2026 at a reported $3.8B valuation, roughly 25x its September 2024 seed valuation, bringing it to about $630M raised across four rounds. Below that tier, 2026 produced a steady drumbeat of design rounds: BigHat Biosciences took a $75M Series C in September ($223M total), MoleculeMind in China reported a Series A over $100M in June backed by Cathay Biotech, Galux in South Korea closed a $29M Series B (KRW 42bn, $47M total), Scala Biodesign in Israel raised $16M led by Grove Ventures, and Lithuania's Biomatter closed an $18M Series A led by Astanor on 12 November for AI enzyme design with a Vilnius facility planned for 2027. The product is shifting from models to agents: Latent Labs released Latent-Y in October 2026, which it calls the first lab-validated drug design agent, built on its Latent-X2 frontier model for antibody and peptide design, and claims a 56x faster computational antibody workflow versus expert protein designers, with ~4,300x on literature and PDB structure review and ~350x on epitope selection (company technical-report figures, unverified by SynBioBeta). UC Davis's Yarov-Yarovoy lab used the Latent Labs platform to design nanobodies against a human ion channel, with four of five designs inhibiting current and the best at 30 nM IC50 in the first round without optimisation. At SynBioBeta 2026, Xaira CEO Marc Tessier-Lavigne dated the inflection to Baker-lab de novo design in 2023 and said companies can now generate high-affinity antibodies against large fractions of tested targets, while explicitly rejecting one-button drug design. The spillover is the newest part: Quercus Biosolutions raised a $5M seed led by Serra Ventures in July 2026 to design mini-protein binders against herbicide targets, in a crop-protection market where 21 of 31 known sites of action are already compromised by resistance and a new product averages 11+ years and ~$307M (AgbioInvestor for CropLife International, 2026).","body_zh":"Chai Discovery 於 2026 年 7 月完成 4 億美元 C 輪，據報估值 38 億美元，約為 2024 年 9 月種子輪估值的 25 倍，四輪合計募得約 6.3 億美元。在這一層之下，2026 年設計類募資接連不斷：BigHat Biosciences 於 9 月取得 7,500 萬美元 C 輪（累計 2.23 億美元）；中國的 MoleculeMind 於 6 月回報由凱賽生物（Cathay Biotech）支持、金額逾 1 億美元的 A 輪；南韓的 Galux 完成 2,900 萬美元 B 輪（420 億韓元，累計 4,700 萬美元）；以色列的 Scala Biodesign 由 Grove Ventures 領投募得 1,600 萬美元；立陶宛的 Biomatter 則於 11 月 12 日完成由 Astanor 領投的 1,800 萬美元 A 輪，投入 AI 酵素設計，並計畫 2027 年在維爾紐斯設廠。產品形態正從模型轉向代理：Latent Labs 於 2026 年 10 月推出 Latent-Y，自稱是第一個經實驗室驗證的藥物設計代理，建立在其抗體與胜肽設計的前沿模型 Latent-X2 之上，並聲稱運算型抗體工作流程比專家級蛋白質設計師快 56 倍，在文獻與 PDB 結構審閱上約快 4,300 倍、在表位選擇上約快 350 倍（公司技術報告數字，SynBioBeta 未經查證）。UC Davis 的 Yarov-Yarovoy 實驗室用 Latent Labs 平台設計針對一個人類離子通道的奈米抗體，五個設計中有四個能抑制電流，最佳者在第一輪未經最佳化就達到 30 nM 的 IC50。在 SynBioBeta 2026 上，Xaira 執行長 Marc Tessier-Lavigne 把轉折點定在 2023 年 Baker 實驗室的從頭設計，並表示公司現在能對受測標的中相當大的比例產生高親和力抗體，但他明確否認所謂一鍵式藥物設計。溢出效應是最新的一塊：Quercus Biosolutions 於 2026 年 7 月完成由 Serra Ventures 領投的 500 萬美元種子輪，設計針對除草劑標的的迷你蛋白結合子；而在作物保護這個市場中，31 個已知作用位點已有 21 個因抗藥性而失效，一個新產品平均要花 11 年以上與約 3.07 億美元（AgbioInvestor 為 CropLife International 製作，2026）。","whyItMatters":"The scarce skill in this wave is no longer model training, it is knowing which target to point a design agent at and how to judge whether its output is real. That is exactly the judgement a research institution teaches, and it is now the rate-limiting input to a multi-billion-dollar industry. It also means a small lab with no GPU cluster can do credible design work through a web interface.","whyItMatters_zh":"這一波真正稀缺的能力已不是訓練模型，而是知道該把設計代理指向哪個標的，以及如何判斷它的輸出是不是真的。這正是研究機構所教的判斷力，而它現在成了一個數十億美元產業的限速輸入。這也意味著一間沒有 GPU 叢集的小實驗室，透過網頁介面就能做出可信的設計工作。","gemsAction":"Stand up a design-and-validate module in which students take a defined target, run binder design through a hosted platform (Latent Labs' web interface, Cradle, or open ESM/RFdiffusion-class tooling), and then measure something: binding, inhibition, or expression. Insist every design project ends in a wet-lab number, because the market premium in 2026 is on people who can falsify a model's output, not generate more of it. Approach one Taiwan or Asia-Pacific academic protein-design group as a validation partner so GEMS students can send designs somewhere that will test them.","gemsAction_zh":"建立一個設計與驗證模組：讓學生選定一個標的，透過託管平台（Latent Labs 的網頁介面、Cradle，或 ESM/RFdiffusion 這一類開放工具）跑結合子設計，然後實際量測某個東西——結合、抑制或表現量。堅持每個設計專案都要以一個濕式實驗室的數字收尾，因為 2026 年市場加價的對象是能夠推翻模型輸出的人，而不是能生成更多輸出的人。接洽一個台灣或亞太的學術蛋白質設計團隊作為驗證夥伴，讓 GEMS 的學生有地方把設計送去實測。","maturity":"accelerating","refs":[{"title":"Latent-Y Automates Antibody Design Work that Slows Down Early Drug Development","url":"https://www.synbiobeta.com/read/latent-y-automates-antibody-design-work-that-slows-down-early-drug-development","outlet":"SynBioBeta","date":"2026-10-21"},{"title":"The protein design boom is moving beyond pharma. Quercus raised $5M with the conviction that weeds are next","url":"https://www.synbiobeta.com/read/the-protein-design-boom-is-moving-beyond-pharma.-quercus-raised-5m-with-the-conviction-that-weeds-are-next","outlet":"SynBioBeta","date":"2026-10-21"},{"title":"Chai Discovery Secures $400M Series C to Propel AI-Driven Molecular Innovation","url":"https://www.synbiobeta.com/categories/ai-digital-biology","outlet":"SynBioBeta","date":"2026-07-21"},{"title":"Biomatter raises $18M for AI enzyme design","url":"https://casrai.org/news/biomatter-eighteen-million-ai-enzyme-design-series-a-2026","outlet":"CASRAI","date":"2026-11-12"},{"title":"Galux Raises $29M Series B to Advance AI-Driven Protein Design for Drug Discovery","url":"https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20260209145576/en/Galux-Raises-$29M-Series-B-to-Advance-AI-Driven-Protein-Design-for-Drug-Discovery","outlet":"BusinessWire","date":"2026-02-09"},{"title":"Anthropic Is Hiring Biologists, Building Wet Labs, and Betting Big on Drug Discovery","url":"https://www.synbiobeta.com/read/anthropic-is-hiring-biologists-building-wet-labs-and-betting-big-on-drug-discovery","outlet":"SynBioBeta","date":"2026-05-07"}]},{"id":"foundation-models-as-product","title":"Biological foundation models became a product category, and the moat moved from architecture to proprietary data","title_zh":"生物基礎模型成為一個產品類別，而護城河從架構移到了專有資料","oneLine":"Evo 2 is free and in Nature while Basecamp raised $140M on the claim that its biodiversity data is what public databases cannot give you, which tells you exactly where the value sits.","oneLine_zh":"Evo 2 免費而且登上 Nature，Basecamp 卻靠「它的生物多樣性資料是公開資料庫給不了的」這個主張募得 1.4 億美元，這就清楚說明了價值在哪裡。","body":"Arc Institute's Evo 2, trained on 9.3 trillion DNA base pairs from over 128,000 genomes, was published in Nature in March 2026 and is distributed fully open (weights, training data, inference tools) including via NVIDIA BioNeMo; Arc reports 200+ citations, 88,000+ downloads and over 8 million API requests in its first year. Arc also released its first virtual cell model (State) trained on ~270 million cells and ran the 2026 Virtual Cell Challenge, which asked models to predict post-perturbation expression after CRISPRi knockdown and 10x Flex profiling in cell contexts the model has never seen, sponsored by NVIDIA, 10x Genomics and Ultima Genomics with winners targeted for November 2026. Because the architectures are commoditising, money is going to data: Basecamp Research announced a $140M Series C on 23 September 2026 led by Bill Maris's S32 with NVIDIA and Menlo Ventures participating, explicitly on the premise that its biodiversity-derived BaseData gives its EDEN models training signal unavailable in public databases (totals reported inconsistently at $200M-$225M; an $800M valuation figure appears in one aggregator and is unconfirmed). Ginkgo Datapoints sells that same thesis as a service and told investors it serves 10 of the top 20 pharma companies with repeat training-data orders. Pharma is paying model-licence prices for data too: one aggregator reports GSK paying $50M upfront plus licence fees for non-exclusive access to Noetik's cancer virtual-cell models, and a $200M AstraZeneca-Tempus multimodal oncology data deal, while Tempus itself launched an effort in September 2026 to build the largest multimodal whole-genome dataset. The open-source counter-move is real: Outpost Bio open-sourced a microbiome foundation model, its data and its benchmark in September 2026, showing a model trained only on soil, ocean and wastewater still improves prediction of human gut outcomes, which is the first evidence that microbiome structure is universal enough to support one shared model. GenBio AI announced a world model of the human cell in August 2026. I could not find published per-token or per-seat API rate cards for EvolutionaryScale, Profluent or Basecamp; treat any specific API price as unverified.","body_zh":"Arc Institute 的 Evo 2 以超過 128,000 個基因組、9.3 兆個 DNA 鹼基對訓練，於 2026 年 3 月發表於 Nature，並以完全開放的方式發布（權重、訓練資料、推論工具），通路包括 NVIDIA BioNeMo；Arc 回報第一年累積 200 篇以上引用、88,000 次以上下載，以及超過 800 萬次 API 請求。Arc 也釋出其第一個虛擬細胞模型（State），以約 2.7 億個細胞訓練，並舉辦 2026 年 Virtual Cell Challenge，要求模型在從未見過的細胞情境中，預測經 CRISPRi 敲低與 10x Flex 分析後的擾動後表現量；贊助者為 NVIDIA、10x Genomics 與 Ultima Genomics，預定 2026 年 11 月公布優勝。由於架構正在商品化，資金流向資料：Basecamp Research 於 2026 年 9 月 23 日宣布 1.4 億美元 C 輪，由 Bill Maris 的 S32 領投，NVIDIA 與 Menlo Ventures 參與，明確的前提是其源自生物多樣性的 BaseData 能給 EDEN 模型公開資料庫所沒有的訓練訊號（累計金額各方回報不一，從 2 億到 2.25 億美元；某個資料彙整平台出現 8 億美元估值的數字，未經確認）。Ginkgo Datapoints 把同樣的論點包成服務銷售，並告訴投資人它服務前 20 大製藥公司中的 10 家，且有回購訓練資料的訂單。製藥業也在以模型授權的價格買資料：某個資料彙整平台回報 GSK 為非獨家取用 Noetik 的癌症虛擬細胞模型，支付 5,000 萬美元前期款加授權費，以及一筆 2 億美元的 AstraZeneca-Tempus 多模態腫瘤資料交易；Tempus 本身則於 2026 年 9 月啟動計畫，要建立最大的多模態全基因組資料集。開放原始碼的反制行動也是真的：Outpost Bio 於 2026 年 9 月把一個微生物體基礎模型連同其資料與基準一起開源，顯示只用土壤、海洋與廢水資料訓練的模型，仍能改善對人類腸道結果的預測，這是第一個證據，說明微生物體的結構具有足夠的普遍性，可以支撐一個共用模型。GenBio AI 於 2026 年 8 月宣布一個人類細胞的世界模型。我找不到 EvolutionaryScale、Profluent 或 Basecamp 公開的每 token 或每席次 API 價目表；任何具體的 API 價格都應視為未經查證。","whyItMatters":"A research institution cannot out-train Arc or Basecamp, but it can own a dataset nobody else has. The 2026 lesson is that a modest, well-labelled, locally-collected dataset with a published benchmark is a durable asset, while a model built on public data is not. Taiwan's biodiversity, agriculture and clinical cohorts are exactly that kind of unreplicated signal.","whyItMatters_zh":"研究機構沒辦法在訓練上贏過 Arc 或 Basecamp，但可以擁有一份別人沒有的資料集。2026 年的教訓是：一份規模不大、標註良好、在地採集並附有公開基準的資料集是持久的資產，而建立在公開資料上的模型不是。台灣的生物多樣性、農業與臨床世代資料，正是這種無法被複製的訊號。","gemsAction":"Pick one narrow, locally-sourced dataset GEMS can own and release properly (subtropical soil or coastal microbiomes, local crop pathogens, a defined enzyme family from Taiwanese isolates), with a public benchmark task attached, following Outpost Bio's model-plus-data-plus-benchmark pattern. Teach students to fine-tune and probe Evo 2 or an ESM-class model through NVIDIA BioNeMo rather than training from scratch. Treat the benchmark paper, not the model, as the publishable output.","gemsAction_zh":"挑一份 GEMS 能夠擁有並妥善公開的、範圍明確的在地資料集（亞熱帶土壤或沿岸微生物體、本地作物病原、取自台灣菌株的特定酵素家族），並附上一項公開的基準任務，依照 Outpost Bio「模型加資料加基準」的模式。教學生透過 NVIDIA BioNeMo 微調並探測 Evo 2 或 ESM 這一類模型，而不是從零訓練。把基準論文、而不是模型，當成可發表的產出。","maturity":"accelerating","refs":[{"title":"One Model, Every Microbiome (Outpost Bio open-sources model, data and benchmark)","url":"https://www.synbiobeta.com/read/one-model-every-microbiome","outlet":"SynBioBeta","date":"2026-09-15"},{"title":"The 2026 Virtual Cell Challenge: predicting perturbation responses in cell contexts a model has never seen","url":"https://arcinstitute.org/news/virtual-cell-challenge-2026","outlet":"Arc Institute","date":"2026-08-01"},{"title":"Arc Tools Hub (Evo 2 published March 2026, Nature)","url":"https://arcinstitute.org/tools","outlet":"Arc Institute","date":"2026-03-01"},{"title":"Basecamp Research Raises $140M to Advance AI-Designed Therapeutics","url":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/basecamp-research-raises-140m-to-advance-ai-designed-therapeutics-302887617.html","outlet":"PR Newswire","date":"2026-09-23"},{"title":"Pharma AI Data Licensing: Model Training Deal Structures","url":"https://intuitionlabs.ai/articles/pharma-ai-data-licensing-deal-structures","outlet":"IntuitionLabs","date":"2026-01-01"},{"title":"Tempus Launches Effort to Build the Largest Multimodal Whole-Genome Dataset","url":"https://www.synbiobeta.com/read","outlet":"SynBioBeta","date":"2026-09-15"}]},{"id":"autonomous-labs-and-genesis-mission","title":"The execution layer: autonomous labs became federal infrastructure, and narrow agents became the sellable product","title_zh":"執行層：自主實驗室成了聯邦基礎設施，而窄用途代理成了賣得出去的產品","oneLine":"The Genesis Mission is paying Ginkgo $47M for a 97-robot autonomous lab inside a national lab, while the actual product-market fit in software is narrow agents that do the boring parts of one specific person's week.","oneLine_zh":"Genesis Mission 正支付 Ginkgo 4,700 萬美元，在一座國家實驗室內建一間擁有 97 台機器人的自主實驗室；而軟體真正找到產品市場契合的，卻是替某一種人處理一週中無聊環節的窄用途代理。","body":"Ginkgo Bioworks won $4.6-4.7M for AMP2, an 1,800 sq ft anaerobic autonomous lab at Pacific Northwest National Laboratory's EMSL with 14 Reconfigurable Automation Carts and 18 instruments, plus a $47M award for M2PC, a 32,000 sq ft Microbial Molecular Phenotyping Capability with 97 robots and 100+ instruments, breaking ground in 2026 and opening as a user facility by 2030. Both are among the first concrete projects under the White House Genesis Mission executive order directing the Department of Energy to build robotic laboratories for AI-directed experiments; Jason Kelly compared it to Manhattan and Apollo, and critically both run as user facilities open to competitive academic and industry access, so the capacity is rentable rather than captive. On the venture side the AI-scientist companies carry valuations well ahead of published output: Lila Sciences has disclosed roughly $550M (a ~$200M seed in March 2025, a ~$350M Series A in October 2025) and Bloomberg reported it in June 2026 in talks for ~$2B at a ~$8.5B pre-money valuation, while Periodic Labs raised a $300M seed in September 2025 and Forbes reported advanced talks in May 2026 at $7.5B. Neither close was confirmed in what I could read. The first-generation cloud labs are a cautionary tale: Strateos folded or restructured after an April 2023 announcement (its current status is reported inconsistently), Emerald Cloud Lab still operates from Austin but has had prolonged outages, and March 2026 analysis counts only a handful of commercial cloud labs accessible to outside scientists. The layer that actually sells is narrower and cheaper, and it shares one architectural principle. Potato launched Tater, an AI scientist, in autumn 2025, heard from users that it was not solving their real problem, and narrowed to Optimizer in August 2026, which converts an assay spec sheet plus a statement of available hardware into a multivariable design of experiments, a written protocol, plate maps and Opentrons worklists, using deterministic calculation for volumes, concentrations and dilution series rather than letting a language model guess. Roebling makes the identical claim for process engineering, with CEO Edward Shenderovich saying biological performance goes straight into mass and energy balances, equipment sizing, CapEx and OpEx, and that the calculations are deterministic, not guesses from a language model. Potato's Merrit Savener is explicit that the opportunity is not Ginkgo-scale throughput but better use of the 96-well plates a lab already runs, and that even large organisations skip design of experiments because the available tools are too hard. Alongside these: Transfyr launched a physical-AI platform for science with a $25M seed on 1 September 2026, Latent Labs' Latent-Y automates the literature review, PDB analysis and epitope selection that previously needed an expert designer, Weave Bio partnered with Takeda on AI regulatory automation in September 2026, Schrodinger unveiled the Bunsen AI co-scientist in August 2026, and Arc's genomic intelligence models were integrated into Biomni Lab in July 2026. Latent Labs supplies the structural consequence: when design gets cheap the binding constraint moves to wet-lab testing, target choice and the quality of the data used to judge candidates, and researchers start running experiments that never justified the time before, such as dozens of targets in parallel or several epitope hypotheses on one target at once.","body_zh":"Ginkgo Bioworks 取得 460 萬至 470 萬美元建置 AMP2——位於 Pacific Northwest National Laboratory 的 EMSL、面積 1,800 平方英尺的厭氧自主實驗室，配備 14 台可重組自動化推車與 18 台儀器——另取得 4,700 萬美元建置 M2PC，一座 32,000 平方英尺的微生物分子表現型分析設施，擁有 97 台機器人與 100 台以上儀器，2026 年動工，2030 年前以使用者設施形式開放。兩者都屬於白宮 Genesis Mission 行政命令（指示能源部建造供 AI 主導實驗的機器人實驗室）之下最早的具體專案；Jason Kelly 把它比作曼哈頓計畫與阿波羅計畫，而關鍵在於兩者都以使用者設施形式運作，以競爭方式開放給學術界與產業界申請，因此這些量能是可租用的，而不是被獨佔的。在創投這一側，AI 科學家公司的估值遠超出其已發表的成果：Lila Sciences 已揭露約 5.5 億美元募資（2025 年 3 月約 2 億美元種子輪、2025 年 10 月約 3.5 億美元 A 輪），Bloomberg 於 2026 年 6 月報導其正洽談約 20 億美元、投前估值約 85 億美元；Periodic Labs 則於 2025 年 9 月募得 3 億美元種子輪，Forbes 於 2026 年 5 月報導其以 75 億美元估值進入深度洽談。在我能讀到的資料中，兩筆交易都未確認完成。第一代雲端實驗室是個警世故事：Strateos 在 2023 年 4 月的一則公告後倒閉或重組（其現況各方回報不一），Emerald Cloud Lab 仍在 Austin 營運但曾長期中斷服務，而 2026 年 3 月的分析指出，外部科學家能使用的商業雲端實驗室只有寥寥數家。真正賣得動的那一層更窄、更便宜，而且共享同一個架構原則。Potato 於 2025 年秋天推出 AI 科學家 Tater，從使用者那裡聽到它沒有解決真正的問題，於 2026 年 8 月收窄為 Optimizer：它把一份檢測規格表加上一份可用硬體清單，轉換成多變數的實驗設計、一份書面實驗流程、盤面配置圖與 Opentrons 工作清單，而體積、濃度與稀釋序列都用確定性計算，不讓語言模型去猜。Roebling 在製程工程上提出一樣的主張，執行長 Edward Shenderovich 表示生物表現會直接進入質能平衡、設備選型、資本支出與營運支出的計算，而這些計算是確定性的，不是語言模型的猜測。Potato 的 Merrit Savener 明白表示，機會不在 Ginkgo 那種規模的通量，而在把實驗室本來就在跑的 96 孔盤用得更好；而且即使是大型組織也會跳過實驗設計，因為現有工具太難用。此外：Transfyr 於 2026 年 9 月 1 日以 2,500 萬美元種子輪推出面向科學的實體 AI 平台；Latent Labs 的 Latent-Y 自動化了過去需要專家設計師的文獻回顧、PDB 分析與表位選擇；Weave Bio 於 2026 年 9 月與 Takeda 合作進行 AI 法規自動化；Schrodinger 於 2026 年 8 月發表 Bunsen AI 協作科學家；Arc 的基因組智能模型則於 2026 年 7 月整合進 Biomni Lab。Latent Labs 指出了結構性後果：當設計變便宜，真正的限制就轉移到濕式實驗測試、標的選擇，以及用來評斷候選者的資料品質；研究者也開始做過去不值得花時間的實驗，例如同時平行處理數十個標的，或對同一個標的一次測試好幾個表位假說。","whyItMatters":"Access to autonomous experimentation is becoming a competitive resource allocated like beam time, by proposal rather than purchase, so the institution that can write a good proposal and ship machine-readable protocols will out-produce one with better pipettes. More immediately, agentic design tools lower the skill floor for sophisticated experimental design to exactly the level GEMS teaches: a high-school student with Optimizer-class tooling can run a designed multivariable experiment a postdoc would have run one condition at a time. The risk is students accepting tool output uncritically, which is precisely the judgement the 2026 labour market says it is paying for.","whyItMatters_zh":"自主實驗的使用權正變成一種像光束時間那樣分配的競爭性資源——靠提案而不是靠採購——所以能寫出好提案、能交出機器可讀實驗流程的機構，產出會勝過擁有更好移液器的機構。更直接的是，代理式設計工具把精密實驗設計的技能門檻降到正是 GEMS 所教的程度：一位高中生用 Optimizer 這一級的工具，就能跑出一個博士後過去得一次一個條件慢慢做的多變數設計實驗。風險在於學生不加批判地接受工具輸出，而那正是 2026 年勞動市場說它願意付錢買的判斷力。","gemsAction":"Adopt one agentic design tool this year and build curriculum around it rather than treating it as optional: pair Potato's Optimizer (or equivalent) with an open, scriptable liquid handler such as an Opentrons OT-2, and require every student project to submit an executable protocol and a design-of-experiments plan alongside its notebook. Explicitly teach the deterministic-versus-generative distinction by having students hand-check a tool's dilution maths and audit a predicted structure, and require each project to state what the tool got wrong. Track EMSL/PNNL user-facility calls and Genesis Mission access terms, and identify an Asia-Pacific equivalent to apply to within 12 months.","gemsAction_zh":"今年就採用一套代理式設計工具，並圍繞它建立課程，而不是把它當成選配：把 Potato 的 Optimizer（或同等工具）與一台開放、可腳本化的自動分液設備（例如 Opentrons OT-2）搭配，並要求每個學生專案在實驗記錄之外，同時交出一份可執行的實驗流程與一份實驗設計計畫。明確教導確定性與生成式的差別：讓學生手動核算工具算出的稀釋數學，並審查一個預測結構，而且要求每個專案都寫出工具錯在哪裡。追蹤 EMSL/PNNL 的使用者設施徵案與 Genesis Mission 的使用條件，並在 12 個月內找出一個可以申請的亞太對等設施。","maturity":"accelerating","refs":[{"title":"Ginkgo Joins Genesis Project to Build a $47 Million Autonomous Robot Lab","url":"https://www.synbiobeta.com/read/ginkgo-joins-genesis-project-to-build-a-47-million-autonomous-robot-lab","outlet":"SynBioBeta","date":"2025-12-09"},{"title":"Potato Just Launched the Tool It Wishes It Had as a Lab Scientist","url":"https://www.synbiobeta.com/read/potato-just-launched-the-tool-it-wishes-it-had-as-a-lab-scientist","outlet":"SynBioBeta","date":"2026-08-20"},{"title":"Transfyr Launches Physical AI Platform for Science with $25M Seed Funding","url":"https://www.synbiobeta.com/categories/ai-digital-biology","outlet":"SynBioBeta","date":"2026-09-01"},{"title":"Lila Sciences funding: Every round, investor, and valuation (2026)","url":"https://www.revenuememo.com/p/lila-sciences-funding","outlet":"Revenue Memo","date":"2026-10-01"},{"title":"Former OpenAI Researcher To Raise $500 Million For AI Science Startup","url":"https://www.forbes.com/sites/iainmartin/2026/05/07/former-openai-researcher-to-raise-500-million-for-ai-science-startup/","outlet":"Forbes","date":"2026-05-07"},{"title":"No, there are not hundreds of cloud labs in biology","url":"https://forum.effectivealtruism.org/posts/cyZdRBcRokJ8fhYEd/no-there-are-not-hundreds-of-cloud-labs-in-biology","outlet":"EA Forum","date":"2026-03-01"},{"title":"Latent-Y Automates Antibody Design Work that Slows Down Early Drug Development","url":"https://www.synbiobeta.com/read/latent-y-automates-antibody-design-work-that-slows-down-early-drug-development","outlet":"SynBioBeta","date":"2026-10-21"},{"title":"Cemvita and Roebling Bring AI-Native Engineering to Industrial BioSolutions","url":"https://www.synbiobeta.com/read/cemvita-and-roebling-want-to-kill-the-expensive-surprise-in-industrial-biotech","outlet":"SynBioBeta","date":"2026-10-14"}]},{"id":"post-platform-correction","title":"The post-Ginkgo correction: the platform company is dead, the picks-and-shovels company is compounding","title_zh":"後 Ginkgo 時代的修正：平台公司已死，賣鋤頭鏟子的公司則在複利成長","oneLine":"Ginkgo's revenue roughly halved year-on-year while Twist Bioscience grew 22% to $459M and hit positive adjusted EBITDA, which is the clearest statement the market has made about what the 'platform' business model is actually worth.","oneLine_zh":"Ginkgo 的營收年減約一半，Twist Bioscience 卻成長 22% 達 4.59 億美元並轉為調整後 EBITDA 正值，這是市場對「平台」商業模式究竟值多少，所做出最清楚的表態。","body":"Ginkgo Bioworks reported Q2 2026 revenue of $20.2M against $39.1M a year earlier, attributing the drop to a reduced scope of services for a large agriculture customer and fewer pharma and biotech enterprise programs; aggregator summaries put Q3 2026 at about $28M, down 6% year on year with the sequential rise partly a catch-up on a modified contract. Losses are narrowing but not gone: Q3 net loss from continuing operations improved 44% and adjusted EBITDA improved 58%, yet adjusted EBITDA remained negative at $22M, with quarterly cash burn of $27M, nine-month burn of $120M and full-year burn guidance of $125-150M against liquidity reported between $285M and $373M depending on the date. The company has repositioned around autonomous labs, with Cloud Lab, Datapoints and Solutions as the three businesses feeding it, but management is not breaking out revenue by line, which makes the pivot unmeasurable from outside. Contrast Twist Bioscience, which reported fiscal 2026 revenue of $459.4M, up 22% from $376.6M, gross margin up to 52.4% from 50.7%, record Q4 revenue of $126.6M (up ~28%, its fifteenth consecutive quarter of sequential growth), positive adjusted EBITDA in Q4, and FY2027 guidance of $550-560M. Twist's fastest-growing segment is DNA Synthesis and Protein Solutions at 39% growth versus 12% for NGS Applications, and management explicitly guides AI-related orders from $25M in FY2025 to $50M in FY2026 to a $100M target in FY2027. That is the shape of the correction: the company selling the reagent to every AI design shop is profitable, the company that promised to be the design shop is not. A third model is emerging in between, in which partners stitch together a single contract across the stack rather than one firm owning it: Saku Biosciences and Sable Fermentation announced in September 2026 a single agreement covering US customers from strain engineering through scale-up, and Cemvita partnered with Roebling in October 2026 to put biology, process engineering and techno-economics into one deterministic model.","body_zh":"Ginkgo Bioworks 回報 2026 年第二季營收 2,020 萬美元，去年同期為 3,910 萬美元，並把下滑歸因於某大型農業客戶縮減服務範圍，以及製藥與生技企業專案減少；資料彙整摘要把 2026 年第三季列為約 2,800 萬美元，年減 6%，而季增部分來自一份經修改合約的補認列。虧損在縮小但未消除：第三季持續營業部門淨損改善 44%，調整後 EBITDA 改善 58%，但調整後 EBITDA 仍為負 2,200 萬美元，單季現金消耗 2,700 萬美元，前九個月消耗 1.2 億美元，全年消耗指引為 1.25 億至 1.5 億美元，而流動性視報導日期不同，介於 2.85 億至 3.73 億美元。公司已重新定位到自主實驗室，以 Cloud Lab、Datapoints 與 Solutions 三項業務支撐，但管理層並未分項揭露營收，使得這次轉型從外部無法衡量。對照 Twist Bioscience：2026 財年營收 4.594 億美元，較 3.766 億美元成長 22%，毛利率由 50.7% 升至 52.4%，第四季營收創下 1.266 億美元新高（成長約 28%，為連續第十五季季增），第四季調整後 EBITDA 轉正，2027 財年指引 5.5 億至 5.6 億美元。Twist 成長最快的部門是 DNA 合成與蛋白質解決方案，成長 39%，相對於 NGS 應用的 12%；管理層並明確指引 AI 相關訂單自 2025 財年的 2,500 萬美元，到 2026 財年的 5,000 萬美元，再到 2027 財年的 1 億美元目標。這就是這次修正的形狀：把試劑賣給每一家 AI 設計公司的公司有利潤，而承諾自己就是那家設計公司的則沒有。介於兩者之間的第三種模式正在出現，由夥伴跨層串成單一合約，而不是由一家公司通吃：Saku Biosciences 與 Sable Fermentation 於 2026 年 9 月宣布一份單一協議，為美國客戶涵蓋從菌株工程到放大生產；Cemvita 則於 2026 年 10 月與 Roebling 合作，把生物學、製程工程與技術經濟分析放進同一個確定性模型。","whyItMatters":"Students and faculty need to read company claims sceptically, and the cleanest discipline for that is reading actual filings. It also reframes what a research institution should aspire to be: not a miniature Ginkgo, but a reliable generator of a specific, hard-to-fake capability that someone else needs. Revenue follows a product, not a platform narrative.","whyItMatters_zh":"學生與教師需要以懷疑的眼光讀公司的說法，而最乾淨的訓練方式就是去讀真正的財報文件。它也重新界定了一所研究機構該有什麼志向：不是做一個迷你版 Ginkgo，而是成為某種具體、難以造假、且別人需要的能力的可靠產出者。營收跟著產品走，不是跟著平台敘事走。","gemsAction":"Build a short financial-literacy strand into the programme: have students read the Ginkgo 10-Q and the Twist FY2026 8-K side by side and write the one-page memo explaining the divergence, which is a genuinely employable analytical skill. Define GEMS's own niche as narrowly as Twist defines its: one capability done reliably, with a measurable output, rather than an end-to-end platform claim. Use the Cemvita-Roebling techno-economic framing when evaluating any student project that proposes a product.","gemsAction_zh":"在課程中加入一段簡短的財務素養主軸：讓學生並排閱讀 Ginkgo 的 10-Q 與 Twist 的 2026 財年 8-K，寫一頁備忘錄解釋兩者的分歧，這是一項真正能就業的分析能力。把 GEMS 自己的利基定義得像 Twist 那樣窄：一項做得可靠、有可量測產出的能力，而不是端到端的平台宣稱。評估任何提出產品的學生專案時，採用 Cemvita-Roebling 的技術經濟分析框架。","maturity":"mainstream","refs":[{"title":"Ginkgo Bioworks Holdings, Inc. - Form 10-Q - FY2026 (Q2 2026)","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001830214/000162828026054298/dna-20260630.htm","outlet":"SEC EDGAR","date":"2026-06-30"},{"title":"Ginkgo Bioworks Holdings Inc (DNA) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Highlights: Cost Cuts, First Big Wins","url":"https://finance.yahoo.com/healthcare/articles/ginkgo-bioworks-holdings-inc-dna-050529129.html","outlet":"Yahoo Finance","date":"2026-11-01"},{"title":"Twist Bioscience Corp - Form 8-K - FY2026 fourth quarter and full year results","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001581280/000158128026000053/twst-2026930xex991.htm","outlet":"SEC EDGAR","date":"2026-11-12"},{"title":"Twist Bioscience Corp (TWST) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Highlights: Record Revenue and AI-Driven Growth","url":"https://finance.yahoo.com/healthcare/articles/twist-bioscience-corp-twst-q3-190050269.html","outlet":"Yahoo Finance","date":"2026-08-01"},{"title":"Cemvita and Roebling Bring AI-Native Engineering to Industrial BioSolutions","url":"https://www.synbiobeta.com/read/cemvita-and-roebling-want-to-kill-the-expensive-surprise-in-industrial-biotech","outlet":"SynBioBeta","date":"2026-10-14"},{"title":"Saku Biosciences and Sable Fermentation Offer US Customers One Agreement From Strain Engineering Through Scale Up","url":"https://www.synbiobeta.com/read","outlet":"SynBioBeta","date":"2026-09-23"}]},{"id":"cost-of-goods-wall","title":"The cost-of-goods wall is now an engineering problem with government money behind it","title_zh":"生產成本這道牆現在是一個有政府資金撐著的工程問題","oneLine":"Nobody is short of strains; everybody is short of a tank they can afford, and in 2026 the US Department of War started paying to redesign the tank itself.","oneLine_zh":"沒有人缺菌株，大家缺的是一個負擔得起的發酵槽；而 2026 年美國 Department of War 開始出錢重新設計這個槽本身。","body":"Biosphere received $21M from the Department of War through the Defense Industrial Base Consortium to build, run and prove a 20,000-litre bioreactor sterilised with UV light instead of steam, targeting operation by late 2027 at roughly 100 tons of product per year. The economics are the whole point: engineered microbes making enzymes, food ingredients or specialty chemicals get overrun by contaminants, so they need near-pharmaceutical cleanliness, but steam sterilisation forces pressure-rated steel, a boiler and extensive clean-in-place plumbing. A new 2,000-litre stainless tank alone runs $500,000 to $1,000,000 (figure from cocoa startup California Cultured), and industry estimates put surrounding piping, utilities and cleaning systems at several times the tank cost. CEO Brian Heligman notes biopharma abandoned steam sterilisation as too expensive and unreliable in favour of single-use plastic bags, which cap out at a few thousand litres and can cost tens of thousands of dollars per batch in consumables, economics that work for medicine and not for chemicals. The scale-up record supports the diagnosis. Liberation Labs' 600,000-litre Richmond, Indiana plant has taken three-plus years and $126.5M against an original end-of-2024 production target. Perfect Day's plant was due to reach mechanical completion in September 2026 with first commercial truckloads targeted in Q4 2026 after roughly 20 months of construction. Formo took a €35M (about $36M) EIB loan for biomass and precision-fermentation cheese. Plantible Foods raised $35M helped by a USDA-backed loan to scale Rubisco protein fivefold. Capra Biosciences got $17M from HHS in August 2026 to onshore essential API production, and the Department of War backed Visolis for bio-based solvents in February 2026. The counter-example that proves scale-up is tractable when you instrument it: Cemvita ran a 75,000-litre FermOil campaign at Bio Base Europe Pilot Plant in Ghent in May 2026 with consistent results from 30 litres to 75,000 litres, a 2,500-fold scale increase, and is now feeding that data plus its failures into a Roebling model that connects strain performance directly to mass and energy balances, equipment sizing, CapEx and OpEx.","body_zh":"Biosphere 透過 Defense Industrial Base Consortium 從 Department of War 取得 2,100 萬美元，用以建造、運轉並驗證一座以紫外光而非蒸氣滅菌的 20,000 公升生物反應器，目標在 2027 年底前運轉，年產約 100 公噸產品。經濟性就是整件事的重點：工程化微生物在生產酵素、食品原料或特用化學品時會被污染菌壓過，因此需要接近製藥級的潔淨度，但蒸氣滅菌迫使你採用耐壓鋼材、鍋爐與大量的現場清洗管路。一座全新的 2,000 公升不鏽鋼槽本身就要 50 萬至 100 萬美元（數字來自可可新創 California Cultured），而業界估計周邊管路、公用設施與清洗系統是槽體成本的數倍。執行長 Brian Heligman 指出，生物製藥早已因為太貴又不可靠而放棄蒸氣滅菌，改用單次使用的塑膠袋，但後者上限只有數千公升，每批次的耗材成本可達數萬美元，這種經濟性對藥品可行、對化學品不可行。放大生產的歷史紀錄支持這個診斷。Liberation Labs 位於印第安納州 Richmond 的 600,000 公升工廠已耗費三年多與 1.265 億美元，而原定投產目標是 2024 年底。Perfect Day 的工廠原定 2026 年 9 月機械完工，在約 20 個月的施工後，首批商業出貨目標訂在 2026 年第四季。Formo 取得 3,500 萬歐元（約 3,600 萬美元）的 EIB 貸款，用於生物質與精準發酵乳酪。Plantible Foods 在 USDA 擔保貸款協助下募得 3,500 萬美元，把 Rubisco 蛋白產能放大五倍。Capra Biosciences 於 2026 年 8 月自 HHS 取得 1,700 萬美元，將必要原料藥生產移回本土；Department of War 則於 2026 年 2 月支持 Visolis 發展生物基溶劑。證明只要把製程儀器化、放大生產就可處理的反例是：Cemvita 於 2026 年 5 月在根特的 Bio Base Europe Pilot Plant 執行一次 75,000 公升的 FermOil 生產，從 30 公升到 75,000 公升、放大 2,500 倍都得到一致結果，現在正把這些資料連同失敗經驗餵進一個 Roebling 模型，把菌株表現直接接上質能平衡、設備選型、資本支出與營運支出。","whyItMatters":"Every student project that ends at a shake flask stops exactly where the industry's real problem starts. Teaching scale-aware thinking, including techno-economic analysis, is cheap and almost nobody does it at the secondary or early-undergraduate level. It also happens to be where governments are putting money, which means jobs.","whyItMatters_zh":"每一個停在搖瓶階段的學生專案，都剛好停在產業真正問題開始的地方。教「具規模意識的思考」，包括技術經濟分析，成本很低，而在中學或大學低年級幾乎沒有人在做。這也正好是各國政府正在投錢的地方，也就是有工作機會的地方。","gemsAction":"Add a compulsory techno-economic analysis step to every applied student project: titre, rate, yield, and a one-page cost model including feedstock, utilities and downstream recovery, following the Cemvita-Roebling logic that biological improvements only matter where they move plant economics. Teach bioprocess basics on small instrumented benchtop fermenters with real data logging rather than more flask work. Approach Taiwan's food, enzyme or amino-acid fermentation industry for a scale-up site visit and a student data-analysis project on an existing production dataset.","gemsAction_zh":"為每個應用型學生專案加上一道必修的技術經濟分析步驟：產量、速率、產率，加上一頁含原料、公用設施與下游回收的成本模型，依循 Cemvita-Roebling 的邏輯——生物上的改善只有在能撼動工廠經濟時才有意義。用小型、具儀器與真實資料記錄功能的桌上型發酵槽教生物製程基礎，而不是再多做搖瓶實驗。接洽台灣的食品、酵素或胺基酸發酵業，安排一次放大生產的場勘，以及一個以現有生產資料為題的學生資料分析專案。","maturity":"accelerating","refs":[{"title":"Biosphere Lands $21M From the Department of War to Build a Bioreactor Cleaned With Light","url":"https://www.synbiobeta.com/read/biosphere-lands-21m-from-the-department-of-war-to-build-a-bioreactor-cleaned-with-light","outlet":"SynBioBeta","date":"2026-11-13"},{"title":"Cemvita and Roebling Bring AI-Native Engineering to Industrial BioSolutions","url":"https://www.synbiobeta.com/read/cemvita-and-roebling-want-to-kill-the-expensive-surprise-in-industrial-biotech","outlet":"SynBioBeta","date":"2026-10-14"},{"title":"Fermentation capacity map: who has tanks ($126.5m committed, three years after groundbreaking)","url":"https://lifematetech.com/articles/fermentation-capacity-map-who-has-tanks","outlet":"LifeMate Tech","date":"2026-08-01"},{"title":"2026 State of the Industry report: Fermentation for meat, seafood, eggs, dairy and ingredients","url":"https://gfi.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/GFI-2026-State-of-the-Industry-Fermentation-for-meat-seafood-eggs-dairy-and-ingredients.pdf","outlet":"Good Food Institute","date":"2026-04-01"},{"title":"HHS Backs Capra Biosciences with $17M to Onshore Essential API Production","url":"https://www.synbiobeta.com/insights","outlet":"SynBioBeta","date":"2026-08-05"},{"title":"USDA-Backed Loan Helps Plantible Foods Raise $35M to Scale Up Rubisco Protein Fivefold","url":"https://www.synbiobeta.com/categories/bioeconomy-policy","outlet":"SynBioBeta","date":"2026-08-11"}]},{"id":"ag-food-synbio-regulatory-unlock","title":"Agricultural and food synbio got its regulatory unlock, and the winning pitch is economics not sustainability","title_zh":"農業與食品合成生物學取得了法規上的解鎖，而勝出的說法是經濟效益，不是永續","oneLine":"USDA conditionally licensed the first engineered microbe that manufactures antibodies inside an animal's gut, it is already in 35 million broilers, and the sales argument is feed conversion rather than fewer dead chickens.","oneLine_zh":"USDA 有條件許可了第一株能在動物腸道內製造抗體的工程化微生物，它已用於 3,500 萬隻肉雞，而銷售論點是飼料換肉率，不是少死幾隻雞。","body":"On 29 September 2026 USDA's Center for Veterinary Biologics conditionally licensed BiomEdit's BE-101, a Limosilactobacillus reuteri strain engineered to secrete llama-derived single-domain antibodies against Clostridium perfringens alpha toxin and NetB; it is now in more than 35 million broilers. The design choices are instructive: the expression cassette is chromosomally integrated rather than plasmid-borne for genetic stability, the chassis is two chicken-derived strains from the same clade, and delivery exploits the one day a chicken's gut is nearly empty, via a spray cabinet at hatch, with colonisation in about a day and roughly three weeks of protection from one application. The market framing matters more than the biology: necrotic enteritis costs global poultry production an estimated $6 billion a year, mostly through feed conversion and weight gain rather than mortality, and antibiotics are the wrong tool twice over because C. perfringens is a normal gut resident and because antibiotics have been pulled from broiler production. BiomEdit went to USDA in early 2023, months after launch, and co-created the regulatory path, choosing USDA over FDA and EPA jurisdiction up front so one agency could issue the Finding of No Significant Impact. The rest of the sector shows the same pattern of commercial pragmatism: Leaps by Bayer led Robigo's Series A in September 2026 on engineered microbes for crop protection; Quercus raised $5M to design mini-protein herbicides; Pivot Bio, now valued at roughly $2 billion on about $697M raised and reporting use on more than 15 million corn acres (13 million in its 2024 impact report), cut prices, raised production and announced a price and supply assurance programme spanning the 2026, 2027 and 2028 seasons as fertiliser costs spiked, and moved its headquarters from California to Minnesota; its PROVEN G3 trials report replacing an average of 33 pounds of synthetic nitrogen per acre, a company figure I could not independently verify. C16 Biosciences expanded its Palmless brand into food and beauty in August 2026, and Proxy Foods AI raised a $6M seed for a food R&D platform.","body_zh":"2026 年 9 月 29 日，USDA 的 Center for Veterinary Biologics 有條件許可了 BiomEdit 的 BE-101，一株經工程改造的 Limosilactobacillus reuteri，可分泌源自駱馬的單域抗體，針對 Clostridium perfringens 的 alpha 毒素與 NetB；目前已用於超過 3,500 萬隻肉雞。其設計選擇很有啟發性：表現卡匣是整合到染色體而非以質體攜帶，以確保遺傳穩定性；底盤是兩株取自雞、屬於同一分支的菌株；投遞則利用雞腸道幾乎排空的那一天，在孵化時以噴霧櫃施用，約一天完成移生，一次施用可提供約三週的保護。市場框架比生物學更重要：壞死性腸炎每年讓全球家禽生產損失估計 60 億美元，而且主要是透過飼料換肉率與體重增長，而非死亡率；抗生素在兩個層面上都是錯的工具，因為 C. perfringens 本來就是腸道常住菌，而且抗生素已從肉雞生產中被撤出。BiomEdit 在成立數月後、2023 年初就去找 USDA，共同打造出法規路徑，事先選定 USDA 而非 FDA 或 EPA 的管轄，好讓一個機關就能發出「無重大影響認定」。這個領域其餘部分也顯示同樣的商業務實取向：Leaps by Bayer 於 2026 年 9 月領投 Robigo 的 A 輪，投向作物保護用工程化微生物；Quercus 募得 500 萬美元設計迷你蛋白除草劑；Pivot Bio 目前估值約 20 億美元、累計募資約 6.97 億美元，回報使用面積超過 1,500 萬英畝玉米田（其 2024 年影響力報告為 1,300 萬英畝），並在肥料價格飆漲時降價、提高產量，宣布一個橫跨 2026、2027 與 2028 產季的價格與供應保證方案，同時把總部從加州搬到明尼蘇達；其 PROVEN G3 試驗回報平均每英畝可替代 33 磅合成氮肥，這是公司自己的數字，我無法獨立查證。C16 Biosciences 於 2026 年 8 月把 Palmless 品牌擴展到食品與美妝，Proxy Foods AI 則為一個食品研發平台募得 600 萬美元種子輪。","whyItMatters":"Agriculture and food is where a Taiwanese institution has genuine comparative advantage: subtropical pathogens, aquaculture, local crops and a food industry that buys ingredients. It is also the domain where regulatory literacy, not just molecular skill, decides whether work reaches the field, and that literacy is teachable.","whyItMatters_zh":"農業與食品是台灣機構真正具有比較優勢的領域：亞熱帶病原、水產養殖、本地作物，以及一個會採購原料的食品產業。這也是「法規素養」而非單純分子技術決定工作能否落地的領域，而這種素養是可以教的。","gemsAction":"Run one student cohort project on a locally relevant agricultural target (a Taiwanese crop pathogen, an aquaculture gut health problem, or a feed-conversion question) and require a regulatory pathway memo naming the responsible Taiwanese agency alongside the science, mirroring how BiomEdit chose its agency before developing. Build a relationship with one Taiwanese agricultural research institute or an aquaculture or poultry producer so projects have a real end user. Teach students that the pitch is cost per tonne or per bird, not sustainability.","gemsAction_zh":"以一個與本地相關的農業標的（台灣的作物病原、水產養殖的腸道健康問題，或一個飼料換肉率的課題）執行一次學生梯隊專案，並要求除科學內容外，另附一份指明台灣權責機關的法規路徑備忘錄，仿效 BiomEdit 在開發前就先選定主管機關的做法。與一家台灣的農業研究機構，或一家水產養殖或家禽生產業者建立關係，讓專案有真正的終端使用者。教學生：要訴求的是每公噸或每隻的成本，不是永續。","maturity":"accelerating","refs":[{"title":"USDA Greenlights the First Engineered Microbe That Makes Antibodies in the Gut","url":"https://www.synbiobeta.com/read/usda-greenlights-the-first-engineered-microbe-that-makes-antibodies-in-the-gut","outlet":"SynBioBeta","date":"2026-10-22"},{"title":"Leaps by Bayer Leads Series A in Robigo, Betting on Engineered Microbes for Crop Protection","url":"https://www.synbiobeta.com/read/bayer-leads-series-a-in-robigo-betting-on-engineered-microbes-for-crop-protection","outlet":"SynBioBeta","date":"2026-09-17"},{"title":"Minnesota company is tackling nitrogen pollution with ag science in volatile fertilizer market","url":"https://minnesotareformer.com/2026/08/28/minnesota-company-poised-to-succeed-with-fertilizer-innovation-amid-volatile-market/","outlet":"Minnesota Reformer","date":"2026-08-28"},{"title":"Pivot Bio Silage Data Show Strong Tonnage and Milk Gains with PROVEN 40 and PROVEN G3","url":"https://www.pivotbio.com/press-releases/pivot-bio-silage-data-show-strong-tonnage-and-milk-gains-with-proven-40-and-proven-g3","outlet":"Pivot Bio","date":"2026-01-01"},{"title":"The protein design boom is moving beyond pharma. Quercus raised $5M","url":"https://www.synbiobeta.com/read/the-protein-design-boom-is-moving-beyond-pharma.-quercus-raised-5m-with-the-conviction-that-weeds-are-next","outlet":"SynBioBeta","date":"2026-10-21"}]},{"id":"dna-synthesis-cost-and-length","title":"DNA synthesis competition moved from price per base to length, turnaround guarantees and supply security","title_zh":"DNA 合成的競爭從每個鹼基的價格，轉向長度、交期保證與供應安全","oneLine":"Ansa sells 50 kb clonal constructs from $0.13 per base pair with an on-time guarantee while Twist advertises fragments from $0.07, which means the differentiator is no longer cost per base but what you can get, when.","oneLine_zh":"Ansa 以每鹼基對 0.13 美元起的價格銷售 50 kb 的單株構築體並保證準時交付，Twist 則標示片段每鹼基對 0.07 美元起，這意味著差異化已不在每個鹼基的成本，而在你能拿到什麼、什麼時候拿到。","body":"Ansa Biotechnologies, which uses enzymatic synthesis that binds nucleotides to a DNA polymerase before extension, launched a 50 kb clonal DNA product in October 2025, raised a $54.4M Series B with the industry's first guaranteed on-time service, priced from USD 0.13 per base pair across its 100 bp to 50 kb range per its April 2026 announcement, and partnered with Integrated DNA Technologies, with an upgraded joint e-commerce platform for complex constructs announced in September 2026. Twist Bioscience advertises Gene Fragments from USD 0.07 per base pair and has argued that chemical synthesis remains cheaper, more accurate and capable of longer strands, with CEO Emily Leproust previously calling cost the real fatal flaw of enzymatic synthesis; Twist's own answer has been to cut the expensive nucleoside triphosphate consumption in enzymatic routes. Twist's FY2026 numbers show where demand actually is: DNA Synthesis and Protein Solutions grew 39% versus 12% for NGS Applications, and the company targets $100M in AI-related orders in FY2027 from $25M in FY2025. Elegen launched a Gen II cell-free DNA platform in October 2025 and ENFINIA IVT-Ready DNA for mRNA workflows. Benchtop synthesis remains an awkward value proposition: a DNA Script Syntax-class instrument is cited at around $200,000, against commentary that per-base synthesis cost has fallen to roughly €0.1-0.3 from about €10 in the 1990s, so the instrument only pays back for labs with sustained, security-sensitive or turnaround-critical demand. Market sizing is unreliable: 2026 reports for enzymatic DNA synthesis range from USD 0.47 billion to USD 3.77 billion with a quoted 23.5% CAGR, and a November 2026 report flags tariffs raising prices for imported enzymes, reagents, microfluidic components and synthesis cartridges, which is a new and material cost pressure for any lab outside the US supply chain.","body_zh":"Ansa Biotechnologies 採用酵素合成，在延伸前先把核苷酸結合到一個 DNA 聚合酶上；該公司於 2025 年 10 月推出 50 kb 單株 DNA 產品，募得 5,440 萬美元 B 輪並推出業界首見的準時交付保證服務，依其 2026 年 4 月的公告，100 bp 至 50 kb 的全區間定價自每鹼基對 0.13 美元起，並與 Integrated DNA Technologies 合作，於 2026 年 9 月宣布升級版的複雜構築體聯合電子商務平台。Twist Bioscience 的 Gene Fragments 標價自每鹼基對 0.07 美元起，並主張化學合成仍然更便宜、更準確、也能做更長的鏈；執行長 Emily Leproust 先前稱成本是酵素合成真正的致命缺陷，而 Twist 自己的對策是降低酵素路線中昂貴的核苷三磷酸消耗量。Twist 的 2026 財年數字顯示需求實際在哪裡：DNA 合成與蛋白質解決方案成長 39%，NGS 應用成長 12%，而公司的目標是 AI 相關訂單從 2025 財年的 2,500 萬美元增加到 2027 財年的 1 億美元。Elegen 於 2025 年 10 月推出第二代無細胞 DNA 平台，以及供 mRNA 流程使用的 ENFINIA IVT-Ready DNA。桌上型合成設備仍是一個尷尬的價值主張：一台 DNA Script Syntax 級的儀器報價約 20 萬美元，而評論指出每個鹼基的合成成本已從 1990 年代的約 10 歐元降到約 0.1 至 0.3 歐元，所以這台儀器只對需求持續、對資訊安全敏感或對交期極度敏感的實驗室才划得來。市場規模估計並不可靠：2026 年關於酵素 DNA 合成的報告從 4.7 億美元到 37.7 億美元不等，並引用 23.5% 的年複合成長率；2026 年 11 月的一份報告則指出關稅推高了進口酵素、試劑、微流體元件與合成匣的價格，這對任何不在美國供應鏈內的實驗室都是新增且實質的成本壓力。","whyItMatters":"For a Taiwan-based institution the binding constraints are lead time, customs and tariff exposure, not headline price per base, and a project plan that assumes two-week delivery of a 10 kb construct will fail. Understanding the synthesis supply chain is a practical research-management skill. It also sets the real cost of ambition in any student build-and-test cycle.","whyItMatters_zh":"對一所位於台灣的機構而言，真正的限制是交期、海關與關稅暴露，不是每個鹼基的牌面價格；一個假設 10 kb 構築體兩週就能到貨的專案計畫一定會失敗。了解合成供應鏈是一項實務的研究管理能力。它也決定了任何學生建構與測試循環中，「有野心」的真實成本。","gemsAction":"Negotiate an academic or education account with one long-DNA vendor (IDT, Twist, Ansa or Elegen) and one regional distributor, and publish internal lead-time and landed-cost benchmarks so students plan to real timelines. Teach design-for-synthesis explicitly: codon optimisation, repeat and GC avoidance, modular assembly, and ordering fragments you can assemble locally rather than one long construct. Do not buy a benchtop synthesiser in the next 12 months unless a security or turnaround case justifies the roughly $200,000 instrument cost.","gemsAction_zh":"與一家長鏈 DNA 供應商（IDT、Twist、Ansa 或 Elegen）和一家區域代理商談下學術或教育帳戶，並公布內部的交期與到岸成本基準，好讓學生依真實時程規劃。明確教導「為合成而設計」：密碼子最佳化、避開重複序列與 GC 偏差、模組化組裝，以及訂購可在本地自行組裝的片段，而不是一條長構築體。未來 12 個月內不要購買桌上型合成儀，除非有資訊安全或交期上的理由足以合理化那台約 20 萬美元的設備。","maturity":"mainstream","refs":[{"title":"IDT and Ansa Biotechnologies Enhance E-Commerce Platform for DNA Constructs","url":"https://www.synbiobeta.com/categories/reading-writing-and-editing-dna","outlet":"SynBioBeta","date":"2026-09-01"},{"title":"Ansa Biotechnologies Targets Nucleic Acid Synthesis Market With Ultra-Long Clonal DNA Service","url":"https://ansabio.com/news-events/news/ansa-biotechnologies-targets-nucleic-acid-synthesis-market-with-ultra-long-clonal-dna-service/","outlet":"Ansa Biotechnologies","date":"2026-04-01"},{"title":"Ansa snares $54.4M in series B financing to boost its DNA synthesis platform","url":"https://www.fiercepharma.com/manufacturing/ansa-snares-544m-series-b-financing-boost-its-dna-synthesis-platform","outlet":"Fierce Pharma","date":"2025-10-03"},{"title":"Enzymatic DNA Synthesis Technology Market Report 2026: 23.5% CAGR, DNA Script, Ansa Biotechnologies and Ribbon Bio Scale Long DNA","url":"https://www.globenewswire.com/news-release/2026/11/09/3398520/28124/en/enzymatic-deoxyribonucleic-acid-dna-synthesis-technology-market-report-2026-capitalize-on-23-5-cagr-dna-script-ansa-biotechnologies-and-ribbon-bio-scale-long-dna.html","outlet":"GlobeNewswire","date":"2026-11-09"},{"title":"Emerging biotech atlas part two: Writing DNA to create synthetic life","url":"https://cfg.eu/emerging-biotech-atlas-part-two-writing-dna-to-create-synthetic-life/","outlet":"Centre for Future Generations","date":"2026-01-01"}]},{"id":"biosecurity-screening-becomes-mandatory","title":"Nucleic acid synthesis screening became binding US policy, and it reaches anyone who sells to US-funded labs","title_zh":"核酸合成篩查成為具約束力的美國政策，而且管到任何賣給美國經費支持實驗室的人","oneLine":"The November 2026 National Policy for Nucleic Acid Synthesis Screening forces federally funded researchers to buy only from certified providers that screen orders of 50+ nucleotides with NIST-verified tools and keep records for eight years.","oneLine_zh":"2026 年 11 月的國家核酸合成篩查政策，強制接受聯邦經費的研究人員只能向認證供應商採購，而這些供應商必須以 NIST 驗證過的工具篩查 50 個核苷酸以上的訂單，並保留紀錄八年。","body":"The White House released the National Policy for Nucleic Acid Synthesis Screening on 5 November 2026 alongside NSTM-6, implementing Executive Order 14292 of May 2025 which had directed OSTP to revise or replace the 2024 framework. Under it, federally funded researchers must purchase from certified providers; providers must screen sequence orders of 50 or more nucleotides using NIST-verified tools, verify customer identity, report flagged orders and retain records for eight years, with implementation phased in over roughly a year. Separately, a revised BIOSECURE Act became law in December 2025 as Section 851 of the FY2026 NDAA, prohibiting US entities holding relevant federal contracts, grants or loans from using equipment from specified Chinese biotechnology firms in their supply chains; a July 2026 implementing policy exists but ambiguity over what counts as prohibited research has created real uncertainty for collaborations. Congress is pressing further: the Biosecurity Modernization and Innovation Act (S.3741, with House companion H.R. 3029) was introduced in January 2026 to require Commerce to issue binding regulations for nucleic acid synthesis security, and had not passed as of what I could verify. The commercial layer is appearing alongside the policy: Praio launched an environment screening panel at SynBioBeta 2026 in May, and Neion Bio brought Barnwell Bio's biosurveillance into its egg-based manufacturing flocks in October 2026, which is the beginning of screening and surveillance as purchasable services rather than compliance overhead. Note the coupling to the previous trend: AI protein design plus cheap synthesis is precisely the dual-use pairing these rules target, and Belfer Center analysis frames AI-enabled biotechnology as a governance problem the current regime only partially addresses.","body_zh":"白宮於 2026 年 11 月 5 日隨 NSTM-6 一併發布國家核酸合成篩查政策，落實 2025 年 5 月的第 14292 號行政命令——該命令曾指示 OSTP 修訂或取代 2024 年的框架。依該政策，接受聯邦經費的研究人員必須向認證供應商採購；供應商必須以 NIST 驗證過的工具篩查 50 個核苷酸以上的序列訂單、驗證客戶身分、回報被標記的訂單，並保留紀錄八年，實施期約一年分階段展開。另外，修訂後的 BIOSECURE Act 於 2025 年 12 月成為法律，列為 2026 財年 NDAA 第 851 條，禁止持有相關聯邦合約、補助或貸款的美國實體在供應鏈中使用特定中國生技公司的設備；2026 年 7 月已有實施政策，但「何者構成被禁止的研究」仍有模糊之處，對合作造成實質的不確定性。國會還在繼續推進：Biosecurity Modernization and Innovation Act（S.3741，眾院對應版本 H.R. 3029）於 2026 年 1 月提出，要求商務部就核酸合成安全發布具約束力的法規，就我能查證的範圍而言尚未通過。商業層面也隨政策浮現：Praio 於 2026 年 5 月的 SynBioBeta 2026 推出環境篩查套組，Neion Bio 於 2026 年 10 月把 Barnwell Bio 的生物監測導入其以雞蛋為基礎的生產雞群，這是篩查與監測開始成為可購買的服務、而非法遵負擔的起點。注意它與前一項趨勢的耦合：AI 蛋白質設計加上便宜的合成，正是這些規則所針對的雙重用途組合，而 Belfer Center 的分析把 AI 賦能的生物技術定位為現行體制僅能部分處理的治理問題。","whyItMatters":"Any institution that orders synthetic DNA, collaborates with US-funded partners, or sends students to US labs is now inside this compliance perimeter whether or not it has noticed. For a programme teaching young students to design sequences, screening literacy is not bureaucracy, it is the condition of being taken seriously as a partner. BIOSECURE-style supply-chain rules also complicate instrument and reagent sourcing decisions in Asia.","whyItMatters_zh":"任何會訂購合成 DNA、與受美國經費支持的夥伴合作，或送學生到美國實驗室的機構，現在都已落在這個法遵範圍內，不論它有沒有注意到。對一個教導年輕學生設計序列的計畫而言，篩查素養不是官僚流程，而是能否被當成嚴肅夥伴看待的前提。BIOSECURE 式的供應鏈規則也讓亞洲的儀器與試劑採購決策更加複雜。","gemsAction":"Write and publish a one-page GEMS sequence-ordering and screening policy that mirrors the NSTM-6 requirements (certified providers, 50-nucleotide screening threshold, identity verification, record retention) and have every student sign it before their first order, which both protects the institution and signals seriousness to partners. Teach a short dual-use and biosecurity module using the Belfer and NSTM-6 documents as primary texts rather than generic ethics material. Audit instrument and reagent suppliers for BIOSECURE Section 851 exposure before any US-funded collaboration.","gemsAction_zh":"撰寫並公開一頁的 GEMS 序列訂購與篩查政策，對應 NSTM-6 的要求（認證供應商、50 個核苷酸的篩查門檻、身分驗證、紀錄保存），並要求每位學生在第一次下單前簽署，這既保護機構，也向夥伴表明認真態度。以 Belfer 與 NSTM-6 的文件作為主要文本，教一個簡短的雙重用途與生物安全單元，而不是用泛泛的倫理教材。在任何受美國經費支持的合作之前，先稽核儀器與試劑供應商在 BIOSECURE 第 851 條下的暴露風險。","maturity":"accelerating","refs":[{"title":"National Policy for Nucleic Acid Synthesis Screening, November 2026 (NSTM-6)","url":"https://www.whitehouse.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/NSTM-6-NASS-Policy.pdf","outlet":"The White House","date":"2026-11-05"},{"title":"Text - S.3741 - 119th Congress: Biosecurity Modernization and Innovation Act of 2026","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/senate-bill/3741/text","outlet":"Congress.gov","date":"2026-01-01"},{"title":"Congress Presses Commerce to Mandate DNA Synthesis Screening as White House Misses Its Own Deadline","url":"https://emerging-tech-lab.com/press/congress-presses-commerce-to-mandate-dna-synthesis-screening-as-white-house-miss","outlet":"Emerging Tech Lab","date":"2026-01-01"},{"title":"The Dual-Use Frontier of AI-Enabled Biotechnology","url":"https://www.belfercenter.org/research-analysis/dual-use-frontier-ai-enabled-biotechnology-civilian-opportunities-national","outlet":"Belfer Center","date":"2026-01-01"},{"title":"Praio Launches Environment Screening Panel at SynBioBeta 2026","url":"https://www.synbiobeta.com/categories/biosecurity-bioethics","outlet":"SynBioBeta","date":"2026-05-12"}]},{"id":"asia-pacific-centre-of-gravity","title":"The centre of gravity in engineered biology is shifting to Asia, and Taiwan is positioned on the manufacturing side rather than the design side","title_zh":"工程生物學的重心正移向亞洲，而台灣的位置在製造端，不在設計端","oneLine":"China holds about 70% of world fermentation capacity and supplied 44.5% of global pharma licensing deal value in H1 2025, while Taiwan's state-linked bio-manufacturing push is a CDMO play with no visible synthetic-biology design layer.","oneLine_zh":"中國掌握全球約 70% 的發酵量能，並在 2025 年上半年提供全球製藥授權交易金額的 44.5%；而台灣由國家主導的生物製造布局是一場 CDMO 的局，看不到合成生物學的設計層。","body":"SynBioBeta's analysis frames China's bioeconomy as three sequential waves now running simultaneously: a completed first wave of amino acids, bulk chemicals and food ingredients built by Meihua, Fufeng, Cathay, Anhui Huaheng Bio and CABIO on cost and operational discipline, which industry sources say displaced Ajinomoto and Kyowa Hakko from significant shares of global amino acid markets (market-share figures explicitly unverified by the author); a second wave built on the 2015 CFDA overhaul, the MAH system and ICH accession in 2017, producing the therapeutics licensing boom in which major pharma in-licensed 31% of their innovative pipeline assets from China in 2024 and China accounted for 44.5% of global licensing deal value in H1 2025; and a third wave now forming. The headline fact underneath all of it is that roughly 70% of world fermentation capacity sits in China. Deal evidence: GSK's 2025 Jiangsu Hengrui agreement at $500M upfront and up to $12B with milestones, AstraZeneca's $2.5B Beijing R&D and manufacturing commitment plus a CSPC research collaboration at $110M upfront with up to $1.62B development and $3.6B sales milestones built on CSPC's AI drug discovery platform, and Cathay Industrial Biotech's reported $500M Wusu expansion in long-chain dicarboxylic acids where China holds about 30% of global production. SynBioBeta separately concluded that 2026 was the year China surpassed the USA in biotech innovation, deal value and clinical output. Taiwan's own posture is manufacturing-led: the state-linked Taiwan Bio-Manufacturing Corporation broke ground on a 15,000 m2 GMP facility in Hsinchu Biomedical Science Park in June 2025 with operations expected from Q2 2026, including Taiwan's first GMP mRNA capability, biomedicine sits inside the 5+2 Innovative Industries Plan, the government acquired National Resilience's advanced pharmaceutical production platform, and a 33-company delegation went to BIO 2026 in San Diego led by the Biotechnology and Pharmaceutical Industries Promotion Office. Regional peers are moving on the dry-lab side instead: DayOne launched Singapore's first biological data centre prototype in August 2026, and Israel's Innovation Authority committed roughly NIS 70 million in July 2026 to national infrastructure for AI models built on biological data. I found no Taiwan-specific synthetic-biology policy programme or funding figure.","body_zh":"SynBioBeta 的分析把中國的生物經濟描述為三波現在同時進行的浪潮：第一波已經完成，由梅花、阜豐、凱賽、安徽華恆生物與嘉必優以成本與營運紀律打下的胺基酸、大宗化學品與食品原料，業界消息指出這一波把味之素與協和發酵從全球胺基酸市場的重要份額中擠出（市占率數字作者明確表示未經查證）；第二波建立在 2015 年 CFDA 的改革、MAH 制度與 2017 年加入 ICH 之上，催生了治療藥物的授權熱潮——2024 年大型藥廠創新管線資產中有 31% 是從中國引進，而 2025 年上半年中國占全球授權交易金額的 44.5%；第三波正在形成。所有這些底下的頭號事實是：全球約 70% 的發酵量能位於中國。交易證據包括：GSK 2025 年與江蘇恆瑞的協議，前期款 5 億美元、含里程碑最高 120 億美元；AstraZeneca 承諾在北京投入 25 億美元研發與生產，另與石藥集團（CSPC）展開研究合作，前期款 1.1 億美元、開發里程碑最高 16.2 億美元、銷售里程碑 36 億美元，建立在 CSPC 的 AI 藥物探索平台上；以及凱賽生物據報在烏蘇擴產 5 億美元，投入長鏈二元酸——中國在此約占全球產能 30%。SynBioBeta 另外得出結論：2026 年是中國在生技創新、交易金額與臨床產出上超越美國的一年。台灣自身的姿態則以製造為主：由國家支持的台灣生物醫藥製造公司（TBMC）於 2025 年 6 月在新竹生醫園區為一座 15,000 平方公尺的 GMP 廠動土，預計 2026 年第二季起營運，其中包含台灣首座 GMP mRNA 產能；生醫被納入五加二創新產業計畫；政府收購了 National Resilience 的先進製藥生產平台；一個 33 家公司的代表團則在生技醫藥產業發展推動小組帶領下赴聖地牙哥參加 BIO 2026。區域同儕反而在乾式這一側布局：DayOne 於 2026 年 8 月啟動新加坡第一個生物資料中心原型，以色列創新署則於 2026 年 7 月投入約 7,000 萬新謝克爾，建設以生物資料為基礎的 AI 模型國家級基礎設施。我沒有找到任何台灣專屬的合成生物學政策計畫或經費數字。","whyItMatters":"Taiwan is building tanks and GMP suites while Singapore and Israel build biological data infrastructure, and the computational layer is where this report argues the value now sits. That gap is GEMS's opening: there is no obvious Taiwanese pipeline producing people who can do dry-lab engineered biology. Proximity to Chinese and Japanese manufacturing capacity is an asset if GEMS trains the design side.","whyItMatters_zh":"台灣在蓋發酵槽與 GMP 廠房，新加坡與以色列在蓋生物資料基礎設施，而本報告主張價值現在就落在運算這一層。那個落差就是 GEMS 的切入口：台灣目前顯然沒有任何管道在培養能做乾式工程生物學的人才。鄰近中國與日本的製造量能，在 GEMS 培養設計端能力的前提下，是一項資產。","gemsAction":"Position GEMS explicitly as Taiwan's dry-lab synthetic biology pipeline rather than a smaller wet lab, and say so to the Biotechnology and Pharmaceutical Industries Promotion Office and the Ministry of Economic Affairs when seeking support, pointing at Singapore's DayOne biological data centre and Israel's NIS 70M biological-AI infrastructure as the comparison Taiwan currently lacks. Open a concrete relationship with TBMC in Hsinchu for student visits and a data project, since it is physically close and its ramp from Q2 2026 means it needs people. Build one regional partnership (Japan, Singapore or Korea) for compute or model access rather than trying to replicate it locally.","gemsAction_zh":"明確把 GEMS 定位為台灣的乾式合成生物學人才管道，而不是一間較小的濕式實驗室；在向生技醫藥產業發展推動小組與經濟部尋求支持時就這樣說，並拿新加坡的 DayOne 生物資料中心與以色列 7,000 萬新謝克爾的生物 AI 基礎設施，作為台灣目前所欠缺的對照。與新竹的 TBMC 建立具體關係，安排學生參訪與一個資料專案，因為它地理上很近，而且從 2026 年第二季開始擴產意味著它需要人。建立一個區域夥伴關係（日本、新加坡或韓國）以取得運算或模型資源，而不是試圖在本地從頭複製。","maturity":"accelerating","refs":[{"title":"China's Bioeconomy Is Brewing Its Biggest Wave Yet","url":"https://www.synbiobeta.com/read/china-s-bioeconomy-is-brewing-its-biggest-wave-yet","outlet":"SynBioBeta","date":"2026-07-09"},{"title":"The Year China Surpassed the USA in Biotech Innovation, Deal Value, and Clinical Output","url":"https://www.synbiobeta.com/insights","outlet":"SynBioBeta","date":"2026-01-22"},{"title":"DayOne Launches Singapore's First Biological Data Center Prototype","url":"https://www.synbiobeta.com/categories/bioeconomy-policy","outlet":"SynBioBeta","date":"2026-08-18"},{"title":"Taiwan seeks to replicate semiconductor success in biotech","url":"https://taiwannews.com.tw/news/6055196","outlet":"Taiwan News","date":"2025-06-01"},{"title":"Taiwan Biotech Delegation Heads to BIO 2026 to Advance Global Partnerships and Innovation","url":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/taiwan-biotech-delegation-heads-to-bio-2026-to-advance-global-partnerships-and-innovation-302805308.html","outlet":"PR Newswire","date":"2026-06-01"},{"title":"The Israel Innovation Authority to Invest Approximately NIS 70 Million in National Infrastructure for AI Models Based on Biological Data","url":"https://www.synbiobeta.com/categories/bioeconomy-policy","outlet":"SynBioBeta","date":"2026-07-16"}]},{"id":"therapeutics-reality-check","title":"Therapeutics is where the capital is, and where the dry lab's claims are finally being tested in patients","title_zh":"治療藥物是資本的所在，也是乾式實驗室的宣稱終於在病人身上受檢驗的地方","oneLine":"Isomorphic Labs raised $5B in November 2026 without disclosing a single human trial, while Insilico's AI-originated drug is in a 320-patient Phase III, which is the whole credibility gap in two sentences.","oneLine_zh":"Isomorphic Labs 在 2026 年 11 月募得 50 億美元，卻未揭露任何一項人體試驗；而 Insilico 源自 AI 的藥物已進入 320 人的三期臨床——兩句話就講完了整個可信度落差。","body":"Isomorphic Labs announced a $5 billion Series C co-led by Greenoaks and Sequoia in mid-November 2026 while disclosing no human trial, no named clinical candidate and no valuation; Demis Hassabis had said at Davos in January 2026 that first trials would begin by the end of 2026, and that remains unconfirmed. A claim that Isomorphic advanced a wholly AI-designed candidate to Phase 2 in June 2026 appears in one secondary source and conflicts with better-sourced reporting, so treat it as unverified. The genuinely advanced programme is Insilico Medicine's rentosertib (ISM001-055), a TNIK inhibitor for idiopathic pulmonary fibrosis, which showed a mean forced vital capacity improvement of +98.4 mL at 12 weeks on 60 mg once daily versus a 20.3 mL decline on placebo in Phase IIa, and whose 320-patient Phase III (NCT07687459) was registered on 7 July 2026. Recursion's clinical story is thinner: REC-4881 in familial adenomatous polyposis is Phase 1b/2, REC-994 and REC-2282 are Phase 2 in cerebral cavernous malformation and NF2-related schwannomatosis, REC-2282's failure removed a near-term catalyst, and the company guides additional clinical data to the first half of 2027. No AI-designed drug has FDA approval. Around that core, 2026 was busy: TwoStep Therapeutics closed an oversubscribed $62.5M Series A with FDA IND clearance for a first-in-class peptide-drug conjugate from a Nobel-laureate spinout, Moonwalk Biosciences raised a $70M Series B for adipose-targeted RNAi in obesity, Aureka raised a $100M Series B, Ridge Biotechnologies expanded its investor base on AI-designed bioconjugates, Owkin partnered with Boehringer Ingelheim and Envisagenics partnered with Boehringer on RNA splicing targets, Weave Bio partnered with Takeda on AI regulatory automation, and Recursion partnered with Genentech on neuroscience targets. Anthropic's life sciences lead Eric Kauderer-Abrams told SynBioBeta 2026 that the company aims to compress life-sciences R&D timelines tenfold, has opened wet labs, acquired the eight-month-old Coefficient Bio, and described Opus 4.6 as its first model with extensive biology training, while conceding that biology often has no single unambiguous source of truth to train against. Xaira's Tessier-Lavigne argued the next step is causal models, built by perturbing cells and organoids and measuring outcomes, with a recent paper spanning 16 cellular contexts, and noted two-thirds of clinical failures come from not identifying the right patients.","body_zh":"Isomorphic Labs 於 2026 年 11 月中宣布由 Greenoaks 與 Sequoia 共同領投的 50 億美元 C 輪，但未揭露任何人體試驗、未指名臨床候選藥物，也未公布估值；Demis Hassabis 曾於 2026 年 1 月在達沃斯表示首次試驗將在 2026 年底前開始，此事仍未獲確認。有一項說法稱 Isomorphic 在 2026 年 6 月把一個完全由 AI 設計的候選藥物推進到二期，但只出現在一個二手來源，且與有較佳出處的報導相衝突，應視為未經查證。真正進展最快的計畫是 Insilico Medicine 的 rentosertib（ISM001-055），一個治療原發性肺纖維化的 TNIK 抑制劑，其二期 a 試驗在每日一次 60 mg 下，12 週時用力肺活量平均改善 +98.4 mL，而安慰劑組下降 20.3 mL；其 320 人的三期試驗（NCT07687459）於 2026 年 7 月 7 日登錄。Recursion 的臨床故事較為單薄：REC-4881 用於家族性腺瘤性大腸息肉症處於 1b/2 期，REC-994 與 REC-2282 分別在腦血管畸形與 NF2 相關神經鞘瘤病處於二期，REC-2282 的失敗移除了一個近期催化劑，公司將額外臨床資料指引到 2027 年上半年。目前沒有任何 AI 設計的藥物取得 FDA 核准。在這個核心周圍，2026 年相當熱絡：TwoStep Therapeutics 完成超額認購的 6,250 萬美元 A 輪，並讓一個出自諾貝爾獎得主衍生公司的同類首見胜肽藥物共軛體取得 FDA 的 IND 許可；Moonwalk Biosciences 募得 7,000 萬美元 B 輪，投入針對脂肪組織的 RNAi 治療肥胖；Aureka 募得 1 億美元 B 輪；Ridge Biotechnologies 以 AI 設計的生物共軛體擴大投資人基礎；Owkin 與 Boehringer Ingelheim 合作，Envisagenics 與 Boehringer 就 RNA 剪接標的合作；Weave Bio 與 Takeda 就 AI 法規自動化合作；Recursion 與 Genentech 就神經科學標的合作。Anthropic 的生命科學負責人 Eric Kauderer-Abrams 在 SynBioBeta 2026 表示，公司目標是把生命科學研發時程壓縮十倍，已經設立濕式實驗室、收購了成立僅八個月的 Coefficient Bio，並形容 Opus 4.6 是其第一個接受大量生物學訓練的模型，同時承認生物學往往沒有一個明確無歧義的真實答案可供訓練。Xaira 的 Tessier-Lavigne 主張下一步是因果模型，透過擾動細胞與類器官並量測結果來建立，近期一篇論文橫跨 16 種細胞情境；他也指出三分之二的臨床失敗來自沒有找出正確的病人族群。","whyItMatters":"This is the clearest available lesson in how to read a claim: a $5B round is not evidence, a 98 mL FVC difference is. Teaching students to distinguish benchmark performance from patient data is the single most transferable critical skill in the field right now. It also shows where the jobs are, because therapeutics absorbed the majority of synbio funding in 2026.","whyItMatters_zh":"這是現有最清楚的一堂「如何讀懂一項宣稱」的課：50 億美元的募資不是證據，98 mL 的 FVC 差異才是。教學生區分基準測試表現與病人資料，是目前這個領域最能遷移的批判能力。它也顯示工作機會在哪裡，因為治療藥物吸收了 2026 年合成生物學大部分的資金。","gemsAction":"Run a recurring journal-club format in which students compare a company's press release against its clinical trial registry entry or SEC filing and write the discrepancy memo, using Isomorphic and Insilico as the opening case. Teach the target-validation question (why this target, in which patients) as seriously as the design question, since that is where Tessier-Lavigne locates two-thirds of failures. Point interested students toward causal-perturbation data analysis, which is the skill Xaira and Arc are both hiring for.","gemsAction_zh":"舉辦一個固定形式的期刊討論會，讓學生把一家公司的新聞稿與其臨床試驗登錄資料或 SEC 申報文件對照，寫出差異備忘錄，開場案例就用 Isomorphic 與 Insilico。把標的驗證的問題（為什麼是這個標的、在哪一群病人身上）教得和設計問題一樣認真，因為 Tessier-Lavigne 把三分之二的失敗歸在那裡。把有興趣的學生引導到因果擾動資料分析，那是 Xaira 與 Arc 都在招募的能力。","maturity":"accelerating","refs":[{"title":"Isomorphic Labs Raises $5 Billion, Discloses No Human Trial: AI Drug Benchmarks Are Not Patient Data","url":"https://www.techtimes.com/articles/330909/20261117/isomorphic-labs-raises-5-billion-discloses-no-human-trial-ai-drug-benchmarks-are-not-patient-data.htm","outlet":"TechTimes","date":"2026-11-17"},{"title":"AI-Discovered Drugs in Clinical Trials 2026: Full Pipeline","url":"https://intuitionlabs.ai/articles/ai-discovered-drugs-clinical-trials-2026","outlet":"IntuitionLabs","date":"2026-01-01"},{"title":"Anthropic Is Hiring Biologists, Building Wet Labs, and Betting Big on Drug Discovery","url":"https://www.synbiobeta.com/read/anthropic-is-hiring-biologists-building-wet-labs-and-betting-big-on-drug-discovery","outlet":"SynBioBeta","date":"2026-05-07"},{"title":"TwoStep Therapeutics Announces Oversubscribed $62.5 Million Series A Financing and FDA Clearance of IND","url":"https://www.synbiobeta.com/read","outlet":"SynBioBeta","date":"2026-09-15"},{"title":"The Drug-Building Tools Got Ahead of the Targets. Envisagenics and Boehringer Want to Close the Gap With RNA Splicing","url":"https://www.synbiobeta.com/read/the-drug-building-tools-got-ahead-of-the-targets.-envisagenics-and-boehringer-want-to-close-the-gap-with-rna-splicing","outlet":"SynBioBeta","date":"2026-11-15"},{"title":"A Letter from Our CEO (Recursion 2025 annual report)","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1601830/000160183026000067/recursion2025ars.pdf","outlet":"SEC EDGAR","date":"2026-01-01"}]},{"id":"funding-climate-concentration","title":"The funding climate is up in dollars and down in companies: capital is concentrating into fewer, larger, dry-lab-flavoured rounds","title_zh":"募資環境是金額上升、公司數下降：資本正集中到更少、更大、帶乾式實驗室色彩的輪次","oneLine":"Synbio funding was up 79.5% to about $1.33B through late September 2026, but the number of funded companies fell from 67 to 62, and excluding rounds over $50M growth was only 34.8%.","oneLine_zh":"到 2026 年 9 月下旬，合成生物學募資成長 79.5% 達約 13.3 億美元，但獲得資金的公司數從 67 家降到 62 家，而排除 5,000 萬美元以上的輪次後，成長只有 34.8%。","body":"One tracker puts synthetic biology funding at $1.327 billion through 22 September 2026, up 79.5% on the comparable 2025 period, and then undercuts the headline: excluding rounds above $50M, 2026 ran only about 34.8% ahead, while funded companies fell from 67 to 62 and deals from 68 to 64. Concentration is extreme within quarters too, with Q2 2026 the largest at $501.5M of which NewLimit's $435M round was 86.7%, against Q1 2026 at $263.7M across 14 deals. Therapeutics took $874.4M, 54.5% of the total, from only eight deals. These are vendor trackers with inconsistent definitions, and a separate tracker counting broader biotech reports 232 VC rounds and $30.9B in 2026, so the absolute numbers should not be quoted without checking PitchBook or Dealroom. The qualitative picture is clearer and consistent across sources: the largest rounds of 2026 went to the computational layer (Isomorphic $5B, Chai $400M, Basecamp $140M, Lila and Periodic at multi-billion valuations, Aureka $100M) while scale-up money came disproportionately from governments (Biosphere $21M from the Department of War, Capra $17M from HHS, Plantible's USDA-backed loan, Formo's EIB loan, Visolis, Bitrobius's £700k ARIA grant, Partillion's $2.1M NIH SBIR, Ride Therapeutics' up to $7.3M from the Cystic Fibrosis Foundation). New dedicated capital is still forming, with Luma Group closing LumaBio Fund I at $410M in September 2026. On the labour market, 2026 job-posting snapshots show protein design roles advertised at roughly $150K-$215K against entry-level computational biology at about $80K-$105K, with Python, PyTorch, deep learning, generative AI and foundation models the most-requested skills, most entry-level postings asking for an MS or PhD in a quantitative or life-science field, and some early-stage employers wanting candidates who can own the entire design-make-test-model loop including wet-lab work. These are job-board samples, not labour statistics. The recurring advisory theme is that AI compresses routine bioinformatics and raises the premium on people who can tell when a model output is wrong, for example by auditing a predicted structure.","body_zh":"某個追蹤機構把截至 2026 年 9 月 22 日的合成生物學募資計為 13.27 億美元，較 2025 年同期成長 79.5%，然後自己拆掉了這個標題數字：排除 5,000 萬美元以上的輪次後，2026 年只領先約 34.8%，而獲得資金的公司數從 67 家降到 62 家，案件數從 68 件降到 64 件。單季之內的集中度也極端：2026 年第二季最大，共 5.015 億美元，其中 NewLimit 的 4.35 億美元一輪就占 86.7%；相對地 2026 年第一季為 14 件、共 2.637 億美元。治療藥物拿到 8.744 億美元，占總額 54.5%，而僅來自八筆交易。這些都是廠商自建的追蹤資料，定義並不一致，而另一個涵蓋更廣泛生技的追蹤機構則回報 2026 年有 232 輪創投與 309 億美元，所以這些絕對數字不應在未對照 PitchBook 或 Dealroom 的情況下引用。定性的圖像較為清楚，且各來源一致：2026 年最大的幾輪都流向運算層（Isomorphic 50 億美元、Chai 4 億美元、Basecamp 1.4 億美元、Lila 與 Periodic 的數十億美元估值、Aureka 1 億美元），而放大生產的資金則不成比例地來自政府（Biosphere 自 Department of War 取得 2,100 萬美元、Capra 自 HHS 取得 1,700 萬美元、Plantible 的 USDA 擔保貸款、Formo 的 EIB 貸款、Visolis、Bitrobius 的 70 萬英鎊 ARIA 補助、Partillion 的 210 萬美元 NIH SBIR、Ride Therapeutics 自 Cystic Fibrosis Foundation 取得最高 730 萬美元）。新的專門資金仍在形成，Luma Group 於 2026 年 9 月以 4.1 億美元完成 LumaBio Fund I 的募集。在勞動市場方面，2026 年的職缺快照顯示蛋白質設計職位的開價約在 15 萬至 21.5 萬美元，而入門級計算生物學約為 8 萬至 10.5 萬美元；最常被要求的技能是 Python、PyTorch、深度學習、生成式 AI 與基礎模型，多數入門職缺要求量化或生命科學領域的碩士或博士學位，而部分早期階段的雇主希望候選人能獨立負責整個設計—製作—測試—建模迴路，包含濕式實驗工作。這些是職缺平台的樣本，不是勞動統計。反覆出現的建議主題是：AI 壓縮了例行的生物資訊工作，並提高了「能判斷模型輸出何時是錯的」這種人的身價，例如能審查一個預測結構。","whyItMatters":"An entry-level synbio career in 2026 is a hybrid role: the premium is on someone who can run a model and then design the experiment that proves it wrong. Pure wet-lab technician work is being compressed, and pure modelling without wet-lab judgement is abundant. For a high-school and early-undergraduate programme, this is unusually good news, because the hybrid skill set can be started early and does not require a PhD to begin.","whyItMatters_zh":"2026 年入門級的合成生物學職涯是一個混合型角色：加價的對象是能跑模型、然後設計出能推翻它的實驗的人。純濕式實驗技術員的工作正被壓縮，而沒有濕式判斷力的純建模則供過於求。對一個高中與大學低年級的計畫而言，這是出乎意料的好消息，因為這套混合能力可以很早開始培養，而且不需要博士學位才能起步。","gemsAction":"Make Python, PyTorch and version-controlled, reproducible analysis non-negotiable core curriculum alongside bench skills, and require every student to produce a public portfolio artefact (a GitHub repository with code, data and a validated result) because that is what the 2026 postings screen for. Set the explicit training target as the design-make-test-model loop owner rather than either a modeller or a bench scientist. Track protein-design and computational-biology job boards quarterly and feed the actual requested skills back into the syllabus rather than guessing.","gemsAction_zh":"把 Python、PyTorch，以及有版本控制、可重現的分析，與實驗檯技能並列為不可妥協的核心課程，並要求每位學生產出一件公開的作品（一個含程式碼、資料與已驗證結果的 GitHub 儲存庫），因為那正是 2026 年職缺在篩選的東西。把訓練目標明確設為「設計—製作—測試—建模迴路的負責人」，而不是單純的建模者或實驗檯科學家。每季追蹤蛋白質設計與計算生物學的職缺平台，把實際被要求的技能回饋到課程大綱，而不是憑猜測。","maturity":"accelerating","refs":[{"title":"Synthetic biology: what's funding like now?","url":"https://newmarketpitch.com/blogs/news/synthetic-biology-funding-analysis","outlet":"NewMarketPitch","date":"2026-09-22"},{"title":"Biotech Funding Tracker 2026: 232 VC Rounds, $30.9B Raised","url":"https://www.biobucks.co/biotech-vc-funding-tracker-2026","outlet":"BioBucks","date":"2026-01-01"},{"title":"Luma Group Successfully Closes LumaBio Fund I at $410 Million","url":"https://www.synbiobeta.com/read/luma-group-successfully-closes-lumabio-fund-i-at-410-million","outlet":"SynBioBeta","date":"2026-09-15"},{"title":"AI Skills for Protein Design & Structure Jobs 2026","url":"https://www.compbiojobs.com/guides/ai-ml-skills/protein-design","outlet":"CompBioJobs","date":"2026-01-01"},{"title":"Entry Level Bioinformatics Jobs: 60+ Roles, $80K-$105K","url":"https://www.compbiojobs.com/jobs/entry-level","outlet":"CompBioJobs","date":"2026-01-01"},{"title":"Transitioning to Bioinformatics in 2026: Is AI a Threat or a Turbocharger?","url":"https://hire-omics.com/articles/transitioning-to-bioinformatics-in-2026-is-ai-a-threat-or-a-turbocharger","outlet":"Hire-Omics","date":"2026-01-01"}]},{"id":"light-as-control-layer","title":"Light is becoming the control and cleaning layer of bioprocessing, which makes optogenetics an industrial skill","title_zh":"光正在成為生物製程的控制層與清潔層，這讓光遺傳學變成一項工業技能","oneLine":"Optogenetics stopped being a neuroscience technique and became a way to retrofit existing steel fermenters and sterilise tanks without steam, which is the cheapest route past the CapEx wall.","oneLine_zh":"光遺傳學不再只是神經科學技術，而成了改裝現有鋼製發酵槽、以及不用蒸氣就能滅菌的方法，這是繞過資本支出高牆最便宜的路。","body":"Three independent 2026 plays point the same direction. Biosphere's $21M Department of War award is explicitly for UV sterilisation in place of steam in a 20,000-litre tank, on the argument that removing the pressure-cooker requirement removes most of the auxiliary process piping and vessel cost, with the next engineering problems being heat removal and oxygen transfer because, as CEO Brian Heligman puts it, a reactor is like an engine that burns sugar. Fermeate closed a $2M seed led by Newfund Capital in April 2026 to use light to control gene expression during fermentation, with the pitch that it can convert existing stainless-steel fermenters at a fraction of the cost of installing a new bioreactor, which directly attacks the capacity bottleneck rather than adding capacity. Prolific Machines, which uses light to control cell function across cell types, raised a $55M Series B1 led by the Ki Tua Fund and a 2026 tracker lists an initial closing of a US$50M Series B2 (the two may be separate rounds; the sources are inconsistent). Adjacent sensing is also attracting small, specific money: Scentian Bio raised a $4.1M seed in April 2026 on insect odorant-receptor biosensors, Xsensio closed an oversubscribed $7M Series A for clinical biosensing deployment, Praio launched an environment screening panel built on artificial protocell technology at SynBioBeta 2026, and Neion Bio raised an $11M seed using engineered chicken eggs as bioreactors with Barnwell Bio biosurveillance layered on top. SynBioBeta ran a dedicated analysis of the bioelectric tech stack in February 2026. The common thread is that optical and electrical control are cheaper to add to existing hardware than new hardware is to build, and that genetically encoded light-responsive circuits are the enabling biology.","body_zh":"2026 年有三個彼此獨立的布局指向同一個方向。Biosphere 自 Department of War 取得的 2,100 萬美元，明確用於在一座 20,000 公升槽體中以紫外光取代蒸氣滅菌，其論點是去掉高壓滅菌的需求，就去掉了大部分輔助製程管路與槽體成本；下一個工程難題是散熱與氧氣傳遞，因為正如執行長 Brian Heligman 所說，反應器就像一具燒糖的引擎。Fermeate 於 2026 年 4 月完成由 Newfund Capital 領投的 200 萬美元種子輪，以光控制發酵過程中的基因表現，其訴求是能以安裝新生物反應器的一小部分成本改裝現有的不鏽鋼發酵槽，這直接攻擊量能瓶頸，而不是增加量能。Prolific Machines 以光控制跨細胞類型的細胞功能，募得由 Ki Tua Fund 領投的 5,500 萬美元 B1 輪，而 2026 年某個追蹤機構列出一筆 5,000 萬美元 B2 輪的首次交割（兩者可能是不同輪次；來源彼此不一致）。相鄰的感測領域也吸引到小額而明確的資金：Scentian Bio 於 2026 年 4 月以昆蟲嗅覺受體生物感測器募得 410 萬美元種子輪；Xsensio 完成超額認購的 700 萬美元 A 輪，投入臨床生物感測的部署；Praio 在 SynBioBeta 2026 推出以人工原始細胞技術建構的環境篩查套組；Neion Bio 募得 1,100 萬美元種子輪，以工程化雞蛋作為生物反應器，並在其上疊加 Barnwell Bio 的生物監測。SynBioBeta 於 2026 年 2 月做了一次生物電技術堆疊的專題分析。共同的線索是：在既有硬體上加裝光學與電學控制，比蓋新硬體便宜，而基因編碼的光反應電路就是那個使能的生物學。","whyItMatters":"Optogenetic and biosensor circuit design is unusually well suited to a teaching institution: the parts are small, the readouts are visual, the equipment is cheap compared with fermentation, and the industrial relevance is now documented rather than speculative. It is also one of the few areas where a student-scale build can produce a genuinely novel result. This is a credible wedge for a programme that cannot afford pilot-scale fermentation.","whyItMatters_zh":"光遺傳學與生物感測器電路設計特別適合教學型機構：元件小、讀出是視覺的、設備相對發酵便宜，而工業相關性現在有文件支持而非臆測。它也是少數幾個學生規模的建構就能產出真正新結果的領域之一。對一個負擔不起試量產級發酵的計畫來說，這是一個可信的切入楔子。","gemsAction":"Build a light-controlled gene expression and biosensor teaching module around cheap LED hardware, a plate reader and standard inducible-circuit parts, and have students characterise dose-response and dynamic range properly, which is real engineering data rather than a demonstration. Pair it with a Python analysis pipeline so the same project trains both halves of the dry-wet loop. Read SynBioBeta's bioelectric tech stack piece and approach Fermeate or a Taiwanese fermentation producer about a light-retrofit student study.","gemsAction_zh":"以便宜的 LED 硬體、一台盤式讀取儀與標準的可誘導電路元件，建立一個光控基因表現與生物感測器的教學模組，並讓學生好好地測出劑量反應與動態範圍，那是真正的工程資料，而不是一場示範。搭配一條 Python 分析流程，讓同一個專案同時訓練乾濕迴路的兩半。讀 SynBioBeta 的生物電技術堆疊專文，並接洽 Fermeate 或一家台灣的發酵業者，討論一項光改裝的學生研究。","maturity":"emerging","refs":[{"title":"Fermeate raises $2m to deliver step change in precision fermentation economics with optogenetics","url":"https://agfundernews.com/fermeate-raises-2m-to-deliver-step-change-in-precision-fermentation-economics-with-optogenetics","outlet":"AgFunderNews","date":"2026-04-01"},{"title":"Optogenetics startup Prolific Machines raises $55m series B1, uses light to control virtually any cell function in any cell type","url":"https://agfundernews.com/optogenetics-startup-prolific-machines-raises-55m-series-b1-uses-light-to-control-virtually-any-cell-function-in-any-cell-type","outlet":"AgFunderNews","date":"2026-01-01"},{"title":"Biosphere Lands $21M From the Department of War to Build a Bioreactor Cleaned With Light","url":"https://www.synbiobeta.com/read/biosphere-lands-21m-from-the-department-of-war-to-build-a-bioreactor-cleaned-with-light","outlet":"SynBioBeta","date":"2026-11-13"},{"title":"The Bioelectric Tech Stack","url":"https://www.synbiobeta.com/insights","outlet":"SynBioBeta","date":"2026-02-06"},{"title":"Oversubscribed $7M Series A to boost Xsensio biosensing clinical deployment","url":"https://www.startupticker.ch/en/news/oversubscribed-7m-series-a-to-boost-clinical-deployment-of-xsensio-biosensing","outlet":"Startupticker","date":"2026-01-01"}]}],"companiesToWatch":[{"name":"Latent Labs","what":"Latent-X2 frontier model for antibody and peptide design, plus Latent-Y, marketed as the first lab-validated drug design agent, delivered through a web interface.","what_zh":"Latent-X2 為抗體與胜肽設計的前沿模型，另有 Latent-Y，宣稱是第一個經實驗室驗證的藥物設計代理，透過網頁介面提供。","why":"The clearest example of design capability being packaged for people with no machine-learning background, which is exactly GEMS's student profile. Its UC Davis ion-channel nanobody collaboration shows the academic entry path.","why_zh":"最清楚的例子，說明設計能力如何被包裝給沒有機器學習背景的人使用，而那正是 GEMS 的學生樣貌。它與 UC Davis 的離子通道奈米抗體合作展示了學術界的切入路徑。","url":"https://www.synbiobeta.com/read/latent-y-automates-antibody-design-work-that-slows-down-early-drug-development"},{"name":"Arc Institute","what":"Non-profit research institute behind Evo 2 (9.3T base pairs, 128k+ genomes, Nature March 2026, fully open weights and data) and the State virtual cell model, plus the annual Virtual Cell Challenge.","what_zh":"非營利研究機構，Evo 2（9.3 兆鹼基對、12.8 萬個以上基因組，2026 年 3 月 Nature，權重與資料完全開放）與 State 虛擬細胞模型的開發者，並主辦年度 Virtual Cell Challenge。","why":"The best free on-ramp to biological foundation models, and the Virtual Cell Challenge is a competition GEMS students could realistically enter, giving the programme an external benchmark.","why_zh":"通往生物基礎模型最好的免費入門，而 Virtual Cell Challenge 是 GEMS 學生實際有可能參加的競賽，能為整個計畫提供一個外部基準。","url":"https://arcinstitute.org/tools"},{"name":"Twist Bioscience","what":"Synthetic DNA and protein reagents; FY2026 revenue $459.4M up 22%, FY2027 guidance $550-560M, positive adjusted EBITDA in Q4 FY2026, targeting $100M of AI-related orders in FY2027.","what_zh":"合成 DNA 與蛋白質試劑；2026 財年營收 4.594 億美元、成長 22%，2027 財年指引 5.5 億至 5.6 億美元，2026 財年第四季調整後 EBITDA 轉正，目標 2027 財年 AI 相關訂單 1 億美元。","why":"The proof that picks-and-shovels beats platform narratives, the likely supplier for GEMS constructs, and a live indicator of how fast AI-driven design is actually pulling through to physical orders.","why_zh":"證明賣鋤頭鏟子勝過平台敘事，很可能是 GEMS 構築體的供應商，也是一個即時指標，顯示 AI 驅動的設計實際上以多快的速度轉化為實體訂單。","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001581280/000158128026000053/twst-2026930xex991.htm"},{"name":"Ansa Biotechnologies","what":"Enzymatic DNA synthesis service selling clonal constructs from 100 bp to 50 kb from about $0.13 per base pair with an on-time delivery guarantee, now co-selling through IDT's e-commerce platform.","what_zh":"酵素 DNA 合成服務，銷售 100 bp 到 50 kb 的單株構築體，每鹼基對約 0.13 美元起，附準時交付保證，現已透過 IDT 的電子商務平台共同銷售。","why":"Long clonal DNA with a delivery guarantee is what makes ambitious student build projects feasible on a term timetable. Service-only model means no capital equipment required.","why_zh":"附交期保證的長鏈單株 DNA，是讓有野心的學生建構專案能在一個學期時程內做完的關鍵。純服務模式意味著不需要任何資本設備。","url":"https://ansabio.com/news-events/news/ansa-biotechnologies-targets-nucleic-acid-synthesis-market-with-ultra-long-clonal-dna-service/"},{"name":"Ginkgo Bioworks","what":"Pivoting from service platform to autonomous labs, Datapoints training data and Solutions; building AMP2 and the 97-robot $47M M2PC autonomous labs at PNNL under the Genesis Mission; Q2 2026 revenue $20.2M versus $39.1M a year earlier.","what_zh":"正從服務平台轉向自主實驗室、Datapoints 訓練資料與 Solutions；在 Genesis Mission 之下於 PNNL 建造 AMP2 與擁有 97 台機器人、4,700 萬美元的 M2PC 自主實驗室；2026 年第二季營收 2,020 萬美元，去年同期為 3,910 萬美元。","why":"Both the cautionary tale about platform economics and the operator of the autonomous-lab infrastructure GEMS may eventually apply to use, since both PNNL facilities run as open user facilities.","why_zh":"既是平台經濟學的警世故事，也是 GEMS 未來可能申請使用的自主實驗室基礎設施的營運者，因為 PNNL 的兩座設施都以開放的使用者設施形式運作。","url":"https://www.synbiobeta.com/read/ginkgo-joins-genesis-project-to-build-a-47-million-autonomous-robot-lab"},{"name":"Potato","what":"Optimizer, an early-access tool turning an assay spec and a statement of available lab hardware into a multivariable design of experiments, protocol, plate maps and Opentrons worklists, with deterministic rather than generated calculations.","what_zh":"Optimizer 是一個早期取用的工具，能把一份檢測規格與一份可用實驗室硬體清單，轉換成多變數實驗設計、實驗流程、盤面配置圖與 Opentrons 工作清單，計算採用確定性方式而非生成式。","why":"The single most adoptable dry-lab tool for a teaching lab in the next 12 months: it raises experimental design quality without new instruments and outputs to Opentrons, the open automation default.","why_zh":"未來 12 個月內，對教學型實驗室而言最容易採用的乾式工具：它在不添購儀器的前提下提升實驗設計品質，而且輸出對接 Opentrons——開放自動化的預設選擇。","url":"https://www.synbiobeta.com/read/potato-just-launched-the-tool-it-wishes-it-had-as-a-lab-scientist"},{"name":"Outpost Bio","what":"Open-sourced a microbiome foundation model trained on soil, ocean and wastewater samples, together with its training data and a public benchmark, showing cross-domain transfer into human gut prediction.","what_zh":"開源了一個以土壤、海洋與廢水樣本訓練的微生物體基礎模型，連同其訓練資料與一項公開基準，並展示跨領域遷移到人類腸道的預測能力。","why":"A replicable template for how a smaller institution creates a defensible asset: own a dataset, publish a benchmark, release the model. Directly applicable to Taiwanese environmental and agricultural microbiomes.","why_zh":"一個可複製的範本，說明較小的機構如何建立具防禦性的資產：擁有一份資料集、發表一項基準、釋出模型。可直接套用在台灣的環境與農業微生物體上。","url":"https://www.synbiobeta.com/read/one-model-every-microbiome"},{"name":"BiomEdit","what":"BE-101, a chromosomally engineered Limosilactobacillus reuteri secreting anti-toxin single-domain antibodies in the chicken gut; USDA conditional licence 29 September 2026, now in 35+ million broilers.","what_zh":"BE-101，一株以染色體方式工程化的 Limosilactobacillus reuteri，可在雞腸道中分泌抗毒素單域抗體；2026 年 9 月 29 日取得 USDA 有條件許可，目前已用於 3,500 萬隻以上肉雞。","why":"The first engineered live therapeutic microbe through a regulatory door, and a case study in choosing the right agency early. The nearest real-world analogue for Taiwan-relevant livestock and aquaculture projects.","why_zh":"第一個通過法規大門的工程化活體治療微生物，也是「及早選對主管機關」的案例研究。對與台灣相關的畜產與水產養殖專案而言，這是最接近的真實世界類比。","url":"https://www.synbiobeta.com/read/usda-greenlights-the-first-engineered-microbe-that-makes-antibodies-in-the-gut"},{"name":"Basecamp Research","what":"$140M Series C on 23 September 2026 led by S32 with NVIDIA and Menlo Ventures participating; EDEN protein models trained on proprietary biodiversity-derived BaseData, moving into its own therapeutics pipeline.","what_zh":"2026 年 9 月 23 日的 1.4 億美元 C 輪，由 S32 領投，NVIDIA 與 Menlo Ventures 參與；EDEN 蛋白質模型以其專有、源自生物多樣性的 BaseData 訓練，並正切入自有的治療藥物管線。","why":"The clearest statement that the moat is proprietary biological data rather than model architecture, which is the strategic argument for GEMS collecting something locally unique.","why_zh":"最清楚的一項宣告：護城河是專有的生物資料，而不是模型架構——這也是 GEMS 應該去採集某種在地獨有資料的策略論據。","url":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/basecamp-research-raises-140m-to-advance-ai-designed-therapeutics-302887617.html"},{"name":"Biosphere","what":"$21M from the US Department of War via the Defense Industrial Base Consortium for a 20,000-litre UV-sterilised bioreactor targeting roughly 100 tons/year, operational in the Bay Area by late 2027.","what_zh":"自美國 Department of War 透過 Defense Industrial Base Consortium 取得 2,100 萬美元，建造一座以紫外光滅菌的 20,000 公升生物反應器，目標年產約 100 公噸，2027 年底前在灣區投入運轉。","why":"The sharpest illustration of the cost-of-goods wall and of governments funding manufacturing redesign. Its UV approach, plus Fermeate's light-retrofit model, makes optical control a credible teaching focus.","why_zh":"最尖銳地說明了生產成本這道牆，以及政府正在出錢重新設計製造方式。它的紫外光路線加上 Fermeate 的光改裝模式，讓光學控制成為一個可信的教學重點。","url":"https://www.synbiobeta.com/read/biosphere-lands-21m-from-the-department-of-war-to-build-a-bioreactor-cleaned-with-light"},{"name":"Insilico Medicine","what":"Rentosertib (ISM001-055), an AI-originated TNIK inhibitor for idiopathic pulmonary fibrosis; Phase IIa showed +98.4 mL mean FVC at 12 weeks versus a 20.3 mL placebo decline, with a 320-patient Phase III (NCT07687459) registered 7 July 2026.","what_zh":"Rentosertib（ISM001-055），一個源自 AI 的 TNIK 抑制劑，用於原發性肺纖維化；二期 a 顯示 12 週時 FVC 平均 +98.4 mL，安慰劑組則下降 20.3 mL，320 人的三期試驗（NCT07687459）於 2026 年 7 月 7 日登錄。","why":"The most clinically advanced test of whether AI-originated drug design works in patients, and the right benchmark against which to judge every other AI drug discovery claim.","why_zh":"目前臨床進展最快、檢驗「源自 AI 的藥物設計在病人身上是否有效」的案例，也是評斷其他所有 AI 藥物探索宣稱時最適當的標竿。","url":"https://intuitionlabs.ai/articles/ai-discovered-drugs-clinical-trials-2026"},{"name":"Taiwan Bio-Manufacturing Corporation (TBMC)","what":"State-linked CDMO with a 15,000 m2 GMP facility in Hsinchu Biomedical Science Park, including Taiwan's first GMP mRNA capability, with operations expected from Q2 2026.","what_zh":"由國家支持的 CDMO，在新竹生醫園區擁有一座 15,000 平方公尺的 GMP 廠，含台灣首座 GMP mRNA 產能，預計 2026 年第二季起營運。","why":"The nearest significant engineered-biology manufacturing asset to GEMS, ramping now and therefore hiring and needing skills. The obvious first domestic partner for site visits, data projects and student placements.","why_zh":"距離 GEMS 最近的重要工程生物學製造資產，正在擴產，因此也正在招人、需要技能。是場勘、資料專案與學生實習最明顯的首選國內夥伴。","url":"https://taiwannews.com.tw/news/6055196"}],"readingList":[{"title":"China's Bioeconomy Is Brewing Its Biggest Wave Yet","url":"https://www.synbiobeta.com/read/china-s-bioeconomy-is-brewing-its-biggest-wave-yet","outlet":"SynBioBeta","why":"The single best piece on why 70% of world fermentation capacity being in China reshapes every strategic choice an Asian institution makes.","why_zh":"最好的一篇文章，說明全球 70% 發酵量能位於中國，如何重塑一所亞洲機構的每一個策略選擇。"},{"title":"The protein design boom is moving beyond pharma. Quercus raised $5M with the conviction that weeds are next","url":"https://www.synbiobeta.com/read/the-protein-design-boom-is-moving-beyond-pharma.-quercus-raised-5m-with-the-conviction-that-weeds-are-next","outlet":"SynBioBeta","why":"Explains undruggability and design-space blind spots better than most textbooks, and shows the pharma toolkit migrating into agriculture.","why_zh":"把「不可成藥性」與設計空間的盲點解釋得比多數教科書更清楚，也展示製藥工具組如何移植到農業。"},{"title":"USDA Greenlights the First Engineered Microbe That Makes Antibodies in the Gut","url":"https://www.synbiobeta.com/read/usda-greenlights-the-first-engineered-microbe-that-makes-antibodies-in-the-gut","outlet":"SynBioBeta","why":"A complete worked example of chassis choice, genetic stability, delivery design and regulatory strategy in one product.","why_zh":"一個完整的實例演練，在同一個產品中涵蓋底盤選擇、遺傳穩定性、投遞設計與法規策略。"},{"title":"Biosphere Lands $21M From the Department of War to Build a Bioreactor Cleaned With Light","url":"https://www.synbiobeta.com/read/biosphere-lands-21m-from-the-department-of-war-to-build-a-bioreactor-cleaned-with-light","outlet":"SynBioBeta","why":"The clearest explanation available of why bioprocess CapEx, not biology, is what kills industrial synbio companies.","why_zh":"現有最清楚的解釋，說明殺死工業合成生物學公司的是生物製程的資本支出，而不是生物學。"},{"title":"One Model, Every Microbiome","url":"https://www.synbiobeta.com/read/one-model-every-microbiome","outlet":"SynBioBeta","why":"Teaches what a foundation model actually buys you (learning structure before you ask the question) using a concrete 200-patient overfitting problem.","why_zh":"用一個具體的 200 位病人過度配適問題，說明基礎模型究竟替你買到了什麼（在你提出問題之前就先學會結構）。"},{"title":"Potato Just Launched the Tool It Wishes It Had as a Lab Scientist","url":"https://www.synbiobeta.com/read/potato-just-launched-the-tool-it-wishes-it-had-as-a-lab-scientist","outlet":"SynBioBeta","why":"The best short argument for why design of experiments and automation literacy, not more pipetting, is the skill gap in 2026.","why_zh":"最好的簡短論證，說明 2026 年的技能缺口是實驗設計與自動化素養，而不是更多的移液操作。"},{"title":"National Policy for Nucleic Acid Synthesis Screening (NSTM-6)","url":"https://www.whitehouse.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/NSTM-6-NASS-Policy.pdf","outlet":"The White House","why":"The primary document that now governs who may sell synthetic DNA to anyone touching US federal funding; read it before setting GEMS ordering policy.","why_zh":"如今規範「誰可以把合成 DNA 賣給任何沾到美國聯邦經費的人」的主要文件；在訂定 GEMS 的訂購政策之前先讀它。"},{"title":"The 2026 Virtual Cell Challenge","url":"https://arcinstitute.org/news/virtual-cell-challenge-2026","outlet":"Arc Institute","why":"A live, well-specified prediction task with real data that GEMS students could attempt, and a map of what the field considers an unsolved problem.","why_zh":"一個進行中、規格明確、有真實資料的預測任務，GEMS 學生有可能嘗試，同時也是一張地圖，標出這個領域認定還沒解決的問題。"},{"title":"Anthropic Is Hiring Biologists, Building Wet Labs, and Betting Big on Drug Discovery","url":"https://www.synbiobeta.com/read/anthropic-is-hiring-biologists-building-wet-labs-and-betting-big-on-drug-discovery","outlet":"SynBioBeta","why":"Honest account from both an AI lab and a drug-discovery CEO of what AI can and cannot do in biology, including why biology resists clean training signals.","why_zh":"來自一間 AI 公司與一位藥物探索執行長的誠實說法，談 AI 在生物學中能做到與做不到什麼，包括生物學為何難以提供乾淨的訓練訊號。"},{"title":"Twist Bioscience FY2026 fourth quarter and full year results (Form 8-K)","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001581280/000158128026000053/twst-2026930xex991.htm","outlet":"SEC EDGAR","why":"A primary filing showing what real revenue in engineered biology looks like, including the explicit AI-order ramp from $25M to a $100M target.","why_zh":"一份原始申報文件，顯示工程生物學中真實的營收長什麼樣子，包括 AI 訂單從 2,500 萬美元明確攀升到 1 億美元目標。"},{"title":"Ginkgo Bioworks Form 10-Q, Q2 2026","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001830214/000162828026054298/dna-20260630.htm","outlet":"SEC EDGAR","why":"Read against the Twist filing, it is the cheapest available lesson in distinguishing a platform narrative from a business.","why_zh":"與 Twist 的申報文件對讀，它是最便宜的一堂課，教你如何區分平台敘事與一樁生意。"},{"title":"AI Skills for Protein Design & Structure Jobs 2026","url":"https://www.compbiojobs.com/guides/ai-ml-skills/protein-design","outlet":"CompBioJobs","why":"A posting-level snapshot of the exact skills employers name, useful for syllabus design even though it is a job board's own sample.","why_zh":"職缺層級的快照，列出雇主實際指名的技能，即使它只是某個職缺平台自己的樣本，對課程設計仍然有用。"}],"careerPaths":["Protein design engineer: runs generative design (ESM/RFdiffusion-class models, or hosted platforms like Latent Labs and Cradle) against a chosen target and owns the wet-lab validation that proves or kills the design; postings in 2026 cluster around Python, PyTorch, deep learning and de novo design, at roughly $150K-$215K in the US market.","Biological foundation model specialist: fine-tunes, probes and benchmarks models such as Evo 2 or ESM via NVIDIA BioNeMo, builds evaluation sets, and can say precisely where a model generalises and where it fails, which is the skill the Arc Virtual Cell Challenge is designed to surface.","Lab automation and protocol-as-code engineer: translates scientific questions into designs of experiments, plate maps and Opentrons or RAC-executable worklists, the translation bottleneck Potato's Optimizer targets and the capability that autonomous user facilities like PNNL's AMP2 and M2PC require of their users.","Bioprocess data and techno-economic analyst: links strain performance (titre, rate, yield) to mass and energy balances, equipment sizing, CapEx and OpEx, the Cemvita-Roebling role; the scarcest skill in the sector because it sits between biology, engineering and finance.","Biological data curator and benchmark builder: assembles, labels, licenses and publishes proprietary datasets with benchmark tasks attached, the business Basecamp Research, Ginkgo Datapoints and Tempus are all in, and the role where a Taiwan-specific dataset becomes a career asset.","Biosecurity and regulatory affairs specialist for engineered biology: implements nucleic-acid synthesis screening under NSTM-6, assesses BIOSECURE Section 851 supply-chain exposure, and does what BiomEdit did in choosing and co-creating a regulatory path before development, a growing and under-supplied function.","Agricultural and food synbio applications scientist: takes designed proteins or engineered microbes into field, feed or aquaculture settings, owns the economics (cost per acre, per tonne, per bird) and the local regulatory route; the Robigo, Quercus, Pivot Bio and BiomEdit track, and the one best matched to Taiwan's existing industries."],"careerPaths_zh":["蛋白質設計工程師：針對選定的標的執行生成式設計（ESM/RFdiffusion 這一類模型，或 Latent Labs、Cradle 等託管平台），並負責證明或推翻該設計的濕式實驗驗證；2026 年的職缺集中在 Python、PyTorch、深度學習與從頭設計，美國市場開價約 15 萬至 21.5 萬美元。","生物基礎模型專家：透過 NVIDIA BioNeMo 微調、探測並評測 Evo 2 或 ESM 這類模型，建立評估資料集，並能精確說出模型在哪裡能泛化、在哪裡失效——這正是 Arc 的 Virtual Cell Challenge 設計要篩出的能力。","實驗室自動化與流程即程式碼工程師：把科學問題翻譯成實驗設計、盤面配置圖，以及 Opentrons 或 RAC 可執行的工作清單；這個翻譯瓶頸是 Potato 的 Optimizer 所針對的，也是 PNNL 的 AMP2 與 M2PC 等自主使用者設施對使用者所要求的能力。","生物製程資料與技術經濟分析師：把菌株表現（產量、速率、產率）連結到質能平衡、設備選型、資本支出與營運支出，也就是 Cemvita-Roebling 那個角色；這是整個產業最稀缺的能力，因為它坐落在生物學、工程與財務之間。","生物資料策劃與基準建置者：彙整、標註、授權並發表附有基準任務的專有資料集，這正是 Basecamp Research、Ginkgo Datapoints 與 Tempus 都在做的生意，也是一份台灣專屬資料集能變成職涯資產的角色。","工程生物學的生物安全與法規事務專家：依 NSTM-6 落實核酸合成篩查、評估 BIOSECURE 第 851 條的供應鏈暴露風險，並做 BiomEdit 所做的事——在開發之前就選定並共同打造法規路徑；這是一個正在成長而供給不足的職能。","農業與食品合成生物學應用科學家：把設計好的蛋白質或工程化微生物帶進田間、飼料或水產養殖場景，負責經濟性（每英畝、每公噸、每隻的成本）與在地的法規路徑；這是 Robigo、Quercus、Pivot Bio 與 BiomEdit 的路線，也是最契合台灣既有產業的一條。"]}};
